(15, 'Malisia', '<p data-start=\"224\" data-end=\"567\"><strong data-start=\"224\" data-end=\"236\">Malaysia</strong> is a vibrant and diverse country located in Southeast Asia, divided into two main regions: <strong data-start=\"328\" data-end=\"351\">Peninsular Malaysia</strong> and <strong data-start=\"356\" data-end=\"392\">Malaysian Borneo (East Malaysia)</strong>. It is known for its rich cultural heritage, blending <strong data-start=\"447\" data-end=\"500\">Malay, Chinese, Indian, and Indigenous traditions</strong>, which is reflected in its festivals, architecture, and cuisine.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"569\" data-end=\"974\">The capital city, <strong data-start=\"587\" data-end=\"603\">Kuala Lumpur</strong>, is a modern metropolis famous for the <strong data-start=\"643\" data-end=\"667\">Petronas Twin Towers</strong>, bustling markets, and a dynamic mix of old and new. Other iconic destinations include <strong data-start=\"755\" data-end=\"765\">Penang</strong> (a UNESCO World Heritage Site with colonial charm and street food culture), the lush <strong data-start=\"851\" data-end=\"872\">Cameron Highlands</strong>, and the natural wonders of <strong data-start=\"901\" data-end=\"922\">Sabah and Sarawak</strong> with rainforests, orangutans, and Mount Kinabalu.</p>', 'en', 3),
