(22, 'Brazil', '<p data-start=\"55\" data-end=\"448\"><strong data-start=\"55\" data-end=\"65\">Brazil</strong> is the largest country in <strong data-start=\"92\" data-end=\"109\">South America</strong> and the <strong data-start=\"118\" data-end=\"148\">fifth-largest in the world</strong>, both by area and population. It is famous for its <strong data-start=\"200\" data-end=\"261\">cultural vibrancy, natural beauty, and diverse landscapes</strong>. The capital is <strong data-start=\"278\" data-end=\"290\">Bras&iacute;lia</strong>, while <strong data-start=\"298\" data-end=\"311\">S&atilde;o Paulo</strong> is its largest city and <strong data-start=\"336\" data-end=\"354\">Rio de Janeiro</strong> is world-renowned for its beaches, Carnival, and the iconic <strong data-start=\"415\" data-end=\"438\" data-is-only-node=\"\">Christ the Redeemer</strong> statue.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"450\" data-end=\"737\">Brazil&rsquo;s geography is incredibly varied&mdash;featuring the <strong data-start=\"504\" data-end=\"525\">Amazon Rainforest</strong> (the planet&rsquo;s largest tropical rainforest and home to unparalleled biodiversity), the <strong data-start=\"612\" data-end=\"633\">Pantanal wetlands</strong> (a wildlife paradise), vast highlands, and beautiful coastlines stretching over <strong data-start=\"714\" data-end=\"734\">7,000 kilometers</strong>.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"739\" data-end=\"1013\">Culturally, Brazil is a melting pot of <strong data-start=\"778\" data-end=\"839\">Indigenous, Portuguese, African, and immigrant influences</strong>, which shape its music, dance, religion, and cuisine. Traditions such as <strong data-start=\"913\" data-end=\"944\">samba, bossa nova, capoeira</strong>, and the colorful <strong data-start=\"963\" data-end=\"984\">Carnival festival</strong> reflect its lively spirit.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1015\" data-end=\"1319\">&nbsp;</p>', 'en', 4),
