(183, 'Alexandria', '<p data-start=\"49\" data-end=\"597\">Alexandria, often called the &ldquo;Pearl of the Mediterranean,&rdquo; blends ancient heritage with a relaxed coastal atmosphere. Founded by Alexander the Great, the city is home to iconic landmarks such as the modern Bibliotheca Alexandrina, the historic Qaitbay Citadel overlooking the sea, and the Roman Amphitheatre. Visitors can stroll along the Corniche, explore charming cafes and local markets, and discover traces of Egypt&rsquo;s Greco-Roman past throughout the city. Alexandria offers culture, history, and seaside beauty in one unforgettable destination.</p>', 'en', 27),
