(178, 46, 'en', 'Day 3 • Aswan', '<div class=\"accordion__item-body accordion__item-body-outline\" data-cy=\"accordion-body\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"rich-text\">\r\n<p>Catch a morning flight to Aswan &ndash; Egypt&rsquo;s southernmost city. Check into your hotel, then travel to Philae Island and visit the Temple of Isis &ndash; the goddess of health, marriage and wisdom &ndash; rescued from the rising waters of the Nile and relocated here. Your leader will share stories of the history and changing landscape of the island. Then, take a boat to a Nubian village on an island in the middle of the Nile. Walk through the village before sitting down to dinner with a local Nubian family in their home. Enjoy traditional Nubian food, swap stories with your friendly hosts and gain a unique perspective into their way of life.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meta-data-section u-margin-top--2\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--6-col l-grid__cell--12-col-tablet\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Accommodation</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li>Sonesta Nouba or similar (1 night)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Meals</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Breakfast</li>\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Dinner</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(179, 47, 'en', 'Day 4 • Aswan - Nile Cruise', '<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col l-grid__cell--4-col-desktop\">\r\n<div class=\"accordion__item-body accordion__item-body-outline\" data-cy=\"accordion-body\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"rich-text\">\r\n<p>After breakfast, you may like to take a stroll around Aswan or join an optional tour of Abu Simbel &ndash; a temple complex that was dismantled and moved to make way for the Aswan High Dam. Board a Nile riverboat &ndash; your Feature Stay accommodation for the next three nights! Travelling by riverboat allows you to get to the heart of each destination while ensuring the journeys in between are every bit as interesting. In the afternoon, board a traditional felucca sailing boat where you can sit back and relax with some drinks as the sun sets over your surroundings. Return to your riverboat for dinner.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meta-data-section u-margin-top--2\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--6-col l-grid__cell--12-col-tablet\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\">&nbsp;<strong>Accommodation</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li>Amwaj Nile Cruise (Feature Stay) or similar (1 night)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\">&nbsp;<strong>Meals</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Breakfast</li>\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Lunch</li>\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Dinner</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(180, 48, 'en', 'Day 5 • Nile Cruise - Edfu', '<div class=\"accordion__item-body accordion__item-body-outline\" data-cy=\"accordion-body\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"rich-text\">\r\n<p>Enjoy a peaceful morning on board your riverboat, then set out in the afternoon along the river, relaxing in the sun on deck and taking in the desert hills. Arrive at Kom Ombo Temple, where your leader will let you in on the secrets of this ancient sanctuary. Built in approximately 181 BC, Kom Ombo is dedicated to two gods &ndash; Horus (god of protection) and Sobek (god of fertility, linked to the Nile&rsquo;s water). Each god has a dedicated section &ndash; north or south &ndash; and there have been recent discoveries of mummified crocodiles in the Sobek section. After, return to your riverboat and continue to Edfu where you&rsquo;ll dock for the evening.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meta-data-section u-margin-top--2\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--6-col l-grid__cell--12-col-tablet\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Accommodation</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li>Amwaj Nile Cruise (Feature Stay) or similar (1 night)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Meals</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Breakfast</li>\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Lunch</li>\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Dinner</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(181, 49, 'en', 'Day 6 • Nile Cruise - Luxor', '<div class=\"accordion__item-body accordion__item-body-outline\" data-cy=\"accordion-body\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"rich-text\">\r\n<p>This morning, you&rsquo;ll be moored near Edfu and may have the option to venture independently into town to see the nearby temple. Sail towards Luxor passing through the Esna Locks. Arrive at the open-air museum of Luxor &ndash; from the spectacular temple complex of Karnak to the Valley of the Kings, Luxor is full of wonderfully preserved reminders of the Pharaohs. Today you\'ll explore the Karnak Temple. One of the world\'s most celebrated temple complexes, Karnak is a house of the gods built over a period of some 200 years. You&rsquo;ll also head over to our Intrepid Foundation partner, Animal Care in Egypt (ACE), a local NGO dedicated to providing free veterinary care for wounded working animals in the region.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meta-data-section u-margin-top--2\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--6-col l-grid__cell--12-col-tablet\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Accommodation</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li>Amwaj Nile Cruise (Feature Stay) or similar (1 night)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\">&nbsp;<strong>Meals</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Breakfast</li>\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Lunch</li>\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Dinner</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(182, 50, 'en', 'Day 7 • Luxor', '<div class=\"accordion__item-body accordion__item-body-outline\" data-cy=\"accordion-body\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"rich-text\">\r\n<p>Today you will leave your riverboat and travel to the Valley of the Kings. Buried under the arid hills are over 60 tombs of pharaohs, many richly decorated with reliefs and paintings. With your leader, explore the place where the pharaohs of the New Kingdom (16th to 11th century BC) were secretly interred for all eternity, and where discoveries are still being made. Your leader will explain the history and legends of these people and the significance of the many paintings and hieroglyphics. Entry is included to three tombs of your choosing, as well as access to the tomb of Tutankhamun. The unearthing of the young Pharaoh&rsquo;s resting place is one of the world&rsquo;s greatest archaeological discoveries, and today you&rsquo;ll explore the painted chamber that holds his famous golden sarcophagus. Continue to the Temple of Queen Hatshepsut then view the Colossi of Memnon &ndash; two 17-m-high statues on Luxor\'s west bank.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meta-data-section u-margin-top--2\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--6-col l-grid__cell--12-col-tablet\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Accommodation</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li>Sonesta St George Hotel or similar (1 night)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\">&nbsp;<strong>Meals</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Breakfast</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(183, 51, 'en', 'Day 8 • Cairo', '<div class=\"accordion__item-body accordion__item-body-outline\" data-cy=\"accordion-body\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"rich-text\">\r\n<p>Board a flight to Cairo this morning. When you arrive, settle into your hotel then head out to the Al-Azhar neighbourhood to visit Khan al-Khalili Bazaar &ndash; a sprawling maze of alleyways including the gold market, cloth market, \'perfume street\' and the spice market. Continue to the 9th-century Al-Azhar Mosque &ndash; one of the oldest and largest in Egypt and a masterpiece of Islamic architecture. Stop off in Cairo&rsquo;s oldest coffeeshop for an Arabic coffee or mint tea as you watch the world go by. The best food in Cairo is made inside a local home &ndash; this afternoon, you&rsquo;ll be welcomed into the home of a local family to sit down and enjoy a meal of traditional dishes as you gain an inside look at modern Egyptian life.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meta-data-section u-margin-top--2\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--6-col l-grid__cell--12-col-tablet\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Accommodation</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li>Steigenberger Hotel El Tahrir Cairo, Sonesta Cairo, or similar (1 night)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Meals</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Breakfast</li>\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Dinner</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(184, 52, 'en', 'Day 9 • Cairo', '<div class=\"accordion__item-body accordion__item-body-outline\" data-cy=\"accordion-body\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"rich-text\">\r\n<p>Your trip will come to an end today after breakfast and you&rsquo;re free to leave at any time after check out. If you have arranged a private airport transfer, you&rsquo;ll be advised of the pick-up time. If you would like to spend more time in Cairo, just get in touch with your booking agent ahead of time to organise additional accommodation.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meta-data-section u-margin-top--2\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--6-col l-grid__cell--12-col-tablet\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Meals</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Breakfast</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(185, 53, 'en', 'Day 2 • Cairo', '<div class=\"accordion__item-body accordion__item-body-outline\" data-cy=\"accordion-body\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"rich-text\">\r\n<p>This morning, tour the mighty Pyramids of Giza &ndash; one of the famed Seven Wonders of the World &ndash;and the Sphinx with your leader and expert local guide. For an additional charge, you may be able to go inside the Great Pyramid of Khufu (or Cheops). After some time for lunch, your adventure continues to the Egyptian Museum &ndash; home to one of the world\'s great collections of ancient artefacts recovered from the tomb of Tutankhamun. From jewellery to the famous golden death mask and his gilded sarcophagi, this pharaoh was certainly prepared for the afterlife. Your leader will take you through some of Egypt&rsquo;s dynastic history and you&rsquo;ll have plenty of time to explore on your own &ndash; home to almost 100,000 artefacts, there&rsquo;s a whole ancient world to uncover!</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meta-data-section u-margin-top--2\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--6-col l-grid__cell--12-col-tablet\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid\">\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Accommodation</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li>Steigenberger Cairo Pyramids Hotel or similar (1 night)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--12-col\">\r\n<div class=\"u-font-weight--bold\"><strong>&nbsp;Meals</strong></div>\r\n<ul class=\"u-padding-left--2\">\r\n<li class=\"trip-itinerary-day__meals-list-item\">Breakfast</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l-grid__cell l-grid__cell--6-col l-grid__cell--12-col-tablet\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
