(364, 88, 'en', 'Day 3-The Grand Egyptian Museum', '<div>\r\n<div class=\"flex gap-1 items-center\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"flex flex-col gap-2 mt-3 md:mt-2 px-2 md:px-0\">\r\n<div class=\"flex flex-col gap-2 lg:block\">\r\n<p class=\"text-otg-neutrals-900  group-open:animate-fadeIn text-sm md:text-base\">Cairo - Aswan. This morning we join our guided tour of the incredible new Grand Egyptian Museum in Giza. This vast 490,000 sq.m complex showcases an astonishing collection of artefacts from nearly every period of ancient Egyptian history. Among the highlights are treasures of King Tutankhamun, with plans for his famous solid gold funerary mask to eventually be showcased here, alongside many items being exhibited for the first time.<br><br>Later, we make our way to the Egyptian Museum in Cairo, which remains home to a vast collection of statues, jewellery, and sarcophagi. Here, we&rsquo;ll see the well-preserved mummies of Yuya and Thuyu, high-ranking nobles and the great-grandparents of King Tutankhamun. Some mummies are so well preserved they still have thick locks of hair and visible fingernails. Then there\'s time to relax back at the hotel before boarding the night train to Aswan this evening. You can opt to fly the distance to Aswan by choosing our \'Fly Cairo to Aswan\' Add-on.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"flex flex-col gap-1 pl-[4px] pt-2\">\r\n<div class=\"flex gap-1 items-center\"><span class=\"text-base md:text-lg text-otg-neutrals-900 font-semibold\">Overnight:</span><span class=\"text-base md:text-lg text-black font-normal\">Sleeper Train</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"flex gap-1 items-center\"><span class=\"text-base md:text-lg text-otg-neutrals-900 font-semibold\">Meals:</span><span class=\"text-base md:text-lg text-black font-normal\">Breakfast</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(365, 88, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
