(378, 90, 'en', 'Day 5-Nile Cruise & Kom Ombo. Optional Abu Simbel', '<div>\r\n<div class=\"flex gap-1 items-center\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"flex flex-col gap-2 mt-3 md:mt-2 px-2 md:px-0\">\r\n<div class=\"flex flex-col gap-2 lg:block\">\r\n<p class=\"text-otg-neutrals-900  group-open:animate-fadeIn text-sm md:text-base\">Aswan - Nile Cruise - Kom Ombo. Early birds can go on an optional excursion to the majestic Temple of&nbsp;Abu Simbel. The gargantuan rock-cut temple at Abu Simbel was created to revere the mighty pharaonic ruler King Ramses II. Guarding the entrance to the temple, the four colossal statues of Ramses II sit majestically, staring out across the desert. This afternoon our cruiser plies its way along the Nile toward Kom Ombo where we disembark to visit the temple which is dedicated to the crocodile headed god - Sobek before returning to our floating hotel for the night,</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"flex flex-col gap-1 pl-[4px] pt-2\">\r\n<div class=\"flex gap-1 items-center\"><span class=\"text-base md:text-lg text-otg-neutrals-900 font-semibold\">Overnight:</span><span class=\"text-base md:text-lg text-black font-normal\">Nile Cruiser</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"flex gap-1 items-center\"><span class=\"text-base md:text-lg text-otg-neutrals-900 font-semibold\">Meals:</span><span class=\"text-base md:text-lg text-black font-normal\">Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
