(548, 122, 'en', 'Day 1:   Arrive into Cairo, transfer to hotel', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Upon arrival our staff will meet you at the airport and transfer you to your hotel for the start of your trip. They will help you settle in, introduce you to the local area, and explain tomorrow\'s arrangements.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"day-included row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>OVERNIGHT: </strong>Cairo hotel</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>EXTRAS: </strong>Single room supplement (EGSG27)</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(549, 122, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(550, 122, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(551, 122, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(552, 122, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(553, 122, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(554, 122, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(555, 123, 'en', 'Day 2:   Visit the Pyramids in Giza and the stepped Pyramid in Saqqara', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info animated fadeIn delay-2s\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Our Egyptian adventure begins with a journey back in time to the Giza Plateau, home to the iconic Great Pyramids.&nbsp; These magnificent structures, declared one of the Seven Wonders of the ancient world by the Greeks,&nbsp; will leave you breathless with their sheer size and intricate construction. We\'ll explore the Pyramids of Giza, including the Great Pyramid of Khufu, and encounter the enigmatic Sphinx, standing guard over these ancient wonders.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">But that\'s not all! We\'ll also delve deeper into Egypt\'s rich history with a visit to Memphis, the first capital of the ancient kingdom. Here, we\'ll come face-to-face with the colossal statue of Ramses II, a powerful reminder of the pharaohs who once ruled this land.&nbsp; Our journey continues to Sakkara, where we\'ll marvel at the Step Pyramid of Djoser, an architectural masterpiece that predates the Great Pyramids and offers a fascinating glimpse into the evolution of pyramid construction.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"day-included row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>OVERNIGHT: </strong>Cairo hotel</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>MEALS: </strong>Breakfast</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(556, 124, 'en', 'Day 3:   Discover the wonders of ancient Egypt at the GEM. Fly to Luxor', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info animated fadeIn delay-2s\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Begin your day with breakfast at the hotel, anticipating a truly monumental experience. Today, we delve into the treasures of Egypt\'s Pharaonic past at the Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM), located near the Giza Plateau. This state-of-the-art museum houses an unparalleled collection of artefacts, offering a comprehensive insight into ancient Egyptian civilisation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Prepare to be amazed as you explore the vast exhibition halls. The highlight for many is the complete Tutankhamun collection, displayed together for the first time, showcasing the dazzling golden mask, sarcophagi, chariots, and thousands of other objects discovered in the young pharaoh\'s tomb. Wander through galleries dedicated to different periods, marvelling at colossal statues, intricate jewellery, and everyday items that bring ancient Egypt vividly to life. The museum\'s modern design and interpretative displays provide a captivating context for these timeless wonders.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Following our immersive museum visit, we will have a break for lunch before transferring to Cairo Airport. Here, we board a short domestic flight southwards to Luxor, the city often described as the world\'s greatest open-air museum. Upon arrival in Luxor, ancient Thebes, you\'ll be met and transferred to the Beau Rivage Nile Cruise which will be your base for the next 6 nights.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">After settling in, enjoy dinner and relax. The evening is yours to perhaps take a gentle stroll or simply rest, ready to explore the magnificent temples and tombs of Luxor, the heartland of the New Kingdom pharaohs, tomorrow.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"day-included row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>OVERNIGHT: </strong>Beau Rivage Nile Cruise</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>MEALS: </strong>Breakfast, Dinner</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(557, 125, 'en', 'Day 4:   Morning visit to the West Bank of the Nile. Afternoon exploring Karnak and Luxor Temples on the East Bank', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info animated fadeIn delay-2s\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Get ready to be impressed as we begin our exploration of the Nile\'s West Bank, a place steeped in ancient Egyptian mythology and history.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Our first stop will be the Colossi of Memnon, two towering statues that have stood sentinel for millennia.&nbsp; Imagine the stories these giants could tell!&nbsp; From there, we\'ll venture into the Valley of the Kings, a hidden valley where pharaohs, including the legendary Tutankhamun, were laid to rest.&nbsp; We\'ll get to explore these elaborately decorated tombs and uncover the secrets of their fascinating past.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Next, we\'ll journey to the Temple of Queen Hatshepsut, a magnificent complex built into the cliffs, dedicated to one of Egypt\'s few female pharaohs.&nbsp; We\'ll marvel at its grandeur and learn about the powerful queen who ruled over Egypt.&nbsp; Our West Bank adventure culminates with a visit to Medinat Habu, a temple complex adorned with vibrant and intricate hieroglyphics that depict scenes of ancient Egyptian life and mythology.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">After a break for lunch our next stop is the sprawling Karnak Temple complex, arguably the largest religious building ever constructed. We will spend time navigating its immense grounds, exploring the layers of history built by generations of pharaohs and marvelling at key features like the Sacred Lake and the towering columns of the Great Hypostyle Hall. Subsequently, our visit takes us to Luxor Temple. We\'ll explore its elegant courts, chapels, and the remaining sections of the Avenue of Sphinxes, appreciating the temple\'s unique construction, which includes Roman and Coptic additions, reflecting its long history.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"day-included row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>OVERNIGHT: </strong>Beau Rivage Nile Cruise</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>MEALS: </strong>Breakfast, Dinner, Lunch</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>EXTRAS: </strong>Hot air balloon in Luxor</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(558, 126, 'en', 'Day 5:   Witnessing the Great Luxor Eclipse. Sail to Edfu.', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info animated fadeIn delay-2s\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Today promises to be an extraordinary highlight of your journey, a day centred around one of nature\'s most awe-inspiring spectacles: a total solar eclipse. On this date, Luxor finds itself uniquely positioned as a prime gateway to witness an exceptionally long totality, occurring just outside the city limits.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">The morning will begin with palpable excitement and anticipation. After breakfast, preparations will be made to travel to a carefully selected viewing site in Luxor, and you will be provided with a packed lunch for the day. This location has been chosen to ensure the best possible, unobstructed view of the sky, placing you directly within the path of totality for the maximum duration possible in this region &ndash; predicted to be over an incredible six minutes!</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">As the morning progresses, the celestial drama will begin to unfold. You will witness the Moon starting its slow passage across the face of the Sun, taking an increasingly large \'bite\' out of it. You will be provided with special eclipse viewing glasses, essential for protecting your eyes during these partial phases. Observe the subtle, yet increasingly noticeable, changes in the quality of light; colours may seem sharper, shadows strangely defined, and the ambient temperature might begin a slight, perceptible dip even before the main event.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Then, in the moments leading up to totality, the sky will dramatically darken. You might witness the phenomenon of shadow bands rippling across the landscape. As the last sliver of the Sun vanishes behind the Moon, the world will transform. Day will plunge into an eerie, deep twilight. Remove your viewing glasses only when totality begins, and prepare to be mesmerised.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">For over six breathtaking minutes &ndash; an unusually long duration for a total eclipse &ndash; you will stand under a sky unlike any other. The Sun\'s magnificent outer atmosphere, the ethereal corona, will blaze into view, streaming outwards around the black silhouette of the Moon. Brighter stars and planets may become visible in the darkened sky. Look towards the horizon, and you might see colours reminiscent of a 360-degree sunset. Experience the distinct drop in temperature and listen to the potential reactions of wildlife or the hushed awe of your fellow observers. It is a truly multi-sensory experience, standing in the Moon\'s shadow.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Just as suddenly as it began, the end of totality will approach. A brilliant burst of light, known as the \'diamond ring effect\', will signal the Sun\'s reappearance, requiring you to immediately use your eclipse glasses again. Daylight will swiftly return, the temperature will climb, and the partial phases will proceed in reverse as the Moon gradually moves away from the Sun.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Reflecting on this profound experience, perhaps contemplating how the ancient Egyptians themselves might have reacted to such an event amidst their monumental temples, will add another layer to the day.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">While the precise timings and logistical details for accessing the prime viewing location will be finalised and communicated closer to August 2027, rest assured that every arrangement will be made to guarantee you are in an optimal position, complete with necessary viewing equipment and refreshments, to safely witness the full, spellbinding totality of this historic solar eclipse near Luxor.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">After witnessing the Solar Eclipse, we\'ll return to our cruise boat and sail south to Edfu.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"day-included row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>OVERNIGHT: </strong>Beau Rivage Nile Cruise</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>MEALS: </strong>Breakfast, Dinner, Lunch</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(559, 127, 'en', 'Day 6:   Visit Edfu Temple and cruise to Aswan', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info animated fadeIn delay-2s\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">After a leisurely breakfast on board, we\'ll disembark and head to the nearby Temple of Edfu. This remarkably well-preserved temple, dedicated to the falcon-headed god Horus, is a stunning example of Ptolemaic architecture. As you wander through its impressive courtyards, you\'ll be transported back in time, imagining the processions of priests and pharaohs that once graced these halls. Admire the intricate reliefs depicting scenes of Horus\'s mythology, and learn about the temple\'s important role in ancient Egyptian religious practices.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Back on board our comfortable cruise ship, we\'ll continue our journey up the Nile towards Aswan, soaking in the ever-changing scenery. The pace of life along the riverbanks unfolds at a slower pace here, offering a captivating glimpse into traditional rural life in Egypt. Watch as farmers tend their fields using age-old methods, fishermen cast their nets into the flowing waters, and children play along the shore. It\'s a timeless scene that speaks to the enduring connection between the Egyptian people and the Nile River.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">As we cruise, why not take some time for yourself to relax and unwind? Head to the sundeck and enjoy a refreshing dip in the plunge pool, perhaps with a cool drink in hand. Or simply find a comfortable spot to lounge in the sun with a good book, letting the gentle rocking of the boat and the warm breeze lull you into a state of pure tranquility.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Our cruise continues southward towards Aswan, the historic gateway to Nubia. Enjoy the remaining daylight hours out on deck, watching the sun cast long shadows over the river and the desert landscape as we approach this vibrant city. Perhaps you\'ll spot traditional felucca sailboats gliding along the water, or catch sight of a Nubian village with its brightly painted houses.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"day-included row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>OVERNIGHT: </strong>Beau Rivage Nile Cruise</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>MEALS: </strong>Breakfast, Dinner, Lunch</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(560, 128, 'en', 'Day 7:   Abu Simbel option. Sail the Nile on a traditional Felucca. Visit Philae Temple & Aswan Dam', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info animated fadeIn delay-2s\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">This morning, you have the incredible opportunity to embark on an optional excursion to the awe-inspiring Abu Simbel, a UNESCO World Heritage Site that stands as a testament to the grandeur of ancient Egypt. We\'ll depart before dawn, making our way through the desert landscape. Our goal is to arrive in time to witness the magical moment when the rising sun illuminates the facade of the temples, casting a golden glow on the colossal statues of Ramses II. It\'s a truly unforgettable experience that captures the mystique and majesty of this ancient wonder. Please note that if you choose to visit Abu Simbel, you will not participate in the Felucca sailboat trip which takes place this morning.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">If you choose to remain in Aswan, we\'ll step back in time and experience the magic of the Nile River firsthand with a leisurely sail on a traditional Felucca sailboat. Imagine yourself gliding along the legendary waters, the gentle breeze filling the sails as you soak in the stunning scenery of Aswan from a unique perspective. It\'s the perfect way to unwind and connect with the soul of Egypt before continuing our explorations.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Our afternoon tour in Aswan takes us to the enchanting island temple complex of Philae, dedicated to the goddess Isis. We\'ll journey by boat to this picturesque island, where the temple complex, with its graceful columns and intricate carvings, seems to rise organically from the water. Philae remains one of Egypt\'s most romantic and picturesque sites, its beauty enhanced by its remarkable history. The entire complex was carefully dismantled and relocated to its current location following the construction of the Aswan High Dam, ensuring its preservation for generations to come.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Speaking of the dam, we\'ll also pay a visit to the impressive Aswan High Dam, a monumental feat of engineering that harnessed the power of the Nile and created Lake Nasser, one of the world\'s largest man-made lakes. We\'ll learn about the dam\'s construction and its impact on Egypt, both positive and negative, gaining a deeper understanding of this country\'s complex relationship with its lifeline, the Nile River.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"day-included row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>OVERNIGHT: </strong>Beau Rivage Nile Cruise</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>MEALS: </strong>Breakfast, Dinner, Lunch</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>EXTRAS: </strong>Abu Simbel overland</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(561, 129, 'en', 'Day 8:   Sail to Luxor, stopping at Kom Ombo Temple along the way', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info animated fadeIn delay-2s\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">With our cruise ship turning back towards Luxor, our next port of call is Kom Ombo, home to a truly remarkable temple. Standing dramatically on the Nile\'s edge, this temple holds the distinction of being dedicated to two deities: Sobek, the crocodile god, and Haroeris, the falcon god. We\'ll have the chance to explore its intriguing chambers and discover the story behind its unique dual dedication. Be sure to see the display of mummified crocodiles, which highlights the ancient Egyptians\' deep respect for these formidable animals. We\'ll then have a final night onboard in Luxor with free time to further explore the town at your leisure, or perhaps revisit Karnak Temple for the Sound and Light Show.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"day-included row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>OVERNIGHT: </strong>Beau Rivage Nile Cruise</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>MEALS: </strong>Breakfast, Dinner, Lunch</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>EXTRAS: </strong>Karnak Sound &amp; Light Show</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(562, 130, 'en', 'Day 9:   Morning flight to Cairo. Explore Khan-el-Khalili Bazaar', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info animated fadeIn delay-2s\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Our day begins with a transfer to Luxor airport to catch a morning flight northwards to Cairo. Upon arrival at Cairo Airport, you will be met and transferred towards the heart of the historic city for an unforgettable cultural immersion.</p>\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">This afternoon\'s tour takes you to the famous Khan el-Khalili bazaar, one of the oldest and most atmospheric marketplaces in the Middle East. Prepare to be captivated as you navigate its maze-like alleys, which have buzzed with activity for centuries. Experience the vibrant tapestry of sights, sounds, and smells &ndash; from the glint of handcrafted metalwork and colourful lanterns to the rich scent of exotic spices and perfumes, and the lively calls of vendors. It is the perfect place to browse for unique souvenirs, traditional crafts, jewellery, and textiles, or perhaps pause to soak up the bustling atmosphere in a traditional coffeehouse (ahwa). This visit offers a fascinating glimpse into the enduring commercial and cultural spirit of Cairo.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"day-included row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>OVERNIGHT: </strong>Cairo hotel</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-md-3\">\r\n<p class=\"m-0 p-0 \"><strong>MEALS: </strong>Breakfast</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(563, 131, 'en', 'Day 10:   Cairo, departure transfer to the airport', '<div class=\"row toggle-itin\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"itinerary-info animated fadeIn delay-2s\">\r\n<div class=\"row \">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-12 \">\r\n<p class=\"lead text-justify \">Your time is free today until we transfer you to the airport for your departure flight. Extensions are available to add onto the end of the tour to spend some time by the Red Sea, add some day trips to Alexandria or visit the World Heritage Site of Wadi Rayan and the Valley of the Whales.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
