(1215, 225, 'en', 'ARRIVAL Day 1 FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will<br>assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we<br>will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local<br>surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey.</p>'),
(1216, 225, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1217, 225, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1218, 225, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1219, 225, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1220, 225, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1221, 225, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1222, 226, 'en', 'FREE DAY - Day 2 - SATURDAY,31TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>After Breakfast, you will have free time to relax and enjoy the beautiful of the red sea at your leisure.<br><strong>Overnight in Hurghada.</strong><br><br></p>'),
(1223, 227, 'en', 'FREE DAY - Day 3 - SUNDAY,1 ST OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After Breakfast, Enjoy more free time by the red sea to relax, explore, or just soak up the sun.<br><strong>Overnight in Hurghada</strong></p>'),
(1224, 228, 'en', 'KARNAK TEMPLE & LUXOR TEMPLE - MONDAY,2ND OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>leave Hurghada in the early Morning, transfer to Luxor. Next, Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple, A special chance to witness the total<br>solar eclipse from Karnak Temple. Watching this rare event from such a historic place will be a truly unforgettable experience.<br>Proceeding our tour to Luxor Temple in which you&rsquo;ll stand in the shadows of the Great Ramses II colossi.<br>Back to Hurghada.KARNAK TEMPLE<br><strong>Overnight in Hurghada.</strong></p>'),
(1225, 229, 'en', 'FREE DAY - Day 5 - TUESDAY,3RD OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>free day at leisure.<br>optional activities: Snorkeling, diving, desert safari.Overnight in Hurghada</p>'),
(1226, 230, 'en', 'CHECK OUT - FLY BACK TO CAIRO, FINAL DEPARTURE - WEDNESDAY,4TH OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out from your Hotel.<br>Catch our flight back to Cairo. catch your international flight.<br><br></p>'),
(1227, 231, 'en', 'Day 1 CAIRO BY NIGHT TUESDAY,27TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will&nbsp;assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we&nbsp;will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local&nbsp;surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey.<br><br><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(1228, 231, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1229, 231, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1230, 231, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1231, 231, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1232, 231, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1233, 231, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1234, 232, 'en', 'THE PYRAMIDS OF GIZA, THE GREAT SPHINX, LUNCH, GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After Breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to visit the Pyramids and the Sphinx, which are the only surviving<br>wonder of the ancient world. You will have the option to enjoy a memorable camel ride in the vicinity of these magnificent<br>structures. Ahead of the pyramids, lies the Sphinx known as the guardian of the pyramids facing the sun every morning as it<br>rises from the east. Lunch will then be served at a local hygienic restaurant. Proceeding to The Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)<br>will host over 100,000 artifacts from ancient Egyptian civilization, many pieces are displayed for the first time.<br><br><strong>WEDNESDAY,28TH OF JULY 2027 - Overnight in Cairo</strong></p>'),
(1235, 233, 'en', 'THURSDAY,29TH OF JULY 2027 - FLY TO ASWAN, PHILAE TEMPLE, HIGH DAM', '<p>After Breakfast, you will catch your flight to Aswan . Check in your Hotel.<br>Next, you will visit Philae Temple also referred to as the Temple of Lovers which narrates the most ancient love story in&nbsp;history between Isis and Osiris. After that visit The High Dam, a rock fill dam across the River Nile at Aswan, completed&nbsp;in 1970 (and formally inaugurated in January 1971) The dam is 364 feet (111 meters) high, with a crest length of 12,562&nbsp;feet (3,830 meters) and a volume of 57,940,000 cubic yards (44,300,000 cubic meters), impounds a reservoir, Lake&nbsp;Nasser, that has a gross capacity of 5.97 trillion cubic feet (169 billion cubic meters.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Aswan</strong></p>'),
(1236, 234, 'en', 'ABU SIMBEL - FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will be transferred to Abu Simbel where you will be standing in front of a<br>temple carved in the mountain; a true miracle of ancient and modern engineering that<br>deserves to be counted among the wonders of the world.<br>back to Aswan.<br><br><strong>Overnight in Aswan.</strong></p>'),
(1237, 235, 'en', 'KOMOMBO TEMPLE & EDFU TEMPLE - SATURDAY,31TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>After having breakfast, we will transfer to Luxor by car. Next will visit Kom Ombo Temple, a very unusual temple. It\'s<br>uniqueness is for several reasons. It is dedication to two different deities, the local crocodile-headed god, Sobek, and the<br>falcon-headed god Horus. After that we will visit Edfu Temple . Considered to be one of the best preserved temples from<br>ancient Egypt, It is the largest temple dedicated to the god Horus.<br><br><strong>Overnight in Luxor</strong></p>'),
(1238, 236, 'en', 'VALLEY OF KINGS, QUEEN HATSHEPSUT MORTURY TEMPLE, COLOSSI OF MEMNON', '<p>After having breakfast, you will be taken to the West Bank and visit The Valley of Kings the home Egypt most known Pharoahs. The tour&nbsp;covers the special visit of 5 tombs including the Golden Pharaoh Tutankhamun&rsquo;s tomb and Ramesses VI. Then we head to visit Queen<br>Hatshepsut&rsquo;s magnificant Mortuary Temple built 3300 years ago; a unique temple that is engraved by the mountains and partially carved&nbsp;out of the rocks. After that visit Colossi of Memnon,Two towering statues of Pharaoh Amenhotep III, standing 18 meters high, built to guard&nbsp;the entrance of his lost mortuary temple. They are among the most iconic landmarks on Luxor&rsquo;s west bank.<br><strong>SUNDAY,1ST OF AUGUST 2027</strong><br><strong>Overnight in Luxor</strong></p>'),
(1239, 237, 'en', 'KARNAK TEMPLE & LUXOR TEMPLE - MONDAY,2ND OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>In the Morning: Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple, A special chance to witness the total solar eclipse from Karnak Temple. Watching<br>this rare event from such a historic place will be a truly unforgettable experience.<br>Proceeding our tour to Luxor Temple in which you&rsquo;ll stand in the shadows of the Great Ramses II colossi.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Luxor .</strong></p>'),
(1240, 238, 'en', 'CHECK OUT - FLY BACK TO CAIRO, FINAL DEPARTURE - TUESDAY,3RD OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out from your Hotel.<br>Catch our flight back to Cairo. catch your international flight.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Final Departure</strong></p>'),
(1241, 239, 'en', 'ARRIVAL - FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will&nbsp;assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we&nbsp;will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local&nbsp;surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(1242, 239, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1243, 239, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1244, 239, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1245, 239, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1246, 239, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1247, 239, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1248, 240, 'en', 'THE PYRAMIDS OF GIZA, THE GREAT SPHINX, LUNCH, GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After Breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to visit the Pyramids and the Sphinx, which are the only surviving&nbsp;wonder of the ancient world. You will have the option to enjoy a memorable camel ride in the vicinity of these magnificent&nbsp;structures. Ahead of the pyramids, lies the Sphinx known as the guardian of the pyramids facing the sun every morning as it&nbsp;rises from the east. Lunch will then be served at a local hygienic restaurant. Proceeding to The Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)&nbsp;will host over 100,000 artifacts from ancient Egyptian civilization, many pieces are displayed for the first time<br><br><strong>SATURDAY,31TH OF JULY 2027 - Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(1249, 241, 'en', 'VALLEY OF KINGS, QUEEN HATSHEPSUT MORTURY TEMPLE, COLOSSI OF MEMNON', '<p>After having breakfast, After Breakfast, you will catch your flight to Luxor. Check in your Hotel. Next, you will be taken to the West Bank and&nbsp;visit The Valley of Kings the home Egypt most known Pharoahs. The tour covers the special visit of 5 tombs including the Golden Pharaoh&nbsp;Tutankhamun&rsquo;s tomb and Ramesses VI. Then we head to visit Queen Hatshepsut&rsquo;s magnificant Mortuary Temple built 3300 years ago; a&nbsp;unique temple that is engraved by the mountains and partially carved out of the rocks. After that visit Colossi of Memnon,Two towering&nbsp;statues of Pharaoh Amenhotep III, standing 18 meters high, built to guard the entrance of his lost mortuary temple. They are among the&nbsp;most iconic landmarks on Luxor&rsquo;s west bank.</p>\r\n<p><strong>SUNDAY,1ST OF AUGUST 2027 - Overnight in Luxor</strong></p>'),
(1250, 242, 'en', 'KARNAK TEMPLE & LUXOR TEMPLE - MONDAY,2ND OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>In the Morning: Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple, A special chance to witness the total solar eclipse from Karnak Temple. Watching&nbsp;this rare event from such a historic place will be a truly unforgettable experience.<br>Proceeding our tour to Luxor Temple in which you&rsquo;ll stand in the shadows of the Great Ramses II colossi</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Luxor .</strong></p>'),
(1251, 243, 'en', 'CHECK OUT - FLY BACK TO CAIRO, FINAL DEPARTURE - TUESDAY,3RD OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out from your Hotel.<br>Catch our flight back to Cairo. catch your international flight.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Final Departure</strong></p>'),
(1252, 244, 'en', 'ARRIVAL - FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will&nbsp;assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we&nbsp;will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local&nbsp;surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey<br><br><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
