(1258, 244, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1259, 245, 'en', 'THE PYRAMIDS OF GIZA, THE GREAT SPHINX, LUNCH, GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After Breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to visit the Pyramids and the Sphinx, which are the only surviving&nbsp;wonder of the ancient world. You will have the option to enjoy a memorable camel ride in the vicinity of these magnificent&nbsp;structures. Ahead of the pyramids, lies the Sphinx known as the guardian of the pyramids facing the sun every morning as it&nbsp;rises from the east. Lunch will then be served at a local hygienic restaurant. Proceeding to The Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)&nbsp;will host over 100,000 artifacts from ancient Egyptian civilization, many pieces are displayed for the first time</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(1260, 246, 'en', 'FLY TO HURGHADA - SUNDAY,1 ST OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After Breakfast, you will catch your flight to Hurghada. Check in your Hotel.<br>Afternoon free time to enjoy the red sea</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Hurghada</strong></p>'),
(1261, 247, 'en', 'KARNAK TEMPLE & LUXOR TEMPLE - MONDAY,2ND OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>leave Hurghada in the early Morning, transfer to Luxor. Next, Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple, A special chance to witness the total&nbsp;solar eclipse from Karnak Temple. Watching this rare event from such a historic place will be a truly unforgettable experience.<br>Proceeding our tour to Luxor Temple in which you&rsquo;ll stand in the shadows of the Great Ramses II colossi.&nbsp;Back to Hurghada.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Hurghada</strong></p>'),
(1262, 248, 'en', 'FREE DAY - TUESDAY,3RD OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>free day at leisure.<br>optional activities: Snorkeling, diving, desert safari.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Hurghada</strong></p>'),
(1263, 249, 'en', 'Day 1: Arrival', '<p>Upon arrival at Cairo International Airport, you will be met and<br>escorted by one of Egygo Travel representatives . They will assist<br>you in obtaining the necessary entry documents and guide you<br>through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we will<br>travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on<br>your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local<br>surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your<br>journey.<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(1264, 249, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1265, 249, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1266, 249, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1267, 249, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1268, 249, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1269, 249, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1270, 250, 'en', 'Day 2 GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to&nbsp;visit the Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM) Located near the&nbsp;Pyramids, the Grand Egyptian Museum is the largest&nbsp;archaeological museum in the world. It houses over&nbsp;100,000 artifacts, including the complete collection of&nbsp;King Tutankhamun. Designed to reflect ancient Egyptian&nbsp;heritage with a modern touch, GEM features state-of-the-&nbsp;art exhibits, conservation labs, and a grand staircase with&nbsp;colossal statues. A cultural landmark, it offers a unique&nbsp;journey through 5,000 years of history in one spectacular&nbsp;setting.<br>Egygo Travel would like to invite you to the Welcome&nbsp;Dinner.<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(1271, 251, 'en', 'Day 3 Private visit to the Great Sphinx and Saqqara complex', '<p>Following breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you<br>for your special private visit to The Great Sphinx, arranged<br>by Egygo\'s experienced Egyptologist, commences by<br>private motor coach to the Giza Plateau. Constructed<br>around 2500BC (Old Kingdom) , the Great Sphinx is a<br>mythical creature with the head of a human and the body<br>of a lion. Facing east, The Great Sphinx greets the morning<br>sun while protecting the Giza pyramids.<br>After that, you will get to visit the Sakkara Complex, which<br>was the main burial area for kings, queens and nobles<br>during the old kingdom, in the same area, you will have the<br>opportunity to visit the Step Pyramid of King Djoser,<br>renowned as the first successful attempt at constructing a<br>standing pyramid 4800 years old</p>'),
(1272, 252, 'en', 'Day 4 Flight to Luxor, Abydos Temple and overnight in Suhag', '<p>After breakfast, we travel to Cairo International Airport for<br>your flight to Luxor.<br>Upon arrival, we will be taken by private motor coach to<br>explore Abydos.<br>Abydos, home to the Temple of Seti I, father of Ramses II, is<br>one of the most important archaeological sites of Ancient<br>Egypt. During ancient times, it was the necropolis for Egypt\'s<br>earliest kings. The \"Abydos King List\" as well as Phoenician<br>and Aramaic graffiti are found on the temple walls.<br>While in Abydos, Egygo\'s Egytologist has arranged for a<br>private visit to the Osierion, it is normally closed to tourists.<br>The Osierion, a megalithic structure, built below ground<br>simulates an island. It is positioned at the rear of the Temple,<br>accessed only through the Temple body. On one of its<br>monoliths is painted the FLOWER OF LIFE, one of the most<br>important symbols of sacred geometry.<br>Overnight in Suhag</p>'),
(1273, 253, 'en', 'Day 5 Dendera Temple and back to Luxor', '<p>Following breakfast, we set off, accompanied by our Egygo Egyptologist, to explore Dendera Temple.<br>Dedicated to goddess Hathor , the Temple is one of the best-preserved temples in Egypt. Depictions of Cleopatra VI appear on<br>Temple walls. On the rear wall is a carving of Cleoppatra VI (the popular Cleopatria) and her son Ptolemy XV who was fathered by Julius<br>Cesar.<br>Following our visits, we will have lunch at a local restaurant.<br>After lunch, we will transfer to Luxor for check-in at our Dahabiya.<br>Overnight in Luxor on board of Dahabiya.</p>'),
(1274, 254, 'en', 'Day 6 Valley of the Kings and Karnak Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will start our tour by visiting Karnak Temple<br>which is believed to be the second most visited historical site<br>surpassed only by the Giza Pyramids. One of the many<br>highlights of Karnak Temple\'s is it hypostyle hall consisting of<br>134 massive columns in 16 rows.<br>Next stop is The Valley of Kings, the final resting place of many<br>of the ancient Egyptian Pharaohs. Here, we will visit some of the<br>better known tombs including that of Pharaoh Tutankhamen.<br>Overnight on board our dahabiya</p>'),
(1275, 255, 'en', 'Day 7 Edfu Temple and Komombo Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will visit Edfu Temple . Considered to be one of<br>the best preserved temples from ancient Egypt, It is the largest<br>temple dedicated to the god Horus and his consort , the goddess,<br>Hathor of Dendera. Each year, Hathor would travel from her temple<br>in Dendera to visit Horus at Edfu. This event marked their sacred<br>marriage and, in ancient times, was an occasion of a great Festival<br>and pilgrimage. we will visit Kom Ombo Temple, a very unusual<br>temple. It\'s uniqueness is for several reasons. It is dedication to<br>two different deities, the local crocodile-headed god, Sobek, and<br>the falcon-headed god Horus.<br>Return to Dahabiya for overnight sailing Aswan<br>Overnight on board.</p>'),
(1276, 256, 'en', 'Day 8 Philae Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will be boarding a small motor boat from the landing, We will head to the Philae Island. The island is home to Philae<br>Temple aka \"Temple of Lovers\" Dedicated to the goddess Isis, Philae Temple presents the perfect backdrop to the most ancient of all<br>love stories in history, that of Isis and Osiris.<br>Back to Dahabiya<br>Overnight on board</p>'),
(1277, 257, 'en', 'Day 9 Abu Simble Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will travel to Abu Simble, visit the Temple of Ramesses the great which is carved in the mountain; a true miracle of<br>ancient and modern engineering that deserves to be counted among the wonders of the world. back to Aswan</p>'),
(1278, 258, 'en', 'Day 10 Back to Cairo', '<p>After breakfast, we will check out from our cruise to catch our flight back to Cairo.<br>Arrive to Cairo.<br>Check in at the hotel<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(1279, 259, 'en', 'Day 11: Private Opening of The Great Pyramid of Giza & Aromatherapy experience', '<p>After breakfast, you will experience an exclusive special private<br>opening of the Great Pyramid of Giza, the only surviving wonder of<br>the ancient world.<br>Next, we will visit a well-known perfumery.<br>Here, drawing on the knowledge of his ancestors, we will<br>be guided through this subject by a certified<br>aromatherapist. Known as \"Healer from the Heart\", he will present a<br>detailed explanation about the physical and psychological uses of<br>the organic essential oils of Egypt. Historically, the beneficial<br>effects of their use has been documented in various papyri of the<br>Ancients. After our essential oil lesson, we return to our hotel.<br>Egygo Travel would like to invite you to the Farewell Dinner.<br>Overnight in Cairo</p>'),
(1280, 260, 'en', 'Day 12 Departure', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out and be transported to Cairo<br>International Airport by private coach to catch your international<br>flight</p>'),
(1281, 261, 'en', 'ARRIVAL Day 1 FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will<br>assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we<br>will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local<br>surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey.</p>'),
