(1611, 335, 'en', NULL, NULL),
(1612, 336, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p>Embark on a timeless journey with <strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>, where our expert guide will whisk you away from your hotel to the awe-inspiring</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Giza Pyramids Complex</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Giza Pyramids Complex</strong>, is home to three of the most iconic pyramids: the Great Pyramid of Khufu, the Pyramid of Khafre, and the Pyramid of Menkaure. Built during the Fourth Dynasty around 2600 BCE, these pyramids served as monumental tombs for the pharaohs. The complex also includes the Great Sphinx, a massive limestone statue with the body of a lion and the head of a pharaoh.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Great Pyramid</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Great Pyramid</strong>, also known as the Pyramid of Khufu or Cheops, is the largest and oldest of the three pyramids in the Giza Pyramids Complex. Built around 2580-2560 BCE during the Fourth Dynasty, it originally stood at 481 feet tall and was the tallest man-made structure in the world for over 3,800 years. Constructed from millions of limestone blocks, the Great Pyramid was built as a tomb for Pharaoh Khufu. It remains one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World and is a remarkable example of ancient Egyptian engineering and architectural prowess.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The&nbsp;</strong><strong>Great&nbsp;</strong><strong>Sphinx of Chephren</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Great Sphinx</strong>&nbsp;of Chephren, also known as the Great Sphinx of&nbsp;<strong>Giza</strong>, is a monumental limestone statue located near the Giza Pyramids in Egypt. Believed to have been carved during the reign of Pharaoh Khafre (Chephren) around 2500 BCE, the Sphinx features the body of a lion and the head of a pharaoh, likely representing Khafre himself. Measuring about 240 feet in length and 66 feet in height, the Great Sphinx is one of the most iconic&nbsp;<strong>symbols of ancient Egypt</strong>.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Valley Temple</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Valley Temple, is an ancient Egyptian structure dating back to approximately 2500 BCE. Constructed for Pharaoh Khafre, the temple was primarily used for mummification and ceremonial purification. It is renowned for its impressive architecture, featuring massive limestone blocks and granite pillars that showcase the grandeur and precision of ancient Egyptian craftsmanship.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Saqqara Step Pyramid</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Saqqara Step Pyramid</strong>, with its six towering steps reaching towards the heavens, stands at a height of 62 meters and is the earliest large-scale stone construction, built for King Djoser. This remarkable pyramid marks the beginning of the golden era of pyramid construction in ancient Egypt, laying the foundation for the grand monuments that would follow.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Lunch Time</strong></p>\r\n<p>Enjoy a delightful lunch at a local restaurant in Cairo, then continue your&nbsp;<strong>Full Day Tour To Giza Pyramids, Memphis, Sakkara and Dahshur</strong>. With your private guide to visit:</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Memphis City</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>Memphis</strong>&nbsp;City, was Egypt\'s ancient capital founded around 3100 BCE. It served as a major political and cultural hub with notable temples, including the Temple of Ptah. Today, it&rsquo;s an archaeological site with significant&nbsp;<strong>artifacts</strong>, including a colossal statue of Ramses II and the Alabaster Sphinx.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Dahshur Pyramids</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Dahshur Pyramids, south of Cairo, include the&nbsp;<strong>Bent Pyramid</strong>&nbsp;and the Red Pyramid, built by Pharaoh Snefru. The Bent Pyramid is notable for its unique shape, while the Red Pyramid is the first successful smooth-sided pyramid. These pyramids are significant in the evolution of pyramid architecture.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Book with us</strong>&nbsp;for an unparalleled exploration of Egypt\'s ancient wonders, where every step is a story and every monument a memory etched in stone.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>With <strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>, your journey into the heart of history begins.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(1613, 337, 'en', NULL, '<p>Your adventure begins at morning as our expert guide whisks you away from your hotel to the awe-inspiring Step Pyramid of Zoser. Marvel at the world\'s earliest colossal stone monument, erected during the 3rd Dynasty for the venerable King Zoser.</p>\r\n<p>Your odyssey continues to Dahshur, where you\'ll step inside the Red Pyramid, hailed as history\'s inaugural true pyramid. Gaze upon the Bent Pyramid, renowned for its remarkable preservation. These architectural wonders offer a glimpse into the ingenuity of ancient builders.</p>\r\n<p>Next, we transport you to the storied city of Memphis, established by the illustrious King Menes. Once the heart of Egyptian rule and culture, Memphis thrived as the nation\'s capital for over three millennia. Here, we stand in the presence of the colossal Statue of Ramses II and the enigmatic alabaster Sphinx, symbols of a civilization that has captivated the world.</p>\r\n<p>Join us for an unforgettable day as we explore the grandeur of Egypt\'s storied past, bringing history to life with tales of pharaohs and pyramids. This is more than a tour; it\'s a passage through time, where every moment is a treasure waiting to be discovered. Take advantage of this opportunity to witness the most incredible ancient sites near Cairo in a single day. Secure your spot on this epic voyage into history with <strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(1614, 338, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p>We will pick you up from your hotel in Cairo, where you&rsquo;ll meet your private tour guide. Together, in a comfortable air-conditioned vehicle, you\'ll embark on your&nbsp;<strong>Egyptian Museum, Citadel And Khan Khalili Bazaar tour</strong>, beginning with a visit to:</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Egyptian Museum</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Egyptian Museum</strong>&nbsp;in Cairo houses one of the world&rsquo;s largest collections of ancient&nbsp;<strong>Egyptian artifacts</strong>. Established in 1902, it showcases over 120,000 items, including statues, jewelry, and mummies.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Citadel of Salah El Din</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Citadel of Salah El Din, is a historic fortress built in the 12th century by Salah El Din (Saladin) to defend against Crusaders. The citadel served as Egypt&rsquo;s seat of government for over 700 years. It houses several important buildings, including the impressive Mohamed Ali Mosque. The Citadel offers stunning views of Cairo and is a significant symbol of Egypt\'s medieval history.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Mohamed Ali Mosque</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Mohamed Ali Mosque, Built between 1830 and 1848 by Mohamed Ali Pasha, the mosque is named for its extensive use of alabaster in its interior and exterior. It features a large central dome, two towering minarets, and intricate Ottoman-style architecture.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Khan El Khalili Bazaar</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>Khan El Khalili Bazaar</strong>, located in the heart of Islamic&nbsp;<strong>Cairo</strong>, is one of the city&rsquo;s oldest and most famous markets. Dating back to the 14th century, this bustling bazaar is filled with narrow alleys lined with shops selling everything from spices, jewelry, and textiles to traditional crafts and souvenirs. Visitors can also enjoy authentic Egyptian food at local cafes.</p>\r\n<p>As your day of exploration concludes, we&rsquo;ll ensure your safe return to your hotel. With&nbsp;<strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>&nbsp;every journey is a doorway into the heart of Egypt&rsquo;s vibrant history and culture.&nbsp;<strong>Join us</strong> for an experience that will leave you with memories to cherish!</p>'),
(1615, 339, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p>You&rsquo;ll be picked up from your hotel in Cairo or Giza in an air-conditioned vehicle</p>\r\n<p>Enjoy the National Museum of Egyptian Civilization. Located in Old Cairo, the museum showcases 50,000 artifacts and will tell you the story of Egyptian heritage and culture.</p>\r\n<p>Next, head to the Saladin Citadel, built in 1183. This huge structure&nbsp;protected Cairo from several enemy attacks. Admire the beautiful city views of Cairo and the desert from the citadel. Listen to interesting stories about its construction and history from your guide.</p>\r\n<p>The next stop is the Khan El-Khalili Bazaar, one of the oldest&nbsp;markets in the Middle East. Explore the countless lanes and old-fashioned shops selling antiques, souvenirs, perfumes, spices, and jewelry. Then, it&rsquo;s time to</p>\r\n<p>Enjoy an authentic lunch at a local restaurant.</p>\r\n<p>After a memorable day discovering the city, you will be dropped off at your selected location or hotel in Cairo or Giza.</p>'),
(1616, 340, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p><strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours representative will pick you up from your hotel</strong></p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Egyptian Museum</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Egyptian Museum, right in the heart of&nbsp;<strong>Cairo</strong>, has been showcasing Egypt\'s most important artifacts since it opened in 1901. It\'s like stepping into a time machine that takes you through thousands of years of history, with treasures that tell the story of ancient Egypt like no other place.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Salah El Din Citadel</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Salah El Din Citadel in Cairo, built in the 12th century by Saladin, offers stunning city views and a deep dive into Egypt\'s history. Highlights include the grand Mosque of Muhammad Ali and the Egyptian Military Museum. Exploring its ancient walls feels like stepping into a different era.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Mohamed Ali Mosque</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Mohamed Ali Mosque</strong>, also known as the Alabaster Mosque, is a highlight of Cairo\'s Salah El Din Citadel. Built in the 19th century, its grand domes and elegant design are truly awe-inspiring. Step inside to admire the intricate details and experience a key piece of Egypt\'s rich architectural heritage.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Lunch Time</strong></p>\r\n<p>Lunch will be served at a local restaurant in Cairo then join your tour guide to visit:</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Hanging Church</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Hanging Church</strong>&nbsp;in Cairo, one of the city\'s oldest and most famous Coptic Christian churches, is a true gem. Perched above a gatehouse of the ancient Roman fortress, this 3rd-century church seems to float in the air. Inside, you\'ll find stunning icons, intricate woodwork, and a serene atmosphere that\'s perfect for a moment of reflection.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Ben Ezra Synagogue</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Ben Ezra Synagogue</strong>&nbsp;in Cairo is a fascinating historical site. Originally built in the 9th century, it\'s the oldest Jewish temple in the city. Legend has it that this is where baby Moses was found. Inside, you\'ll find beautiful architecture and rich history that highlight Egypt\'s diverse cultural tapestry.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Church of St. Barbara</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Church of St. Barbara in Cairo is a hidden gem among the city\'s historic sites. Dating back to the 4th century, it\'s one of the oldest Coptic churches. Known for its beautiful icons and intricate woodwork, this church offers a peaceful retreat and a glimpse into Egypt\'s rich Christian heritage.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Abu Serga Church</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Abu Serga Church</strong>&nbsp;in Cairo is a remarkable testament to Egypt\'s early Christian history. Dating back to the 4th century, it is believed to be built upon the site where the Holy Family rested during their journey into Egypt. The church\'s ancient architecture and vibrant Coptic artwork make it a must-visit for anyone interested in Egypt\'s religious heritage.</p>\r\n<p>Finally, we will transfer you in one of our private A.C vehicles back to your hotel in Cairo-Giza to end your day tour to Egyptian Museum, Citadel And Old Cairo, Coptic sites.</p>'),
(1617, 341, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Embark on a captivating journey through time with Sun Pyramids Tours as we present our exclusive half-day tour to Islamic Cairo. Our representative, equipped with a modern air-conditioned vehicle, will escort you from your hotel in Cairo to the historic Citadel of Cairo, a fortification from the medieval Islamic era. \\n\\nThis architectural marvel was constructed by Salah ad-Din (Saladin) and has been meticulously preserved and enhanced by successive Egyptian rulers.\\n\\nThe Citadel is home to the renowned Mohamed Ali\'s Mosque, also known as the Alabaster Mosque, a must-visit destination in Cairo. Immerse yourself in the spiritual ambiance and marvel at the intricate designs that adorn this sacred place of worship.\\n\\nOur journey continues to the Mosque and Madrasa of Sultan Hassan, a testament to the resilience of the human spirit. Despite the Black Plague that ravaged Cairo in the mid-14th century, this mosque\'s construction began in 1356 CE and stands today as a symbol of perseverance.\\n\\nNext, we visit the Mosque of Al-Refai, a gem of early Mamluk architecture. Constructed between 1356 and 1363 during the Bahri Mamluk period, this mosque is celebrated for its grandeur and innovative architectural elements. It remains one of Cairo\'s most awe-inspiring historic monuments.\\n\\nAs our enriching tour concludes, we ensure a comfortable transfer back to your hotel. With Sun Pyramids Tours, experience the magic of Islamic Cairo, where history comes alive. Join us and create memories that will last a lifetime.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:9153,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;9&quot;:1,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Embark on a captivating journey through time with Pharaoh Vibes Tours as we present our exclusive half-day tour to Islamic Cairo. Our representative, equipped with a modern air-conditioned vehicle, will escort you from your hotel in Cairo to the historic Citadel of Cairo, a fortification from the medieval Islamic era.<br><br>This architectural marvel was constructed by Salah ad-Din (Saladin) and has been meticulously preserved and enhanced by successive Egyptian rulers.<br><br>The Citadel is home to the renowned Mohamed Ali\'s Mosque, also known as the Alabaster Mosque, a must-visit destination in Cairo. Immerse yourself in the spiritual ambiance and marvel at the intricate designs that adorn this sacred place of worship.<br><br>Our journey continues to the Mosque and Madrasa of Sultan Hassan, a testament to the resilience of the human spirit. Despite the Black Plague that ravaged Cairo in the mid-14th century, this mosque\'s construction began in 1356 CE and stands today as a symbol of perseverance.<br><br>Next, we visit the Mosque of Al-Refai, a gem of early Mamluk architecture. Constructed between 1356 and 1363 during the Bahri Mamluk period, this mosque is celebrated for its grandeur and innovative architectural elements. It remains one of Cairo\'s most awe-inspiring historic monuments.<br><br>As our enriching tour concludes, we ensure a comfortable transfer back to your hotel. With Pharaoh Vibes Tours, experience the magic of Islamic Cairo, where history comes alive. Join us and create memories that will last a lifetime.</span></p>\r\n<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Embark on a captivating journey through time with Sun Pyramids Tours as we present our exclusive half-day tour to Islamic Cairo. Our representative, equipped with a modern air-conditioned vehicle, will escort you from your hotel in Cairo to the historic Citadel of Cairo, a fortification from the medieval Islamic era. \\n\\nThis architectural marvel was constructed by Salah ad-Din (Saladin) and has been meticulously preserved and enhanced by successive Egyptian rulers.\\n\\nThe Citadel is home to the renowned Mohamed Ali\'s Mosque, also known as the Alabaster Mosque, a must-visit destination in Cairo. Immerse yourself in the spiritual ambiance and marvel at the intricate designs that adorn this sacred place of worship.\\n\\nOur journey continues to the Mosque and Madrasa of Sultan Hassan, a testament to the resilience of the human spirit. Despite the Black Plague that ravaged Cairo in the mid-14th century, this mosque\'s construction began in 1356 CE and stands today as a symbol of perseverance.\\n\\nNext, we visit the Mosque of Al-Refai, a gem of early Mamluk architecture. Constructed between 1356 and 1363 during the Bahri Mamluk period, this mosque is celebrated for its grandeur and innovative architectural elements. It remains one of Cairo\'s most awe-inspiring historic monuments.\\n\\nAs our enriching tour concludes, we ensure a comfortable transfer back to your hotel. With Sun Pyramids Tours, experience the magic of Islamic Cairo, where history comes alive. Join us and create memories that will last a lifetime.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:9153,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;9&quot;:1,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;16&quot;:12}\"><strong>Note :</strong>&nbsp;For pick up / drop off form Cairo airport, Sphinx airport, New Administrative Capital, New Cairo, Helioplis, Badr City, Shorouk, Rehab, Obour, Sheraton Almatar, Sheikh Zayed city or Madinty City will be for additional cost</span></p>'),
(1618, 342, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Pharaoh Vibes Tours guide will pick up you from your Hotel to visit&nbsp;<strong>Old Cairo</strong>&nbsp;that known as&nbsp;<strong>Christian Coptic Cairo</strong>&nbsp;which is Among the most important locations visited by the Holy Family where the spiritual impact of their presence is most felt still; though their stay was brief, for the Governor of what was then Fustat enraged by the tumbling down of idols at Jesus&rsquo; approach sought to kill the Child. But they took shelter from his wrath in a cave above which, in later years, the Church of Abu Serga (St Sergious) was built. This, and the whole area of the Fort of Babylon, is a destination of pilgrimage not only for the Egyptians but for Christians from around the world. An air of piety and devotion pervades the whole district there. Also There you will be able to visit and Enter the Church of Abu-Sergah and St. Barbara, the&nbsp;<strong>hanging church.</strong></p>\r\n<p>Visit The Famous Cave Church of St. Simon in Cairo There are seven cave churches carved into the nearby Moqattam Mountain. The Monastery of St. Simon the Tanner is the largest and has an amphitheater with a seating capacity of 20,000. It is worth a visit if you are interesting to see something different in Egypt. after that return back to your Hotel.</p>'),
(1619, 343, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p data-start=\"106\" data-end=\"667\">Your evening begins with a pickup from your hotel before heading to the iconic Cairo Tower, where you&rsquo;ll enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of the city illuminated at night. Next, stroll through the lively lanes of Khan El Khalili Bazaar, soaking in the vibrant atmosphere and browsing its countless treasures. The experience continues with your choice of either a serene felucca ride on the Nile under the stars or a romantic horse-drawn carriage ride through the city&rsquo;s charming streets. At the end of the tour, you&rsquo;ll be comfortably returned to your hotel.</p>'),
(1620, 344, 'en', 'Day 1 : Nile Cruise', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 21.0pt; background: white;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #333333; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">Arrival to Luxor <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>and transfer to visit The Temple of Karnak &amp; the Temple of Luxor. Excursion to the Luxor Temple to see its courtyard and the granite statues of Ramses the Great. Proceed to Karnak. Transfer to the Nile Cruise. Boarding . Lunch on board. Overnight in Luxor.</span></p>'),
(1621, 345, 'en', 'Day 2: Nile Cruise', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 21.0pt; background: white;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #333333; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">Breakfast. Visit The West Bank &ndash; the Valley of the Kings, Colossi of Memnon and The Temple of Rey <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>Ramses III <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>at Medinet Habu.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 21.0pt; background: white;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #333333; background: yellow; mso-highlight: yellow; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">(Optional)</span><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #333333; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\"> Hot Air Balloon: Should you want to make your stay in Luxor an unforgettable. Drifting peacefully over the Valley of King, Valley of the Queens and the Mountain on the Nobles.<br>The flight is approximately 30:40 minutes depend on the weather&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #001d38; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: ES; mso-bidi-language: ES;\"><!--[endif]--></span></p>'),
(1622, 346, 'en', 'Day 3 Nile Cruise', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 21.0pt; background: white;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #333333; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">Breakfast on board. Visit the Temple of Horus in Edfu. Lunch on board. Visit the Temple shared by the two Gods Sobek &amp; Haroeris in Kom Ombo. Afternoon Tea. Overnight in Kom Ombo.</span></p>'),
(1623, 347, 'en', 'Day 4 Nile Cruise', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 21.0pt; background: white;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #333333; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">Breakfast on board. Sail to Aswan. Visit <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>the Temple of Philae Lunch on board. </span></p>'),
(1624, 348, 'en', 'Day 5 Aswan', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 21.0pt; background: white;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #333333; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">Breakfast on board. Disembarkation. <span style=\"background: yellow; mso-highlight: yellow;\">(</span></span><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Calibri\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #333333; background: yellow; mso-highlight: yellow; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">optional</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #333333; background: yellow; mso-highlight: yellow; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">)</span><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: #333333; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\"> Abu Simbel Trip.<br>Departure to visit the Temple of Abu Simbel, The colossal Temple of Abu Simbel built by Ramses II (XIXth. Dynasty) and lately saved from inundation of the Nile waters in among the glories of ancient Egyptian monuments. The temples were built out of a sandstone rock cliff, and representation of the deities to which each was dedicated is carved on its huge fa&ccedil;ade. Nearby, also saved, lies the small Temple of the King\'s wife Nefertari, dedicated to the goddess Hathor. Back to Aswan.<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Transfer out.</span></p>'),
(1625, 349, 'en', 'Day 1: Aswan', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">We\'ll pick you up on the first day at Aswan airport, the train station, your hotel, or whichever point you would like. Then we\'ll take you to the cruise boat,&nbsp;where your full room and board is waiting for you.&nbsp;We\'ll visit the&nbsp;Temple of Philae&nbsp;</span></p>'),
(1626, 350, 'en', 'Day 2: Aswan – Kom Ombo – Edfu', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">After breakfast, anyone who wants to can take an&nbsp;optional&nbsp;excursion to the temples of Abu simbel which comes highly recommended.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">Then, back on the boat, we\'ll eat and begin to&nbsp;sail along the Nile, arriving at the&nbsp;Kom Ombo Temple at sunset, one of the images of Egypt which will stay with you for life. Then having visited the temple, we\'ll continue sailing towards&nbsp;Edfu, where we\'ll drop anchor to eat dinner and spend the night.</span></p>'),
(1627, 351, 'en', 'Day 3: Edfu – Esna – Luxor', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">Once we\'ve eaten and with batteries fully charged, we\'ll visit the Edfu Temple, dedicated to the God Horus. The cruise will then continue on its way towards Esna, where we\'ll&nbsp;cross the famous floodgate.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">Having arrived at the majestic city of&nbsp;Luxor&nbsp;we\'ll visit two of the most spectacular temples in the country, the&nbsp;Luxor and Karnak temples. These temples were&nbsp;separated in antiquity by the 3-kilometre-long&nbsp;Avenue of the Sphinxes. Here we\'ll eat and spend the night anchored in Luxor.</span></p>'),
(1628, 352, 'en', 'Day 4: Luxor', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">Having eaten and checked out, around 6 am we\'ll hit the road towards the giant necropoles nearby. We\'ll visit the Valley of the Kings (taking a look inside three of the tombs) the&nbsp;Hatshepsut Temple&nbsp;(dedicated to the only woman to rule over Egypt for an extended period of time) and the&nbsp;Colossi of Memnon. The tour then finishes at around 1:30 pm, then we\'ll take you to the Luxor airport, the train station, or whichever point in the city you would like.</span></p>'),
(1629, 353, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"tab-stops: 12.75pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: \'Calibri\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #344054; background: white; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">In the first stage of your day tour, you will be picked up from your hotel. Dendera Temple Enjoy a masterclass in ancient Egyptian religion from your own Egyptologist tour guide at Dendera Temple. The construction was dedicated to the Goddess Hathor and was built in the late Ptolemaic Dynasty by Cleopatra VII &amp; Ptolemy XII. The complex was very known among travelers and pilgrims, who have come to seek healing from the goddess as shown by the sanatorium in the temple complex.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"tab-stops: 12.75pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: \'Calibri\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #344054; background: white; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">The temple is visually stunning with its grand entrance, detailed carvings, hieroglyphs, and decorated ceilings. After finishing your tour inside the previous site, you&rsquo;ll be heading to the holy Abydos Temple.&nbsp; Abydos Temple Abydos Temple is one of the most impressive religious structures in Egypt, as ancient Egyptians believed the lord of the underworld Osiris was buried there. Take some memorable photoshoots with the memorial temple of Seti I, which holds enchanting descriptions from the 19th Dynasty, <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>known as the Abydos King List.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"tab-stops: 12.75pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: \'Calibri\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #344054; background: white; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>The said list is a chronological one containing a cartouche of most dynastic pharaohs of Egypt from Menes until Ramesses I, Seti\'s father. Seti I constructed the temple to hold small chapels dedicated to each side of the major gods, such as Ptah, Amun-Ra, Isis, Osiris, Horus, and others. You&rsquo;ll then enjoy your delicious lunch at Abydos Temple, then you will drive back safely to hotel.</span></p>'),
(1630, 354, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>We will take you to the Sacred Valley of the Kings, where you will visit its most famous tombs. Then you will head to the great Temple of Hatshepsut, one of the greatest ancient architectures ever built. Its three massive terraces rise above the desert floor and into the cliffs of&nbsp;Deir El-Bahari. Images presented on the walls are of offerings and cult activity, with a painting showing Anubis escorting Hatshepsut to the shrine, and many more historic stories for you to discover. Then you will go to the famous Colossi of Memnon, and the great temple of Habu.</p>\r\n<p>A complimentary visit to the Alabaster Factory will be arranged for you, free of charge, so you can shop for the best Souvenirs to take back home.</p>\r\n<p>Guided by our professional Egyptologists, you will enjoy listening to the Story behind these ancient wonders and have all your inquiries answered with full attention.</p>'),
(1631, 355, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Start your marvelous day on&nbsp;Luxor East Bank Tour,&nbsp;the&nbsp;Early morning, you will be accompanied by your Egyptologist tour&nbsp;guide to visit the East Bank of&nbsp;the Nile River, You will start&nbsp;Luxor excursions&nbsp;with&nbsp;Karnak Temple, which&nbsp;is an immense temple that is considered as the most ancient worship place in the whole country of Egypt. it is considered as the greatest example of greatness in the history of the&nbsp;New Kingdom&nbsp;in ancient Egypt.</p>\r\n<p>The temple was dedicated to the triad of the sun&nbsp;God&nbsp;Amon Re, his wife&nbsp;Mut, the cat Goddess, and their son Khonsu. It was constructed from the beginning of the&nbsp;Middle Kingdom&nbsp;to the&nbsp;Greco-Roman&nbsp;epoch&nbsp;by many Kings and Pharaohs.</p>\r\n<p>Then continue your&nbsp;Luxor East Bank Tours&nbsp;as you will move to wander the&nbsp;Luxor Temple, there are chapels to the back of the temple established by King Amenhotep III who ruled Egypt during the 18th Dynasty, and Alexander The Great, the Macedonian-origin king who founded the city of Alexandria in 332 B.C. Other parts of the temple were really built by Tutankhamun and Ramses II.</p>'),
(1632, 356, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>In the morning, an air-conditioned coach will pick you up at your hotel in Aswan.&nbsp;Accompanied by a guide, you will be taken to the&nbsp;Kom Ombo Temple&nbsp;, located on the Nile about 50 km north of Aswan.</p>\r\n<p>Built in the Greco-Roman era, Kom Ombo is home to an unusual double temple. The temple on the right is dedicated to the crocodile god, Sobek, while the temple on the left was in honor of Haroeris. Each temple has its own entrance, courtyard, halls and shrine. The temple is supposed to change color after the sunset.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Further on, go to the&nbsp;Temple of Edfu&nbsp;built in sandstone during the Ptolemaic period.&nbsp;The temple is dedicated to the falcon god, Horus.&nbsp;It is the best preserved temple in Egypt and beautifully constructed, offering wonderful use of natural sunlight.&nbsp;The temple contains a nilometer, windows and wells, including a variety of battle and religious inscriptions on the walls.&nbsp;Two statues of hawks are located at the entrance of the temple.&nbsp;The interior includes a library, a cloakroom, a laboratory, a treasure room, a hall, a sanctuary and other rooms.</p>\r\n<p>After exploring the temple sites, you will return to your hotel in Aswan.</p>');
INSERT INTO `tour_day_translations` (`id`, `tour_day_id`, `locale`, `title`, `description`) VALUES
(1633, 357, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>In&nbsp;Abu Simbel, there exists one of the most famous ancient Egyptian monuments.&nbsp; The temple of Ramses II with his four massive Colossi adorning the entrance of the temple. The temple was marked as a convey of Egyptian supremacy for whoever intended to approach Egypt from the south. To the north of the temple is the smaller temple of Hathor, which was built in honor of Ramses&rsquo; wife Nefertari. Both these temples are the best-known archeological sites of Egypt. The huge sandstone statues carved into the temple facades and the decorated interiors with art and hieroglyphics should not be missed.</p>\r\n<p>The Abu Simbel Temples were originally carved into solid rock cliffs, but UNESCO relocated the temples in the 1960s after the building of the Aswan High Dam to save them from inundation. They are now present near the banks of Lake Nasser. Our Abu Simbel tour begins from the city of Aswan, after your tour to Abu Simbel, you will return to your hotel.</p>\r\n<p>with daily departures about 5:00 am. Transfer to Abu Simbel which is approximately three and half hours from Aswan.&nbsp;</p>'),
(1634, 358, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Aswan excursion and Day Tour to visit main highlights of the city to visit the unfinished Oblisk, Philae temple and High Dam. Then proceed Shallal to take a motor boat and visit the&nbsp;Philae temple&nbsp;devoted to God Isis. After the building of the&nbsp;High Dam the temple was dismantled and reconstructed in its present location in Agilika Island. You will end your tour by visiting the High Dam which was constructed to save Egypt from the Nile River flooding.</p>\r\n<p>You will be taken along the road past the Fatimid Cemetery to the&nbsp;Unfinished Obelisk which is a curious sight where a huge obelisk is perfectly shaped on three sides but the fourth side is still attached to the rock bed. It was abandoned after a flaw was discovered on the rock.</p>\r\n<p>Philae Temple, originally located on Philae Island, is&nbsp;a complex of ancient Egyptian temples dedicated to the goddess Isis and other deities.&nbsp;Due to flooding from the Aswan High Dam, the temple complex was relocated to Agilkia Island.&nbsp;It\'s known for its well-preserved structures, including the Temple of Isis, the&nbsp;Kiosk of Trajan,&nbsp;and the&nbsp;Temple of Hathor.&nbsp;</p>'),
(1635, 359, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Pharaoh Vibes Tours representative will pick you up from your hotel in Cairo, and then transfer to enjoy amazing day trip to Alexandria.</p>\r\n<p>First visit&nbsp;Pompay\'s Pillar. It was constructed in honor of the Emperor Diocletian at the end of the 4th century. Originally from the temple of the Serapis, it was once a magnificent structure rivaling the Soma and the Caesarean.</p>\r\n<p>Then you drive to visit the&nbsp;Catacombs which are the largest Roman Cemetery consisting of three levels cut in the rock.</p>\r\n<p>Lunch at local restaurant in Alexandria, then proceed to see the&nbsp;Qaitbay Citadel which was built on the site of the ancient pharaohs (lighthouse) of Alexandria then to Bibliotheca Alexandrina. Finally you will drive back to your hotel in Cairo.</p>\r\n<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Note: Alexandria library is closed on Friday so you can visit the roman&nbsp;theater&nbsp;instead&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:15357,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:4408131},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Note:</span></p>\r\n<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Note: Alexandria library is closed on Friday so you can visit the roman&nbsp;theater&nbsp;instead&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:15357,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:4408131},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Alexandria library is closed on Friday so you can visit the roman theater instead</span></p>'),
(1636, 360, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>It is a fabulous way to enjoy a night on the Nile while you are in Cairo. So, you are invited to dinner on the Nile cruising restaurant for two hours sailing trip on the Nile with belly dancer, folklore show, Oriental music and dinner. All the time, you&rsquo;ll be delighted in our Chef&rsquo;s menu along with a selection of Egyptian favorites, made with the freshest ingredients, and prepared to make it a memorable dining experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>'),
(1637, 361, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Pharaoh Vibes Tours representative will pick you up from your hotel in Cairo to enjoy El Fayoum famous sites. From Cairo to Fayoum is about 95 km. Today all our visits are in Wadi El Ryan, designated as Protected Area in 1989.</p>\r\n<p>We will start our tour to Wadi Hitan Protected Area (Valley of the Whales), about 90 km far from Fayoum. Wadi Hitan or Valley of the Whales is located in the Protected Area of Wadi El Rayan and it was designated by UNISCO as a world Heritage Site in recognition of the 40 million year &ndash;old whale skeletons found there.</p>\r\n<p>On the way to Wadi El Rayan Water Falls, visit Mudawara Mountain. Then onto Wadi Al Ryan Water Falls. Wadi El Rayan is a natural depression located in the western desert, 42m below sea level. Wadi Rayan consists of two lakes connected by Egypt&rsquo;s only waterfalls, formed in 1970 by an overflow of drainage water from the farmlands in Fayoum.</p>\r\n<p>Enjoy sandboarding in Fayom Late Lunch will be served at a good quality restaurant. After that transfer back to Cairo.</p>'),
(1638, 362, 'en', 'Day 1 : Cairo-Siwa', '<p>Ready for Adventure!!! Early morning departure to Siwa Oasis our private limousine to Siwa oasis , The largest (23,000 habitants) &amp; most remote Egyptian Oasis lying some 17m below sea level. Crossing the Western Desert with a stop in AL alamin 2 world War museum then move to Marsa Matrouh on the Mediterranean Sea for lunch break in one from the local restaurants there after lunch move to Siwa oasis arrive afternoon and overnight in hotel.</p>\r\n<p>Meals: Lunch, Dinner&nbsp;</p>'),
(1639, 362, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1640, 362, 'de', NULL, NULL),
