(1777, 382, 'en', 'Day 3 : Siwa – Bahariya', '<p>After Breakfast, crossing the Western Desert, Then move with our AC private car driving around 10 hours towards Bahariya oasis.</p>\r\n<p>Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner</p>'),
(1778, 382, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1779, 382, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1780, 382, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1781, 382, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1782, 382, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1783, 382, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1784, 383, 'en', 'Day 4 : White Desert', '<div class=\"p-4 bg-[#eeeeee] flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"pt-4 mx-5 pb-6 text-[#666666]\">\r\n<div class=\"mt-\">\r\n<p>Start your adventure visiting white desert national park, we start by the black desert then el hez village and the cold spring ( lunch on the way ) then we drive to visit the crystal mountain and we continue driving to Agapat area, after that we arrive the old white desert ( mushrooms area &amp; tents area ),</p>\r\n<p>Then we visit the new white desert with all the lovely limestone formations when we finish our visit we find a nice place to make our camp for dinner and spending the night under the stars.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(1785, 383, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1786, 383, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1787, 383, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1788, 383, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1789, 383, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1790, 383, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1791, 384, 'en', 'Day 5 : Bahariya Oasis / Cairo', '<div class=\"p-4 bg-[#eeeeee] flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"pt-4 mx-5 pb-6 text-[#666666]\">\r\n<div class=\"mt-\">\r\n<p>After having our breakfast in our camp and when we are ready we drive back with our jeep to the oasis where we will find our car ready to drive us back to Cairo.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Meals: Breakfast</p>\r\n<p><strong>Note</strong>:</p>\r\n<p>If the mentioned cruise or the hotel are not available, the company has the right to change to any cruise or hotel, as long as it is of same category.</p>\r\n<p>That the order of the days could be change according to cruise sailing dates keeping the sightseeing you will visit as it is.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(1792, 384, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1793, 384, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1794, 384, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1795, 384, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1796, 384, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1797, 384, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1798, 385, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Start your marvelous day on&nbsp;Luxor East Bank Tour,&nbsp;the&nbsp;Early morning, you will be accompanied by your Egyptologist tour&nbsp;guide to visit the East Bank of&nbsp;the Nile River, You will start&nbsp;Luxor excursions&nbsp;with&nbsp;Karnak Temple, which&nbsp;is an immense temple that is considered as the most ancient worship place in the whole country of Egypt. it is considered as the greatest example of greatness in the history of the&nbsp;New Kingdom&nbsp;in ancient Egypt.</p>\r\n<p>The temple was dedicated to the triad of the sun&nbsp;God&nbsp;Amon Re, his wife&nbsp;Mut, the cat Goddess, and their son Khonsu. It was constructed from the beginning of the&nbsp;Middle Kingdom&nbsp;to the&nbsp;Greco-Roman&nbsp;epoch&nbsp;by many Kings and Pharaohs.</p>\r\n<p>Then continue your&nbsp;Luxor East Bank Tours&nbsp;as you will move to wander the&nbsp;Luxor Temple, there are chapels to the back of the temple established by King Amenhotep III who ruled Egypt during the 18th Dynasty, and Alexander The Great, the Macedonian-origin king who founded the city of Alexandria in 332 B.C. Other parts of the temple were really built by Tutankhamun and Ramses II.</p>'),
(1799, 385, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1800, 385, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1801, 385, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1802, 385, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1803, 385, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1804, 385, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1805, 386, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>We will take you to the Sacred Valley of the Kings, where you will visit its most famous tombs. Then you will head to the great Temple of Hatshepsut, one of the greatest ancient architectures ever built. Its three massive terraces rise above the desert floor and into the cliffs of&nbsp;Deir El-Bahari. Images presented on the walls are of offerings and cult activity, with a painting showing Anubis escorting Hatshepsut to the shrine, and many more historic stories for you to discover. Then you will go to the famous Colossi of Memnon, and the great temple of Habu.</p>\r\n<p>A complimentary visit to the Alabaster Factory will be arranged for you, free of charge, so you can shop for the best Souvenirs to take back home.</p>\r\n<p>Guided by our professional Egyptologists, you will enjoy listening to the Story behind these ancient wonders and have all your inquiries answered with full attention.</p>'),
(1806, 386, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1807, 386, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1808, 386, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1809, 386, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1810, 386, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1811, 386, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1812, 387, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"tab-stops: 12.75pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: \'Calibri\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #344054; background: white; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">In the first stage of your day tour, you will be picked up from your hotel. Dendera Temple Enjoy a masterclass in ancient Egyptian religion from your own Egyptologist tour guide at Dendera Temple. The construction was dedicated to the Goddess Hathor and was built in the late Ptolemaic Dynasty by Cleopatra VII &amp; Ptolemy XII. The complex was very known among travelers and pilgrims, who have come to seek healing from the goddess as shown by the sanatorium in the temple complex.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"tab-stops: 12.75pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: \'Calibri\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #344054; background: white; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\">The temple is visually stunning with its grand entrance, detailed carvings, hieroglyphs, and decorated ceilings. After finishing your tour inside the previous site, you&rsquo;ll be heading to the holy Abydos Temple.&nbsp; Abydos Temple Abydos Temple is one of the most impressive religious structures in Egypt, as ancient Egyptians believed the lord of the underworld Osiris was buried there. Take some memorable photoshoots with the memorial temple of Seti I, which holds enchanting descriptions from the 19th Dynasty, <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>known as the Abydos King List.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"tab-stops: 12.75pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: \'Calibri\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #344054; background: white; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>The said list is a chronological one containing a cartouche of most dynastic pharaohs of Egypt from Menes until Ramesses I, Seti\'s father. Seti I constructed the temple to hold small chapels dedicated to each side of the major gods, such as Ptah, Amun-Ra, Isis, Osiris, Horus, and others. You&rsquo;ll then enjoy your delicious lunch at Abydos Temple, then you will drive back safely to hotel.</span></p>'),
(1813, 387, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1814, 387, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1815, 387, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1816, 387, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1817, 387, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1818, 387, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1819, 388, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Your adventure begins at morning as our expert guide whisks you away from your hotel to the awe-inspiring Step Pyramid of Zoser. Marvel at the world\'s earliest colossal stone monument, erected during the 3rd Dynasty for the venerable King Zoser.</p>\r\n<p>Your odyssey continues to Dahshur, where you\'ll step inside the Red Pyramid, hailed as history\'s inaugural true pyramid. Gaze upon the Bent Pyramid, renowned for its remarkable preservation. These architectural wonders offer a glimpse into the ingenuity of ancient builders.</p>\r\n<p>Next, we transport you to the storied city of Memphis, established by the illustrious King Menes. Once the heart of Egyptian rule and culture, Memphis thrived as the nation\'s capital for over three millennia. Here, we stand in the presence of the colossal Statue of Ramses II and the enigmatic alabaster Sphinx, symbols of a civilization that has captivated the world.</p>\r\n<p>Join us for an unforgettable day as we explore the grandeur of Egypt\'s storied past, bringing history to life with tales of pharaohs and pyramids. This is more than a tour; it\'s a passage through time, where every moment is a treasure waiting to be discovered. Take advantage of this opportunity to witness the most incredible ancient sites near Cairo in a single day. Secure your spot on this epic voyage into history with <strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(1820, 388, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1821, 388, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1822, 388, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1823, 388, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1824, 388, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1825, 388, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1826, 389, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p>Embark on a timeless journey with <strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>, where our expert guide will whisk you away from your hotel to the awe-inspiring</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Giza Pyramids Complex</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Giza Pyramids Complex</strong>, is home to three of the most iconic pyramids: the Great Pyramid of Khufu, the Pyramid of Khafre, and the Pyramid of Menkaure. Built during the Fourth Dynasty around 2600 BCE, these pyramids served as monumental tombs for the pharaohs. The complex also includes the Great Sphinx, a massive limestone statue with the body of a lion and the head of a pharaoh.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Great Pyramid</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Great Pyramid</strong>, also known as the Pyramid of Khufu or Cheops, is the largest and oldest of the three pyramids in the Giza Pyramids Complex. Built around 2580-2560 BCE during the Fourth Dynasty, it originally stood at 481 feet tall and was the tallest man-made structure in the world for over 3,800 years. Constructed from millions of limestone blocks, the Great Pyramid was built as a tomb for Pharaoh Khufu. It remains one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World and is a remarkable example of ancient Egyptian engineering and architectural prowess.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The&nbsp;</strong><strong>Great&nbsp;</strong><strong>Sphinx of Chephren</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Great Sphinx</strong>&nbsp;of Chephren, also known as the Great Sphinx of&nbsp;<strong>Giza</strong>, is a monumental limestone statue located near the Giza Pyramids in Egypt. Believed to have been carved during the reign of Pharaoh Khafre (Chephren) around 2500 BCE, the Sphinx features the body of a lion and the head of a pharaoh, likely representing Khafre himself. Measuring about 240 feet in length and 66 feet in height, the Great Sphinx is one of the most iconic&nbsp;<strong>symbols of ancient Egypt</strong>.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Valley Temple</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Valley Temple, is an ancient Egyptian structure dating back to approximately 2500 BCE. Constructed for Pharaoh Khafre, the temple was primarily used for mummification and ceremonial purification. It is renowned for its impressive architecture, featuring massive limestone blocks and granite pillars that showcase the grandeur and precision of ancient Egyptian craftsmanship.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Saqqara Step Pyramid</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Saqqara Step Pyramid</strong>, with its six towering steps reaching towards the heavens, stands at a height of 62 meters and is the earliest large-scale stone construction, built for King Djoser. This remarkable pyramid marks the beginning of the golden era of pyramid construction in ancient Egypt, laying the foundation for the grand monuments that would follow.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Lunch Time</strong></p>\r\n<p>Enjoy a delightful lunch at a local restaurant in Cairo, then continue your&nbsp;<strong>Full Day Tour To Giza Pyramids, Memphis, Sakkara and Dahshur</strong>. With your private guide to visit:</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Memphis City</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>Memphis</strong>&nbsp;City, was Egypt\'s ancient capital founded around 3100 BCE. It served as a major political and cultural hub with notable temples, including the Temple of Ptah. Today, it&rsquo;s an archaeological site with significant&nbsp;<strong>artifacts</strong>, including a colossal statue of Ramses II and the Alabaster Sphinx.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Dahshur Pyramids</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Dahshur Pyramids, south of Cairo, include the&nbsp;<strong>Bent Pyramid</strong>&nbsp;and the Red Pyramid, built by Pharaoh Snefru. The Bent Pyramid is notable for its unique shape, while the Red Pyramid is the first successful smooth-sided pyramid. These pyramids are significant in the evolution of pyramid architecture.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Book with us</strong>&nbsp;for an unparalleled exploration of Egypt\'s ancient wonders, where every step is a story and every monument a memory etched in stone.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>With <strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>, your journey into the heart of history begins.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
