(1973, 410, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>It is a fabulous way to enjoy a night on the Nile while you are in Cairo. So, you are invited to dinner on the Nile cruising restaurant for two hours sailing trip on the Nile with belly dancer, folklore show, Oriental music and dinner. All the time, you&rsquo;ll be delighted in our Chef&rsquo;s menu along with a selection of Egyptian favorites, made with the freshest ingredients, and prepared to make it a memorable dining experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>'),
(1974, 410, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1975, 410, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1976, 410, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1977, 410, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1978, 410, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1979, 410, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1980, 411, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Pharaoh Vibes Tours representative will pick you up from your hotel in Cairo, and then transfer to enjoy amazing day trip to Alexandria.</p>\r\n<p>First visit&nbsp;Pompay\'s Pillar. It was constructed in honor of the Emperor Diocletian at the end of the 4th century. Originally from the temple of the Serapis, it was once a magnificent structure rivaling the Soma and the Caesarean.</p>\r\n<p>Then you drive to visit the&nbsp;Catacombs which are the largest Roman Cemetery consisting of three levels cut in the rock.</p>\r\n<p>Lunch at local restaurant in Alexandria, then proceed to see the&nbsp;Qaitbay Citadel which was built on the site of the ancient pharaohs (lighthouse) of Alexandria then to Bibliotheca Alexandrina. Finally you will drive back to your hotel in Cairo.</p>\r\n<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Note: Alexandria library is closed on Friday so you can visit the roman&nbsp;theater&nbsp;instead&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:15357,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:4408131},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Note:</span></p>\r\n<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Note: Alexandria library is closed on Friday so you can visit the roman&nbsp;theater&nbsp;instead&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:15357,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:4408131},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Alexandria library is closed on Friday so you can visit the roman theater instead</span></p>'),
(1981, 411, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1982, 411, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1983, 411, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1984, 411, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1985, 411, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1986, 411, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1987, 412, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p>We will pick you up from your hotel in Cairo, where you&rsquo;ll meet your private tour guide. Together, in a comfortable air-conditioned vehicle, you\'ll embark on your&nbsp;<strong>Egyptian Museum, Citadel And Khan Khalili Bazaar tour</strong>, beginning with a visit to:</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Egyptian Museum</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Egyptian Museum</strong>&nbsp;in Cairo houses one of the world&rsquo;s largest collections of ancient&nbsp;<strong>Egyptian artifacts</strong>. Established in 1902, it showcases over 120,000 items, including statues, jewelry, and mummies.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Citadel of Salah El Din</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Citadel of Salah El Din, is a historic fortress built in the 12th century by Salah El Din (Saladin) to defend against Crusaders. The citadel served as Egypt&rsquo;s seat of government for over 700 years. It houses several important buildings, including the impressive Mohamed Ali Mosque. The Citadel offers stunning views of Cairo and is a significant symbol of Egypt\'s medieval history.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Mohamed Ali Mosque</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Mohamed Ali Mosque, Built between 1830 and 1848 by Mohamed Ali Pasha, the mosque is named for its extensive use of alabaster in its interior and exterior. It features a large central dome, two towering minarets, and intricate Ottoman-style architecture.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Khan El Khalili Bazaar</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>Khan El Khalili Bazaar</strong>, located in the heart of Islamic&nbsp;<strong>Cairo</strong>, is one of the city&rsquo;s oldest and most famous markets. Dating back to the 14th century, this bustling bazaar is filled with narrow alleys lined with shops selling everything from spices, jewelry, and textiles to traditional crafts and souvenirs. Visitors can also enjoy authentic Egyptian food at local cafes.</p>\r\n<p>As your day of exploration concludes, we&rsquo;ll ensure your safe return to your hotel. With&nbsp;<strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>&nbsp;every journey is a doorway into the heart of Egypt&rsquo;s vibrant history and culture.&nbsp;<strong>Join us</strong> for an experience that will leave you with memories to cherish!</p>'),
(1988, 412, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(1989, 412, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(1990, 412, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(1991, 412, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(1992, 412, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(1993, 412, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(1994, 413, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p><strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>&nbsp;representative will pick you up from your&nbsp;<strong>hotel</strong>, in an air-conditioned vehicle to enjoy an excursion to:</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Grand Egyptian Museum</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM), located near the&nbsp;<strong>Giza Pyramids</strong>, is a state-of-the-art facility showcasing Egypt&rsquo;s rich history. Set to house over 100,000&nbsp;<strong>artifacts</strong>,The museum blends modern design with ancient heritage, offering interactive exhibits, galleries, and educational spaces.</p>\r\n<p>in this tour we get to see :</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Hanging obelisk</li>\r\n<li>King Ramses II statue</li>\r\n<li>10 statues of king Senusert ( Distance view )</li>\r\n<li>Grand staircase ( Distance view )</li>\r\n<li>Ptolemaic king and queen</li>\r\n<li>Victory column of king Merenptah</li>\r\n<li>Royal regalia</li>\r\n<li>Grand atrium &amp; gift shop</li>\r\n<li>Main galleries: Discover Egypt\'s ancient history at&nbsp;<strong>The Grand Egyptian Museum</strong>&rsquo;s Main Galleries, opening on October 16, 2024. With 15,000 artifacts across four sections, explore the rise of early societies, the power of Egypt\'s warrior-kings in the New Kingdom, and the fusion of Egyptian and Greco-Roman cultures in the Ptolemaic era. This remarkable journey through Egypt&rsquo;s dynasties brings the past to life with artifacts reflecting the enduring influence of the gods and beliefs in the afterlife.</li>\r\n<li>After enjoying this tour, you will be dropped off at your hotel by our Modern air- conditioned car</li>\r\n</ul>'),
