(1999, 413, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2000, 413, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2001, 414, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p>Embark on a magical evening with <span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Experience the Giza Pyramids\' grandeur under the stars with Sun Pyramids Tours. Witness history come alive at the Sound &amp; Light Show, where Egypt\'s tales echo through ages. A night of wonder awaits!&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:9153,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;9&quot;:1,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Pharaoh Vibes Tours</span> as we transport you from your hotel to the foot of the majestic Giza Pyramids. There, under the stars, you\'ll witness the Sound and Light Show&mdash;a spectacle that brings the legacy of the Pharaohs to life. The night air will fill with tales of the Sphinx, the eternal sentinel of the necropolis, and the grand saga of the pyramids\' construction will unfold before your eyes.<br><br>As the darkness embraces the desert, the Pyramids of Cheops, Chefren, and Mykerinus will light up, narrating the stories of illustrious rulers like Thutmosis IV, the visionary Akhnaten, the revered Nefertiti, and the legendary Tut Ankh Amon. This immersive experience is not just a show; it\'s a journey through time, where history resonates through the voices of the ancients.<br><br>The Sound and Light Show is more than a visual feast; it\'s an educational odyssey that captures the spirit of Ancient Egypt. As the narrative weaves through the epochs, you\'ll feel the presence of the Sphinx, the age-old guardian whose gaze has surveyed the Giza Necropolis for millennia.<br><br>After the echoes of the past have settled, <span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Experience the Giza Pyramids\' grandeur under the stars with Sun Pyramids Tours. Witness history come alive at the Sound &amp; Light Show, where Egypt\'s tales echo through ages. A night of wonder awaits!&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:9153,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;9&quot;:1,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Pharaoh Vibes Tours</span> will ensure your safe return to the hotel, leaving you with memories that glitter brighter than the constellations above the pyramids. Join us for an evening where history is not just told but spectacularly revealed.</p>'),
(2002, 414, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2003, 414, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2004, 414, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2005, 414, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2006, 414, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2007, 414, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2008, 415, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p><strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>&nbsp;representative will pick you up from your hotel in Cairo or Giza, you&rsquo;ll be taken to the Giza Pyramids. Here, you&rsquo;ll begin an easy ride on a quad bike&mdash;an exhilarating way to explore Egypt&rsquo;s ancient wonders. These custom-built buggies can zip over the sand dunes at speeds of over 50 mph. The thrill of riding through the desert will make your&nbsp;<strong>holiday</strong>&nbsp;in Egypt truly unforgettable. Capture stunning photos and take in the majestic sights of&nbsp;<strong>the Great Pyramid</strong>s: Cheops, Chephren, and Mykerinos.&nbsp; Enjoy the&nbsp;<strong>ATV and Quad bike ride</strong> is an exciting desert trip.</p>'),
(2009, 415, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2010, 415, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2011, 415, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2012, 415, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2013, 415, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2014, 415, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2015, 416, 'en', NULL, NULL),
(2016, 416, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2017, 416, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2018, 416, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2019, 416, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2020, 416, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2021, 416, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2022, 417, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Pharaoh Vibes Tours beckons you to a majestic journey through the beginning of time. Your private tour guide will collect you from your Cairo hotel and set you out to the iconic Giza Plateau.<br><br>Here, the Pyramids of Cheops, Chephren, and Mykerinus rise from the sands, a testament to ancient ambition and ingenuity. Stand in awe at the Great Sphinx, Chephren\'s guardian, whose enigmatic visage has stirred the imaginations of travelers for centuries.<br><br>Your exploration continues at the Valley Temple, a site of profound significance. It was here that the pharaohs\' mummies underwent purification and mummification, rituals as essential to their journey to the afterlife as the pyramids themselves.<br><br>Behold the Seven Wonders of the World, where the 5000-year-old necropolis awaits. The Great Pyramids, a marvel of human achievement, stand as sentinels to history, watched over by the vigilant Sphinx. This is not merely a tour; it is a pilgrimage to the heart of Egypt\'s grandeur, a must-see for every wanderer of the world. With Pharaoh Vibes Tours, the past is not just to be seen, but to be experienced.&nbsp;</p>'),
(2023, 417, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2024, 417, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2025, 417, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2026, 417, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2027, 417, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2028, 417, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2029, 418, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Aswan excursion and Day Tour to visit main highlights of the city to visit the unfinished Oblisk, Philae temple and High Dam. Then proceed Shallal to take a motor boat and visit the&nbsp;Philae temple&nbsp;devoted to God Isis. After the building of the&nbsp;High Dam the temple was dismantled and reconstructed in its present location in Agilika Island. You will end your tour by visiting the High Dam which was constructed to save Egypt from the Nile River flooding.</p>\r\n<p>You will be taken along the road past the Fatimid Cemetery to the&nbsp;Unfinished Obelisk which is a curious sight where a huge obelisk is perfectly shaped on three sides but the fourth side is still attached to the rock bed. It was abandoned after a flaw was discovered on the rock.</p>\r\n<p>Philae Temple, originally located on Philae Island, is&nbsp;a complex of ancient Egyptian temples dedicated to the goddess Isis and other deities.&nbsp;Due to flooding from the Aswan High Dam, the temple complex was relocated to Agilkia Island.&nbsp;It\'s known for its well-preserved structures, including the Temple of Isis, the&nbsp;Kiosk of Trajan,&nbsp;and the&nbsp;Temple of Hathor.&nbsp;</p>'),
(2030, 418, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2031, 418, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2032, 418, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2033, 418, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2034, 418, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2035, 418, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2036, 419, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>In&nbsp;Abu Simbel, there exists one of the most famous ancient Egyptian monuments.&nbsp; The temple of Ramses II with his four massive Colossi adorning the entrance of the temple. The temple was marked as a convey of Egyptian supremacy for whoever intended to approach Egypt from the south. To the north of the temple is the smaller temple of Hathor, which was built in honor of Ramses&rsquo; wife Nefertari. Both these temples are the best-known archeological sites of Egypt. The huge sandstone statues carved into the temple facades and the decorated interiors with art and hieroglyphics should not be missed.</p>\r\n<p>The Abu Simbel Temples were originally carved into solid rock cliffs, but UNESCO relocated the temples in the 1960s after the building of the Aswan High Dam to save them from inundation. They are now present near the banks of Lake Nasser. Our Abu Simbel tour begins from the city of Aswan, after your tour to Abu Simbel, you will return to your hotel.</p>\r\n<p>with daily departures about 5:00 am. Transfer to Abu Simbel which is approximately three and half hours from Aswan.&nbsp;</p>'),
(2037, 419, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2038, 419, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2039, 419, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2040, 419, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2041, 419, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2042, 419, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2043, 420, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>In the morning, an air-conditioned coach will pick you up at your hotel in Aswan.&nbsp;Accompanied by a guide, you will be taken to the&nbsp;Kom Ombo Temple&nbsp;, located on the Nile about 50 km north of Aswan.</p>\r\n<p>Built in the Greco-Roman era, Kom Ombo is home to an unusual double temple. The temple on the right is dedicated to the crocodile god, Sobek, while the temple on the left was in honor of Haroeris. Each temple has its own entrance, courtyard, halls and shrine. The temple is supposed to change color after the sunset.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Further on, go to the&nbsp;Temple of Edfu&nbsp;built in sandstone during the Ptolemaic period.&nbsp;The temple is dedicated to the falcon god, Horus.&nbsp;It is the best preserved temple in Egypt and beautifully constructed, offering wonderful use of natural sunlight.&nbsp;The temple contains a nilometer, windows and wells, including a variety of battle and religious inscriptions on the walls.&nbsp;Two statues of hawks are located at the entrance of the temple.&nbsp;The interior includes a library, a cloakroom, a laboratory, a treasure room, a hall, a sanctuary and other rooms.</p>\r\n<p>After exploring the temple sites, you will return to your hotel in Aswan.</p>'),
(2044, 420, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2045, 420, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2046, 420, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2047, 420, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2048, 420, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2049, 420, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2050, 421, 'en', 'Uncover the Mysteries of Kom Ombo and Edfu', '<p>Awaken to a delicious breakfast on board as we set sail for Kom Ombo. Here, you&rsquo;ll have the chance to explore the unique Temple of Sobek and Haeroris, a testament to the region&rsquo;s ancient religious practices. After a delightful lunch on board, we continue our journey to Edfu. Enjoy a sumptuous dinner on board and rest in the comfort of your cabin in Edfu. Meals : breakfast Lunch &amp; Dinner</p>'),
(2051, 421, 'fr', 'Découvrez les mystères de Kom Ombo et d\'Edfou', '<p>R&eacute;veillez-vous avec un d&eacute;licieux petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord alors que nous embarquons pour Kom Ombo. Ici, vous aurez l&rsquo;occasion d&rsquo;explorer le temple unique de Sobek et Haeroris, t&eacute;moignage des anciennes pratiques religieuses de la r&eacute;gion. Apr&egrave;s un d&eacute;licieux d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord, nous continuons notre voyage vers Edfou. Profitez d\'un somptueux d&icirc;ner &agrave; bord et reposez-vous dans le confort de votre cabine &agrave; Edfou. Repas : petit d&eacute;jeuner D&eacute;jeuner &amp; D&icirc;ner</p>'),
(2052, 421, 'de', 'Entdecken Sie die Geheimnisse von Kom Ombo und Edfu', '<p>Erwachen Sie mit einem k&ouml;stlichen Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord, w&auml;hrend wir nach Kom Ombo segeln. Hier haben Sie die M&ouml;glichkeit, den einzigartigen Tempel von Sobek und Haeroris zu erkunden, ein Zeugnis der alten religi&ouml;sen Praktiken der Region. Nach einem k&ouml;stlichen Mittagessen an Bord setzen wir unsere Reise nach Edfu fort. Genie&szlig;en Sie ein &uuml;ppiges Abendessen an Bord und ruhen Sie sich im Komfort Ihrer Kabine in Edfu aus. Mahlzeiten: Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck, Mittag- und Abendessen</p>'),
(2053, 421, 'it', 'Scopri i misteri di Kom Ombo e Edfu', '<p>Svegliati con una deliziosa colazione a bordo mentre salpiamo per Kom Ombo. Qui avrai la possibilit&agrave; di esplorare l\'esclusivo Tempio di Sobek e Haeroris, una testimonianza delle antiche pratiche religiose della regione. Dopo un delizioso pranzo a bordo, continuiamo il nostro viaggio verso Edfu. Goditi una sontuosa cena a bordo e riposa nel comfort della tua cabina a Edfu. Pasti: colazione, pranzo e cena</p>'),
(2054, 421, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2055, 421, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2056, 421, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2057, 422, 'en', 'Discover the Wonders of Aswan', '<p>Your adventure begins at Aswan Airport/Railway Station, where our team will greet you and escort you to your Nile Cruise aboard the cruise. Settle into your comfortable cabin before lunch, then prepare to immerse yourself in the rich culture of Aswan. Marvel at the engineering feat of the High Dam, explore the enchanting Philae Temple and witness the grandeur of the unfinished obelisk. As the day winds down, savor a delicious dinner on board and rest up for the next day&rsquo;s adventures in your cozy cabin.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Meals : Lunch &amp; Dinner</p>'),
(2058, 422, 'fr', 'Découvrez les merveilles d\'Assouan', '<p>Votre aventure commence &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport/gare d\'Assouan, o&ugrave; notre &eacute;quipe vous accueillera et vous accompagnera jusqu\'&agrave; votre croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil &agrave; bord de la croisi&egrave;re. Installez-vous dans votre cabine confortable avant le d&eacute;jeuner, puis pr&eacute;parez-vous &agrave; vous immerger dans la riche culture d\'Assouan. &Eacute;merveillez-vous devant l\'exploit d\'ing&eacute;nierie du haut barrage, explorez le magnifique temple de Philae et admirez la grandeur de l\'ob&eacute;lisque inachev&eacute;. &Agrave; la fin de la journ&eacute;e, savourez un d&eacute;licieux d&icirc;ner &agrave; bord et reposez-vous pour les aventures du lendemain dans votre cabine confortable.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Repas : D&eacute;jeuner et D&icirc;ner</p>'),
(2059, 422, 'de', 'Entdecken Sie die Wunder von Assuan', '<p>Ihr Abenteuer beginnt am Flughafen/Bahnhof Assuan, wo unser Team Sie begr&uuml;&szlig;t und Sie an Bord der Kreuzfahrt zu Ihrer Nilkreuzfahrt begleitet. Machen Sie es sich vor dem Mittagessen in Ihrer komfortablen Kabine gem&uuml;tlich und bereiten Sie sich darauf vor, in die reiche Kultur Assuans einzutauchen. Bewundern Sie die technische Meisterleistung des High Dam, erkunden Sie den bezaubernden Philae-Tempel und werden Sie Zeuge der Pracht des unvollendeten Obelisken. Lassen Sie den Tag ausklingen, genie&szlig;en Sie ein k&ouml;stliches Abendessen an Bord und ruhen Sie sich in Ihrer gem&uuml;tlichen Kabine f&uuml;r die Abenteuer des n&auml;chsten Tages aus.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Mahlzeiten: Mittag- und Abendessen</p>'),
(2060, 422, 'it', 'Scopri le meraviglie di Assuan', '<p>La tua avventura inizia all\'aeroporto/stazione ferroviaria di Aswan, dove il nostro team ti accoglier&agrave; e ti accompagner&agrave; alla tua crociera sul Nilo a bordo della crociera. Sistemati nella tua comoda cabina prima di pranzo, quindi preparati a immergerti nella ricca cultura di Assuan. Lasciati stupire dall\'impresa ingegneristica dell\'Alta Diga, esplora l\'incantevole Tempio di Philae e assisti alla grandiosit&agrave; dell\'obelisco incompiuto. Mentre la giornata volge al termine, assapora una deliziosa cena a bordo e riposati per le avventure del giorno successivo nella tua accogliente cabina.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Pasti: pranzo e cena</p>'),
(2061, 422, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2062, 422, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2063, 422, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2064, 423, 'en', 'Experience the Magic of Luxor’s East Bank', '<p>Rise early for morning tea and coffee before embarking on an adventure to the Temple of Horus in Edfu. Return to the cruise for a hearty breakfast as we sail towards Luxor via Esna. In Luxor, you&rsquo;ll have the opportunity to visit the awe-inspiring Karnak and Luxor Temples on the East Bank. After an afternoon tea on board, enjoy a delectable dinner and a lively Galabeya Party show. Overnight in Luxor, the city of palaces. Meals : breakfast Lunch &amp; Dinner</p>'),
(2065, 423, 'fr', 'Découvrez la magie de la rive est de Louxor', '<p>Levez-vous t&ocirc;t pour prendre le th&eacute; et le caf&eacute; du matin avant de vous lancer dans une aventure au temple d\'Horus &agrave; Edfou. Retour &agrave; la croisi&egrave;re pour un copieux petit-d&eacute;jeuner alors que nous naviguons vers Louxor via Esna. &Agrave; Louxor, vous aurez l&rsquo;occasion de visiter les impressionnants temples de Karnak et de Louxor sur la rive Est. Apr&egrave;s un th&eacute; l\'apr&egrave;s-midi &agrave; bord, savourez un d&eacute;licieux d&icirc;ner et un spectacle anim&eacute; de Galabeya Party. Nuit &agrave; Louxor, la ville des palais. Repas : petit d&eacute;jeuner D&eacute;jeuner &amp; D&icirc;ner</p>'),
(2066, 423, 'de', 'Erleben Sie den Zauber des Ostufers von Luxor', '<p>Stehen Sie fr&uuml;h auf, um morgens Tee und Kaffee zu trinken, bevor Sie sich auf ein Abenteuer zum Tempel des Horus in Edfu begeben. Kehren Sie f&uuml;r ein herzhaftes Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck zur Kreuzfahrt zur&uuml;ck, w&auml;hrend wir &uuml;ber Esna in Richtung Luxor segeln. In Luxor haben Sie die M&ouml;glichkeit, die beeindruckenden Karnak- und Luxor-Tempel am Ostufer zu besichtigen. Genie&szlig;en Sie nach einem Nachmittagstee an Bord ein k&ouml;stliches Abendessen und eine lebhafte Galabeya-Partyshow. &Uuml;bernachtung in Luxor, der Stadt der Pal&auml;ste. Mahlzeiten: Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck, Mittag- und Abendessen</p>'),
(2067, 423, 'it', 'Vivi la magia della sponda orientale di Luxor', '<p>Alzati presto per prendere il t&egrave; e il caff&egrave; mattutino prima di intraprendere un\'avventura al Tempio di Horus a Edfu. Ritorno alla crociera per un\'abbondante colazione mentre navighiamo verso Luxor via Esna. A Luxor avrai l\'opportunit&agrave; di visitare i maestosi templi di Karnak e Luxor sulla sponda orientale. Dopo un t&egrave; pomeridiano a bordo, goditi una cena deliziosa e un vivace spettacolo del Galabeya Party. Pernottamento a Luxor, la citt&agrave; dei palazzi. Pasti: colazione, pranzo e cena</p>'),
(2068, 423, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2069, 423, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2070, 423, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2071, 424, 'en', 'Farewell and Departure', '<p>Savor your final breakfast on board the cruise as we bid farewell to this unforgettable journey. Disembark after breakfast and continue your exploration of Luxor with a visit to the Valley of the Kings (three tombs only) and the majestic Queen Hatshepsut Temple, known as El-Deir El-Bahari. In the afternoon, our representative will accompany you to Luxor Airport/Railway Station for your onward journey. Meals : breakfast Note : if the mentioned cruises are not available, the company have the right to Change the Cruise as it of same category.</p>'),
(2072, 424, 'fr', 'Adieu et départ', '<p>Savourez votre dernier petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de la croisi&egrave;re alors que nous disons adieu &agrave; ce voyage inoubliable. D&eacute;barquez apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner et continuez votre exploration de Louxor avec une visite de la Vall&eacute;e des Rois (trois tombeaux seulement) et du majestueux temple de la reine Hatshepsout, connu sous le nom d\'El-Deir El-Bahari. Dans l\'apr&egrave;s-midi, notre repr&eacute;sentant vous accompagnera &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport/gare de Louxor pour la suite de votre voyage. Repas : petit-d&eacute;jeuner Remarque : si les croisi&egrave;res mentionn&eacute;es ne sont pas disponibles, la compagnie se r&eacute;serve le droit de modifier la croisi&egrave;re car elle est de m&ecirc;me cat&eacute;gorie.</p>'),
(2073, 424, 'de', 'Abschied und Abreise', '<p>Genie&szlig;en Sie Ihr letztes Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord der Kreuzfahrt, w&auml;hrend wir uns von dieser unvergesslichen Reise verabschieden. Gehen Sie nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck von Bord und setzen Sie Ihre Erkundung von Luxor mit einem Besuch des Tals der K&ouml;nige (nur drei Gr&auml;ber) und des majest&auml;tischen K&ouml;nigin-Hatschepsut-Tempels, bekannt als El-Deir El-Bahari, fort. Am Nachmittag begleitet Sie unser Vertreter zum Flughafen/Bahnhof Luxor f&uuml;r Ihre Weiterreise. Mahlzeiten: Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck. Hinweis: Wenn die genannten Kreuzfahrten nicht verf&uuml;gbar sind, hat das Unternehmen das Recht, die Kreuzfahrt in die gleiche Kategorie zu &auml;ndern.</p>'),
(2074, 424, 'it', 'Addio e partenza', '<p>Assapora la tua ultima colazione a bordo della crociera mentre salutiamo questo viaggio indimenticabile. Sbarco dopo colazione e continua la tua esplorazione di Luxor con una visita alla Valle dei Re (solo tre tombe) e al maestoso Tempio della Regina Hatshepsut, noto come El-Deir El-Bahari. Nel pomeriggio, il nostro rappresentante ti accompagner&agrave; all\'aeroporto/stazione ferroviaria di Luxor per il proseguimento del viaggio. Pasti: colazione Nota: se le crociere menzionate non sono disponibili, la compagnia si riserva il diritto di modificare la crociera assegnandola alla stessa categoria.</p>'),
(2075, 424, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2076, 424, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2077, 424, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2078, 425, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p data-start=\"915\" data-end=\"1278\">Your tour begins with a scenic drive south from Aswan through desert landscapes toward the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Abu Simbel. Upon arrival, you will explore the Great Temple of Ramses II, dominated by four monumental seated statues that guard the entrance. Inside, reliefs and scenes depict royal power, religious devotion, and the famous Battle of Kadesh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1280\" data-end=\"1706\">You then continue to the Temple of Queen Nefertari, dedicated to the goddess Hathor. This elegant structure honors the queen alongside Ramses II, showcasing beautifully preserved reliefs and vibrant details. Your guide will also explain how both temples were cut into massive blocks and moved to higher ground to save them from the rising waters of Lake Nasser. After your visit, you will return comfortably to Aswan by coach.</p>'),
(2079, 425, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2080, 425, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2081, 425, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2082, 425, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2083, 425, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2084, 425, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2085, 426, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>get picked up from your hotel in Luxor by your Egyptologist tour guide at 7 AM and begin driving north of Luxor past local daily life. As you drive, admire views of quaint villages all the way to Abydos Temple, and listen closely as your expert guide tells you about interesting historical details of the great temple. Unique because of its limestone construction laid out over three levels, Abydos Temple is considered one-of-kind in many other respects. Find out why as you explore this historical treasure trove.&nbsp; Afterwards, drive on to Dendara Temple. Dedicated to Hathor, the goddess of motherhood, the Dendara Temple dates back to the late Ptolemaic Period and is located on holy Egyptian ground. The site is renowned for its relics of religious structures built during the reign of the Old Kingdom of Pharaoh Pepi the First.&nbsp; Enjoy taking stunning photos at these mesmerizing historical locations. When the adventure is over, get dropped off back at your hotel in Luxor.</p>'),
(2086, 426, 'fr', 'Jour 1', '<p>Faites-vous chercher &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel &agrave; Louxor par votre guide &eacute;gyptologue &agrave; 7 heures du matin et commencez &agrave; conduire au nord de Louxor en passant par la vie quotidienne locale. Pendant que vous conduisez, admirez la vue sur les villages pittoresques jusqu\'au temple d\'Abydos et &eacute;coutez attentivement votre guide expert vous raconter des d&eacute;tails historiques int&eacute;ressants sur le grand temple. Unique en raison de sa construction en pierre calcaire r&eacute;partie sur trois niveaux, le temple d\'Abydos est consid&eacute;r&eacute; comme unique &agrave; bien d\'autres &eacute;gards. D&eacute;couvrez pourquoi en explorant ce tr&eacute;sor historique. Ensuite, continuez vers le temple de Dendara. D&eacute;di&eacute; &agrave; Hathor, la d&eacute;esse de la maternit&eacute;, le temple de Dendara remonte &agrave; la fin de la p&eacute;riode ptol&eacute;ma&iuml;que et est situ&eacute; sur le territoire sacr&eacute; de l\'&Eacute;gypte. Le site est r&eacute;put&eacute; pour ses reliques d\'&eacute;difices religieux construits sous le r&egrave;gne de l\'Ancien Empire du pharaon P&eacute;pi Premier. Profitez de prendre de superbes photos dans ces lieux historiques fascinants. Une fois l\'aventure termin&eacute;e, soyez d&eacute;pos&eacute; &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel &agrave; Louxor.</p>'),
(2087, 426, 'de', 'Tag 1', '<p>Lassen Sie sich um 7 Uhr morgens von Ihrem &auml;gyptologischen Reiseleiter von Ihrem Hotel in Luxor abholen und beginnen Sie mit der Fahrt n&ouml;rdlich von Luxor, vorbei am Alltagsleben der Einheimischen. Bewundern Sie w&auml;hrend der Fahrt die Aussicht auf malerische D&ouml;rfer bis hin zum Abydos-Tempel und h&ouml;ren Sie aufmerksam zu, w&auml;hrend Ihr fachkundiger Reisef&uuml;hrer Ihnen interessante historische Details des gro&szlig;en Tempels erz&auml;hlt. Der Abydos-Tempel ist aufgrund seiner Kalksteinkonstruktion auf drei Ebenen einzigartig und gilt in vielerlei Hinsicht als einzigartig. Finden Sie heraus, warum, w&auml;hrend Sie diese historische Schatzkammer erkunden. Anschlie&szlig;end fahren Sie weiter zum Dendara-Tempel. Der Dendara-Tempel ist Hathor, der G&ouml;ttin der Mutterschaft, gewidmet und stammt aus der sp&auml;ten Ptolem&auml;erzeit. Er befindet sich auf heiligem &auml;gyptischen Boden. Die St&auml;tte ist bekannt f&uuml;r ihre Relikte religi&ouml;ser Bauwerke, die w&auml;hrend der Herrschaft des Alten K&ouml;nigreichs von Pharao Pepi dem Ersten errichtet wurden. Genie&szlig;en Sie atemberaubende Fotos an diesen faszinierenden historischen Orten. Wenn das Abenteuer vorbei ist, werden Sie zu Ihrem Hotel in Luxor zur&uuml;ckgebracht.</p>'),
(2088, 426, 'it', 'Giorno 1', '<p>prendi il prelievo dal tuo hotel a Luxor dalla tua guida turistica egittologa alle 7 del mattino e inizia a guidare a nord di Luxor, oltre la vita quotidiana locale. Mentre guidi, ammira le viste dei pittoreschi villaggi fino al Tempio di Abydos e ascolta attentamente mentre la tua guida esperta ti racconta interessanti dettagli storici del grande tempio. Unico per la sua costruzione in pietra calcarea disposta su tre livelli, il Tempio di Abydos &egrave; considerato unico nel suo genere sotto molti altri aspetti. Scopri perch&eacute; mentre esplori questo tesoro storico. Successivamente, prosegui fino al Tempio di Dendara. Dedicato a Hathor, la dea della maternit&agrave;, il Tempio di Dendara risale al tardo periodo tolemaico e si trova sul suolo sacro egiziano. Il sito &egrave; rinomato per le sue reliquie di strutture religiose costruite durante il regno dell\'Antico Regno del faraone Pepi I. Divertiti a scattare splendide foto in questi affascinanti luoghi storici. Al termine dell\'avventura, fatti riportare al tuo hotel a Luxor.</p>'),
(2089, 426, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2090, 426, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2091, 426, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2092, 427, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Visiting the Nubian village is a must when you are in Aswan. Between all Aswan attractions, this could be the only trip that will capture your heart in all meanings. The Nubian people are so friendly and overwhelming, great hospitality will be waiting for you in one of the Nubian family houses. They have dark skin and speak a language called Nuba or Nubian. Some said they consider their language as a very sacred custom of their own and refuse to teach it to any foreigner.&nbsp; The Nubian houses are made of mud and often colored blue or orange. Palm trees and gardens are everywhere; they raise chickens and goats mostly on their farms. Some locals if not farming, they would live from selling handicrafts and women drawing Henna for tourists. Such a wonderful trip for adults, kids, and all ages. Book Aswan Nubian Village Tour Day Trip Now &amp; Enjoy the best local experience.</p>'),
(2093, 427, 'fr', 'Jour 1', '<p>La visite du village nubien est un incontournable lorsque vous &ecirc;tes &agrave; Assouan. Entre toutes les attractions d\'Assouan, cela pourrait &ecirc;tre le seul voyage qui captivera votre c&oelig;ur dans tous les sens. Le peuple nubien est si sympathique et chaleureux qu\'une grande hospitalit&eacute; vous attend dans l\'une des maisons familiales nubiennes. Ils ont la peau fonc&eacute;e et parlent une langue appel&eacute;e Nuba ou Nubien. Certains ont d&eacute;clar&eacute; qu&rsquo;ils consid&eacute;raient leur langue comme une coutume tr&egrave;s sacr&eacute;e et refusaient de l&rsquo;enseigner &agrave; un &eacute;tranger. Les maisons nubiennes sont faites de boue et souvent color&eacute;es en bleu ou orange. Les palmiers et les jardins sont partout ; ils &eacute;l&egrave;vent des poulets et des ch&egrave;vres principalement dans leurs fermes. Certains habitants, s\'ils ne cultivaient pas, vivaient de la vente d\'objets artisanaux et de femmes dessinant du henn&eacute; pour les touristes. Un voyage merveilleux pour les adultes, les enfants et tous les &acirc;ges. R&eacute;servez d&egrave;s maintenant l\'excursion d\'une journ&eacute;e dans le village nubien d\'Assouan et profitez de la meilleure exp&eacute;rience locale.</p>'),
(2094, 427, 'de', 'Tag 1', '<p>Der Besuch des nubischen Dorfes ist ein Muss, wenn Sie in Assuan sind. Unter all den Sehensw&uuml;rdigkeiten Assuans k&ouml;nnte dies die einzige Reise sein, die Ihr Herz in jeder Hinsicht erobern wird. Das nubische Volk ist so freundlich und &uuml;berw&auml;ltigend, dass Sie in einem der nubischen Familienh&auml;user gro&szlig;artige Gastfreundschaft erwartet. Sie haben dunkle Haut und sprechen eine Sprache namens Nuba oder Nubiisch. Einige sagten, sie betrachten ihre Sprache als einen sehr heiligen Brauch und weigern sich, sie einem Ausl&auml;nder beizubringen. Die nubischen H&auml;user bestehen aus Lehm und sind oft blau oder orange gef&auml;rbt. &Uuml;berall gibt es Palmen und G&auml;rten; Sie z&uuml;chten haupts&auml;chlich H&uuml;hner und Ziegen auf ihren H&ouml;fen. Einige Einheimische lebten, wenn sie nicht in der Landwirtschaft t&auml;tig waren, vom Verkauf von Kunsthandwerk und von Frauen, die Henna f&uuml;r Touristen zeichneten. Was f&uuml;r eine wundervolle Reise f&uuml;r Erwachsene, Kinder und alle Altersgruppen. Buchen Sie jetzt einen Tagesausflug zum nubischen Dorf Assuan und genie&szlig;en Sie das beste Erlebnis vor Ort.</p>');
INSERT INTO `tour_day_translations` (`id`, `tour_day_id`, `locale`, `title`, `description`) VALUES
(2095, 427, 'it', 'Giorno 1', '<p>Visitare il villaggio nubiano &egrave; d\'obbligo quando ti trovi ad Assuan. Tra tutte le attrazioni di Assuan, questo potrebbe essere l\'unico viaggio che catturer&agrave; il tuo cuore in tutti i significati. Il popolo nubiano &egrave; cos&igrave; amichevole e travolgente, una grande ospitalit&agrave; ti aspetter&agrave; in una delle case della famiglia nubiana. Hanno la pelle scura e parlano una lingua chiamata Nuba o Nubiano. Alcuni hanno affermato di considerare la loro lingua come un\'usanza molto sacra e di rifiutarsi di insegnarla a qualsiasi straniero. Le case nubiane sono fatte di fango e spesso colorate di blu o arancione. Palme e giardini sono ovunque; allevano polli e capre principalmente nelle loro fattorie. Alcuni locali, se non coltivassero, vivrebbero vendendo prodotti artigianali e donne che disegnavano l\'henn&eacute; per i turisti. Un viaggio cos&igrave; meraviglioso per adulti, bambini e tutte le et&agrave;. Prenota subito la gita di un giorno al tour del villaggio nubiano di Assuan e goditi la migliore esperienza locale.</p>'),
(2096, 427, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2097, 427, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2098, 427, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2099, 428, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Visiting the Nubian village is a must when you are in Aswan. Between all Aswan attractions, this could be the only trip that will capture your heart in all meanings. The Nubian people are so friendly and overwhelming, great hospitality will be waiting for you in one of the Nubian family houses. They have dark skin and speak a language called Nuba or Nubian. Some said they consider their language as a very sacred custom of their own and refuse to teach it to any foreigner.&nbsp; The Nubian houses are made of mud and often colored blue or orange. Palm trees and gardens are everywhere; they raise chickens and goats mostly on their farms. Some locals if not farming, they would live from selling handicrafts and women drawing Henna for tourists. Such a wonderful trip for adults, kids, and all ages. Book Aswan Nubian Village Tour Day Trip Now &amp; Enjoy the best local experience.</p>'),
