t;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:4408131},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Note : For pick up / drop off form Cairo airport, Sphinx airport, New Administrative Capital, New Cairo, Helioplis, Badr City, Shorouk, Rehab, Obour, Sheraton Almatar, Sheikh Zayed city or Madinty City will be for additional cost</span></strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"my-12\">\r\n<section class=\"p-4 pb-6 flex flex-col gap-4 border-b-2 border-b-[#EEEEEE]\">\r\n<div class=\"flex justify-between items-center\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>'),
(2325, 462, 'en', 'Day 1 : Safari Trip to Bahariya - Black Desert - Old & New White Desert', '<p>The adventure commences in the bustling city of&nbsp;<strong>Cairo</strong>. an early morning pick-up in our air-conditioned vehicle. We journey towards the serene&nbsp;<strong>Bahariya Oasis</strong>, a tranquil retreat in the desert. Upon arrival, an off-road jeep stands ready to kickstart our exhilarating exploration.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>White Desert National Park</strong></h2>\r\n<p>White Desert National Park, is famous for its surreal landscapes of white limestone rock formations shaped by wind erosion. These unique shapes, resembling giant mushrooms or animals, create an otherworldly scenery. The park offers a peaceful, natural escape and is popular for desert safaris, camping under the stars, and photography.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Black Desert</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Black Desert, is known for its unique dark, volcanic hills and black rocks that cover the sand. The landscape is dotted with mountains and hills, giving it a striking contrast to the nearby White Desert.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>El Hez Village&rsquo;s</strong></h2>\r\n<p>El Hez Village&rsquo;s Cold Spring, is a natural oasis spring offering cool, refreshing water in the middle of the desert. It&rsquo;s a popular spot for travelers to relax and enjoy the natural beauty of the area. Surrounded by palm trees and serene landscapes.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Crystal Mountain</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Crystal Mountain, is a natural wonder in Egypt&rsquo;s Western Desert. The mountain is made up of sparkling quartz crystals that shimmer in the sunlight, giving it its name. A popular stop on desert safaris.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Agabat Valley</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Agabat Valley, is known for its breathtaking, otherworldly landscapes. Surrounded by towering white limestone cliffs and golden sand dunes, the valley features stunning rock formations shaped by wind erosion.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The highlight of our expedition is the visit to the Old White Desert, a natural wonder housing unique formations that mimic mushrooms and tents. We further explore the New White Desert, a surreal landscape adorned with striking limestone formations. As the day draws to a close, we set up camp amidst these natural marvels. A delectable dinner under the starry sky offers the perfect setting to reminisce about the day&rsquo;s adventures.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals</strong>: Lunch, Dinner</p>'),
