(2332, 463, 'en', 'Day 2 : Enjoy the Bahariya Oasis Sunrise & Return Back to Cairo', '<p>Awake to a stunning sunrise and savor a hearty breakfast in our camp. After breakfast, we drive back to the oasis in our jeep. A comfortable vehicle awaits to transport us back to the vibrant city of Cairo, marking the culmination of this unforgettable journey.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals</strong>: Breakfast.</p>'),
(2333, 464, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p data-start=\"915\" data-end=\"1278\">Your tour begins with a scenic drive south from Aswan through desert landscapes toward the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Abu Simbel. Upon arrival, you will explore the Great Temple of Ramses II, dominated by four monumental seated statues that guard the entrance. Inside, reliefs and scenes depict royal power, religious devotion, and the famous Battle of Kadesh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1280\" data-end=\"1706\">You then continue to the Temple of Queen Nefertari, dedicated to the goddess Hathor. This elegant structure honors the queen alongside Ramses II, showcasing beautifully preserved reliefs and vibrant details. Your guide will also explain how both temples were cut into massive blocks and moved to higher ground to save them from the rising waters of Lake Nasser. After your visit, you will return comfortably to Aswan by coach.</p>'),
(2334, 464, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2335, 464, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2336, 464, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2337, 464, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2338, 464, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2339, 464, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2340, 465, 'en', 'Tour Itinerary', '<p>Pick up with your expert Bird Guide from your departure point and transferred on to a traditional felucca sailboat at the dockside in Aswan. You will set sail across the Nile from the East Bank to the West Bank of the Nile towards Lord Kitchener\'s Island. From here, your Guide will start pointing out the locations of where you will see the birdlife ranging from Egrets both adult and chicks, to Parakeets amongst the trees. Whilst passing along the Island, there is beautiful flora and fauna such as Hibiscus, lantana, bougainvillea, Poinciana, acacia trees and mimosa all blooming in radiant colors.</p>\r\n<p>Sailing up river towards the Mausoleum of the Aga Khan, you may be astounded at the sight of many more bird species wading in the waters of the Cataract Islands such as Kingfishers, Malachite Kingfishers, Striated Herons, Little Bitten Herons, Night Herons, along with Little Green Bee Eaters, and Nile Valley Sunbirds. A truly delightful tour for nature lovers. at the end you will Return to the dock in Aswan and transferred to your original pick up point.</p>'),
(2341, 465, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2342, 465, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2343, 465, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2344, 465, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2345, 465, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2346, 465, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2347, 466, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p data-start=\"542\" data-end=\"1354\">The Cairo Food Tour typically begins in the late afternoon or early evening with a meet-up in downtown Cairo, where guests are introduced to their guide and fellow participants before heading into vibrant local streets. The tour includes multiple stops at carefully selected food vendors and hidden gems, starting with classic Egyptian street foods like taameya (falafel) and koshary, followed by visits to traditional restaurants for dishes such as grilled meats or shawarma. Along the way, the guide shares stories about Cairo&rsquo;s culinary heritage and local culture, with opportunities to explore markets and bakeries offering fresh bread and pastries. The experience concludes with a sweet finish featuring desserts like basbousa or kunafa, often paired with tea or fresh juice.</p>'),
(2348, 466, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2349, 466, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2350, 466, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2351, 466, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2352, 466, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2353, 466, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2354, 467, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Pharaoh Vibes Tours beckons you to a majestic journey through the beginning of time. Your private tour guide will collect you from your Cairo hotel and set you out to the iconic Giza Plateau.<br><br>Here, the Pyramids of Cheops, Chephren, and Mykerinus rise from the sands, a testament to ancient ambition and ingenuity. Stand in awe at the Great Sphinx, Chephren\'s guardian, whose enigmatic visage has stirred the imaginations of travelers for centuries.<br><br>Your exploration continues at the Valley Temple, a site of profound significance. It was here that the pharaohs\' mummies underwent purification and mummification, rituals as essential to their journey to the afterlife as the pyramids themselves.<br><br>Behold the Seven Wonders of the World, where the 5000-year-old necropolis awaits. The Great Pyramids, a marvel of human achievement, stand as sentinels to history, watched over by the vigilant Sphinx. This is not merely a tour; it is a pilgrimage to the heart of Egypt\'s grandeur, a must-see for every wanderer of the world. With Pharaoh Vibes Tours, the past is not just to be seen, but to be experienced.&nbsp;</p>'),
(2355, 467, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2356, 467, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2357, 467, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2358, 467, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2359, 467, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2360, 467, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2361, 468, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Visiting the Nubian village is a must when you are in Aswan. Between all Aswan attractions, this could be the only trip that will capture your heart in all meanings. The Nubian people are so friendly and overwhelming, great hospitality will be waiting for you in one of the Nubian family houses. They have dark skin and speak a language called Nuba or Nubian. Some said they consider their language as a very sacred custom of their own and refuse to teach it to any foreigner.&nbsp; The Nubian houses are made of mud and often colored blue or orange. Palm trees and gardens are everywhere; they raise chickens and goats mostly on their farms. Some locals if not farming, they would live from selling handicrafts and women drawing Henna for tourists. Such a wonderful trip for adults, kids, and all ages. Book Aswan Nubian Village Tour Day Trip Now &amp; Enjoy the best local experience.</p>'),
(2362, 468, 'fr', 'Jour 1', '<p>La visite du village nubien est un incontournable lorsque vous &ecirc;tes &agrave; Assouan. Entre toutes les attractions d\'Assouan, cela pourrait &ecirc;tre le seul voyage qui captivera votre c&oelig;ur dans tous les sens. Le peuple nubien est si sympathique et chaleureux qu\'une grande hospitalit&eacute; vous attend dans l\'une des maisons familiales nubiennes. Ils ont la peau fonc&eacute;e et parlent une langue appel&eacute;e Nuba ou Nubien. Certains ont d&eacute;clar&eacute; qu&rsquo;ils consid&eacute;raient leur langue comme une coutume tr&egrave;s sacr&eacute;e et refusaient de l&rsquo;enseigner &agrave; un &eacute;tranger. Les maisons nubiennes sont faites de boue et souvent color&eacute;es en bleu ou orange. Les palmiers et les jardins sont partout ; ils &eacute;l&egrave;vent des poulets et des ch&egrave;vres principalement dans leurs fermes. Certains habitants, s\'ils ne cultivaient pas, vivaient de la vente d\'objets artisanaux et de femmes dessinant du henn&eacute; pour les touristes. Un voyage merveilleux pour les adultes, les enfants et tous les &acirc;ges. R&eacute;servez d&egrave;s maintenant l\'excursion d\'une journ&eacute;e dans le village nubien d\'Assouan et profitez de la meilleure exp&eacute;rience locale.</p>'),
(2363, 468, 'de', 'Tag 1', '<p>Der Besuch des nubischen Dorfes ist ein Muss, wenn Sie in Assuan sind. Unter all den Sehensw&uuml;rdigkeiten Assuans k&ouml;nnte dies die einzige Reise sein, die Ihr Herz in jeder Hinsicht erobern wird. Das nubische Volk ist so freundlich und &uuml;berw&auml;ltigend, dass Sie in einem der nubischen Familienh&auml;user gro&szlig;artige Gastfreundschaft erwartet. Sie haben dunkle Haut und sprechen eine Sprache namens Nuba oder Nubiisch. Einige sagten, sie betrachten ihre Sprache als einen sehr heiligen Brauch und weigern sich, sie einem Ausl&auml;nder beizubringen. Die nubischen H&auml;user bestehen aus Lehm und sind oft blau oder orange gef&auml;rbt. &Uuml;berall gibt es Palmen und G&auml;rten; Sie z&uuml;chten haupts&auml;chlich H&uuml;hner und Ziegen auf ihren H&ouml;fen. Einige Einheimische lebten, wenn sie nicht in der Landwirtschaft t&auml;tig waren, vom Verkauf von Kunsthandwerk und von Frauen, die Henna f&uuml;r Touristen zeichneten. Was f&uuml;r eine wundervolle Reise f&uuml;r Erwachsene, Kinder und alle Altersgruppen. Buchen Sie jetzt einen Tagesausflug zum nubischen Dorf Assuan und genie&szlig;en Sie das beste Erlebnis vor Ort.</p>'),
(2364, 468, 'it', 'Giorno 1', '<p>Visitare il villaggio nubiano &egrave; d\'obbligo quando ti trovi ad Assuan. Tra tutte le attrazioni di Assuan, questo potrebbe essere l\'unico viaggio che catturer&agrave; il tuo cuore in tutti i significati. Il popolo nubiano &egrave; cos&igrave; amichevole e travolgente, una grande ospitalit&agrave; ti aspetter&agrave; in una delle case della famiglia nubiana. Hanno la pelle scura e parlano una lingua chiamata Nuba o Nubiano. Alcuni hanno affermato di considerare la loro lingua come un\'usanza molto sacra e di rifiutarsi di insegnarla a qualsiasi straniero. Le case nubiane sono fatte di fango e spesso colorate di blu o arancione. Palme e giardini sono ovunque; allevano polli e capre principalmente nelle loro fattorie. Alcuni locali, se non coltivassero, vivrebbero vendendo prodotti artigianali e donne che disegnavano l\'henn&eacute; per i turisti. Un viaggio cos&igrave; meraviglioso per adulti, bambini e tutte le et&agrave;. Prenota subito la gita di un giorno al tour del villaggio nubiano di Assuan e goditi la migliore esperienza locale.</p>'),
(2365, 468, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2366, 468, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2367, 468, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2368, 469, 'en', 'Tour Itinerary', '<div class=\"flex flex-col text-sm\">\r\n<section class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" data-turn-id=\"request-WEB:3b166c7b-2c9e-41f9-82b4-e0e1fdf274da-0\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-2\" data-scroll-anchor=\"true\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\">\r\n<div class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"0\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"04bda359-08da-4137-8051-40483c334e2f\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-4-thinking\" data-turn-start-message=\"true\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\r\n<div class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word light markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<p data-start=\"44\" data-end=\"637\" data-is-only-node=\"\">Begin your day before sunrise with hotel pickup and transfer to the launch site, where you will enjoy a light refreshment while watching the hot air balloon being prepared. After a short safety briefing, board the balloon and gently rise into the morning sky for a breathtaking flight, taking in panoramic views of the landscape as the sun comes up. Upon landing, celebrate the experience with a traditional toast and commemorative certificate before returning to your hotel. The rest of the morning can be spent at leisure, giving you time to relax and reflect on the unforgettable adventure.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>'),
(2369, 469, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2370, 469, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2371, 469, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2372, 469, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2373, 469, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2374, 469, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2375, 470, 'en', 'Day 6', '<p>after breakfast check out and saying&nbsp;Good&nbsp;bye</p>'),
(2376, 470, 'fr', 'Jour 6', '<p>Apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner, partez et dites Au revoir</p>'),
(2377, 470, 'de', 'Tag 6', '<p>Nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck auschecken und sich verabschieden</p>'),
(2378, 470, 'it', 'Giorno 6', '<p>dopo la colazione fai il check-out e ti salutiamo</p>'),
(2379, 470, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2380, 470, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2381, 470, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2382, 471, 'en', 'Day 5 :', '<p>after breakfast visit KomAbom temple ,&nbsp;<br>After lunch , swimming in the Nile at Herdyab where is nice sand bitch of the Nile&nbsp;<br>Then sailing to Aswan<br>Over night at Aswan</p>'),
(2383, 471, 'fr', 'Jour 5 :', '<p>Apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner, visite du temple de KomAbom, <br>Apr&egrave;s le d&eacute;jeuner, baignade dans le Nil &agrave; Herdyab o&ugrave; se trouve la belle chienne de sable du Nil <br>Puis navigation vers Assouan<br>Nuit &agrave; Assouan</p>'),
(2384, 471, 'de', 'Tag 5:', '<p>Nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck besuchen Sie den KomAbom-Tempel. <br>Nach dem Mittagessen schwimmen Sie im Nil bei Herdyab, wo es einen sch&ouml;nen Sandstreifen am Nil gibt. <br>Dann segeln Sie nach Assuan.<br>&Uuml;bernachtung in Assuan.</p>'),
(2385, 471, 'it', 'Giorno 5:', '<p>dopo la colazione visita al tempio di KomAbom, <br>Dopo pranzo, nuotata nel Nilo a Herdyab dove si trova la bella cagna di sabbia del Nilo <br>Poi navigazione verso Assuan<br>Pernottamento ad Assuan</p>'),
(2386, 471, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2387, 471, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2388, 471, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2389, 472, 'en', 'Day 4', '<p>After breakfasts visit Elsalisla quarry , where it was using for cut off Sandstone that used to built the temples .<br>Then sailing.<br>Before Lunch waking at Faris village&nbsp;<br>Over night Maneha island</p>'),
(2390, 472, 'fr', 'Jour 4', '<p>Apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner, visitez la carri&egrave;re d\'Elsalisla, o&ugrave; elle &eacute;tait utilis&eacute;e pour le gr&egrave;s coup&eacute; utilis&eacute; pour construire les temples.<br>Puis navigation.<br>Avant le d&eacute;jeuner, r&eacute;veil au village de Faris <br>Nuit sur l\'&icirc;le de Maneha</p>'),
(2391, 472, 'de', 'Tag 4', '<p>Nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck besuchen Sie den Elsalisla-Steinbruch, in dem Sandstein abgebaut wurde, aus dem die Tempel gebaut wurden.<br>Dann segeln.<br>Vor dem Mittagessen Aufwachen im Dorf Faris.<br>&Uuml;bernachtung auf der Insel Maneha</p>'),
(2392, 472, 'it', 'Giorno 4', '<p>Dopo la colazione visita la cava di Elsalisla, dove veniva utilizzata per tagliare l\'arenaria utilizzata per costruire i templi.<br>Poi navigazione.<br>Prima di pranzo svegliarsi al villaggio di Faris <br>Pernottamento sull\'isola di Maneha</p>'),
(2393, 472, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2394, 472, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2395, 472, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2396, 473, 'en', 'Day 3', '<p>&nbsp;After breakfast sailing&nbsp;<br>After lunch , waking at Basaw island , to know more about the local people where we have drink with them .<br>Over night at Elsalisla .</p>'),
(2397, 473, 'fr', 'Jour 3', '<p>Apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner, navigation <br>Apr&egrave;s le d&eacute;jeuner, r&eacute;veil sur l\'&icirc;le de Basaw, pour en savoir plus sur la population locale o&ugrave; nous prenons un verre avec eux.<br>Nuit &agrave; Elsalisla.</p>'),
(2398, 473, 'de', 'Tag 3', '<p>Nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck segeln <br>Nach dem Mittagessen Aufwachen auf der Insel Basaw, um mehr &uuml;ber die Einheimischen zu erfahren, mit denen wir etwas trinken.<br>&Uuml;bernachtung in Elsalisla.</p>'),
(2399, 473, 'it', 'Giorno 3', '<p>Dopo la colazione navigazione in barca <br>Dopo pranzo, risveglio all\'isola di Basaw, per conoscere meglio la gente locale dove beviamo qualcosa con loro.<br>Pernottamento a Elsalisla.</p>'),
(2400, 473, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2401, 473, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2402, 473, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2403, 474, 'en', 'Day 2', '<p>After having breakfast visit ElKab tombs , where the nobles tombs from 17&amp;18 dynasty .<br>Then sailing&nbsp;<br>After the lunch visit Edfu temple , where is the most intact temple&nbsp;<br>Diner Barbecue upon the weather.<br>Over night Fawaza island.</p>'),
(2404, 474, 'fr', 'Jour 2', '<p>Apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner, visitez les tombeaux d\'ElKab, o&ugrave; se trouvent les tombeaux des nobles des 17e et 18e dynasties.<br>Puis navigation <br>Apr&egrave;s le d&eacute;jeuner, visitez le temple d\'Edfou, o&ugrave; se trouve le temple le plus intact <br>D&icirc;ner barbecue selon la m&eacute;t&eacute;o.<br>Nuit sur l\'&icirc;le de Fawaza.</p>'),
(2405, 474, 'de', 'Tag 2', '<p>Nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck besuchen Sie die ElKab-Gr&auml;ber, wo sich die Adligengr&auml;ber aus der 17. und 18. Dynastie befinden.<br>Dann segeln wir.<br>Nach dem Mittagessen besuchen Sie den Edfu-Tempel, wo sich der am besten erhaltene Tempel befindet.<br>Abendessen, Barbecue, je nach Wetterlage.<br>&Uuml;ber Nacht auf der Insel Fawaza.</p>'),
(2406, 474, 'it', 'Giorno 2', '<p>Dopo aver fatto colazione, visita le tombe di ElKab, dove si trovano le tombe dei nobili della dinastia 17 e 18.<br>Poi navigazione <br>Dopo il pranzo visita il tempio di Edfu, dove si trova il tempio pi&ugrave; intatto <br>Cena Barbecue a seconda del tempo.<br>Pernottamento sull\'isola di Fawaza.</p>'),
(2407, 474, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2408, 474, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2409, 474, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2410, 475, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>After arriving and check in , visit Esna temple ,<br>Then back to the boat , having lunch and sailing&nbsp;<br>Over night ElHajes</p>'),
(2411, 475, 'fr', 'Jour 1', '<p>Apr&egrave;s votre arriv&eacute;e et votre enregistrement, visitez le temple d\'Esna,<br>Puis retour au bateau, d&eacute;jeuner et navigation <br>Nuit &agrave; ElHajes</p>'),
(2412, 475, 'de', 'Tag 1', '<p>Nach der Ankunft und dem Check-in besuchen Sie den Esna-Tempel.<br>Dann kehren Sie zum Boot zur&uuml;ck, essen zu Mittag und segeln.<br>&Uuml;bernachtung in ElHajes</p>'),
(2413, 475, 'it', 'Giorno 1', '<p>Dopo l\'arrivo e il check-in, visita il tempio di Esna,<br>Poi torna alla barca, pranza e naviga <br>Pernottamento a ElHajes</p>'),
(2414, 475, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2415, 475, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2416, 475, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2417, 476, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>After arriving and check in , visit Esna temple ,<br>Then back to the boat , having lunch and sailing&nbsp;<br>Over night ElHajes</p>'),
