(2792, 529, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2793, 529, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2794, 529, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2795, 530, 'en', 'ARRIVAL Day 1 FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will<br>assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we<br>will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local<br>surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey.</p>'),
(2796, 530, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2797, 530, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2798, 530, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2799, 530, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2800, 530, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2801, 530, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2802, 531, 'en', 'CHECK OUT - FLY BACK TO CAIRO, FINAL DEPARTURE - TUESDAY,3RD OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out from your Hotel.<br>Catch our flight back to Cairo. catch your international flight.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Final Departure</strong></p>'),
(2803, 531, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2804, 531, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2805, 531, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2806, 531, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2807, 531, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2808, 531, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2809, 532, 'en', 'Day 1 CAIRO BY NIGHT TUESDAY,27TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will&nbsp;assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we&nbsp;will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local&nbsp;surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey.<br><br><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(2810, 532, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2811, 532, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2812, 532, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2813, 532, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2814, 532, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2815, 532, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2816, 533, 'en', 'THE PYRAMIDS OF GIZA, THE GREAT SPHINX, LUNCH, GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After Breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to visit the Pyramids and the Sphinx, which are the only surviving<br>wonder of the ancient world. You will have the option to enjoy a memorable camel ride in the vicinity of these magnificent<br>structures. Ahead of the pyramids, lies the Sphinx known as the guardian of the pyramids facing the sun every morning as it<br>rises from the east. Lunch will then be served at a local hygienic restaurant. Proceeding to The Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)<br>will host over 100,000 artifacts from ancient Egyptian civilization, many pieces are displayed for the first time.<br><br><strong>WEDNESDAY,28TH OF JULY 2027 - Overnight in Cairo</strong></p>'),
(2817, 533, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2818, 533, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2819, 533, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2820, 533, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2821, 533, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2822, 533, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2823, 534, 'en', 'THURSDAY,29TH OF JULY 2027 - FLY TO ASWAN, PHILAE TEMPLE, HIGH DAM', '<p>After Breakfast, you will catch your flight to Aswan . Check in your Hotel.<br>Next, you will visit Philae Temple also referred to as the Temple of Lovers which narrates the most ancient love story in&nbsp;history between Isis and Osiris. After that visit The High Dam, a rock fill dam across the River Nile at Aswan, completed&nbsp;in 1970 (and formally inaugurated in January 1971) The dam is 364 feet (111 meters) high, with a crest length of 12,562&nbsp;feet (3,830 meters) and a volume of 57,940,000 cubic yards (44,300,000 cubic meters), impounds a reservoir, Lake&nbsp;Nasser, that has a gross capacity of 5.97 trillion cubic feet (169 billion cubic meters.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Aswan</strong></p>'),
(2824, 534, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2825, 534, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2826, 534, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2827, 534, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2828, 534, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2829, 534, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2830, 535, 'en', 'ABU SIMBEL - FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will be transferred to Abu Simbel where you will be standing in front of a<br>temple carved in the mountain; a true miracle of ancient and modern engineering that<br>deserves to be counted among the wonders of the world.<br>back to Aswan.<br><br><strong>Overnight in Aswan.</strong></p>'),
(2831, 535, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2832, 535, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2833, 535, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2834, 535, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2835, 535, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2836, 535, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2837, 536, 'en', 'KOMOMBO TEMPLE & EDFU TEMPLE - SATURDAY,31TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>After having breakfast, we will transfer to Luxor by car. Next will visit Kom Ombo Temple, a very unusual temple. It\'s<br>uniqueness is for several reasons. It is dedication to two different deities, the local crocodile-headed god, Sobek, and the<br>falcon-headed god Horus. After that we will visit Edfu Temple . Considered to be one of the best preserved temples from<br>ancient Egypt, It is the largest temple dedicated to the god Horus.<br><br><strong>Overnight in Luxor</strong></p>'),
(2838, 536, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2839, 536, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2840, 536, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2841, 536, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2842, 536, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2843, 536, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2844, 537, 'en', 'VALLEY OF KINGS, QUEEN HATSHEPSUT MORTURY TEMPLE, COLOSSI OF MEMNON', '<p>After having breakfast, you will be taken to the West Bank and visit The Valley of Kings the home Egypt most known Pharoahs. The tour&nbsp;covers the special visit of 5 tombs including the Golden Pharaoh Tutankhamun&rsquo;s tomb and Ramesses VI. Then we head to visit Queen<br>Hatshepsut&rsquo;s magnificant Mortuary Temple built 3300 years ago; a unique temple that is engraved by the mountains and partially carved&nbsp;out of the rocks. After that visit Colossi of Memnon,Two towering statues of Pharaoh Amenhotep III, standing 18 meters high, built to guard&nbsp;the entrance of his lost mortuary temple. They are among the most iconic landmarks on Luxor&rsquo;s west bank.<br><strong>SUNDAY,1ST OF AUGUST 2027</strong><br><strong>Overnight in Luxor</strong></p>'),
(2845, 537, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2846, 537, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2847, 537, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2848, 537, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2849, 537, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2850, 537, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2851, 538, 'en', 'KARNAK TEMPLE & LUXOR TEMPLE - MONDAY,2ND OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>In the Morning: Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple, A special chance to witness the total solar eclipse from Karnak Temple. Watching<br>this rare event from such a historic place will be a truly unforgettable experience.<br>Proceeding our tour to Luxor Temple in which you&rsquo;ll stand in the shadows of the Great Ramses II colossi.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Luxor .</strong></p>'),
(2852, 538, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2853, 538, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2854, 538, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2855, 538, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2856, 538, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2857, 538, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2858, 539, 'en', 'Day 12 Departure', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out and be transported to Cairo<br>International Airport by private coach to catch your international<br>flight</p>'),
(2859, 539, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2860, 539, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2861, 539, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2862, 539, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2863, 539, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2864, 539, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2865, 540, 'en', 'Day 11: Private Opening of The Great Pyramid of Giza & Aromatherapy experience', '<p>After breakfast, you will experience an exclusive special private<br>opening of the Great Pyramid of Giza, the only surviving wonder of<br>the ancient world.<br>Next, we will visit a well-known perfumery.<br>Here, drawing on the knowledge of his ancestors, we will<br>be guided through this subject by a certified<br>aromatherapist. Known as \"Healer from the Heart\", he will present a<br>detailed explanation about the physical and psychological uses of<br>the organic essential oils of Egypt. Historically, the beneficial<br>effects of their use has been documented in various papyri of the<br>Ancients. After our essential oil lesson, we return to our hotel.<br>Egygo Travel would like to invite you to the Farewell Dinner.<br>Overnight in Cairo</p>'),
(2866, 540, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2867, 540, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2868, 540, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2869, 540, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2870, 540, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2871, 540, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2872, 541, 'en', 'Day 10 Back to Cairo', '<p>After breakfast, we will check out from our cruise to catch our flight back to Cairo.<br>Arrive to Cairo.<br>Check in at the hotel<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(2873, 541, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2874, 541, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2875, 541, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2876, 541, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2877, 541, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2878, 541, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2879, 542, 'en', 'Day 9 Abu Simble Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will travel to Abu Simble, visit the Temple of Ramesses the great which is carved in the mountain; a true miracle of<br>ancient and modern engineering that deserves to be counted among the wonders of the world. back to Aswan</p>'),
(2880, 542, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2881, 542, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2882, 542, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2883, 542, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2884, 542, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2885, 542, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2886, 543, 'en', 'Day 8 Philae Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will be boarding a small motor boat from the landing, We will head to the Philae Island. The island is home to Philae<br>Temple aka \"Temple of Lovers\" Dedicated to the goddess Isis, Philae Temple presents the perfect backdrop to the most ancient of all<br>love stories in history, that of Isis and Osiris.<br>Back to Dahabiya<br>Overnight on board</p>'),
(2887, 543, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2888, 543, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2889, 543, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2890, 543, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2891, 543, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2892, 543, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2893, 544, 'en', 'Day 7 Edfu Temple and Komombo Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will visit Edfu Temple . Considered to be one of<br>the best preserved temples from ancient Egypt, It is the largest<br>temple dedicated to the god Horus and his consort , the goddess,<br>Hathor of Dendera. Each year, Hathor would travel from her temple<br>in Dendera to visit Horus at Edfu. This event marked their sacred<br>marriage and, in ancient times, was an occasion of a great Festival<br>and pilgrimage. we will visit Kom Ombo Temple, a very unusual<br>temple. It\'s uniqueness is for several reasons. It is dedication to<br>two different deities, the local crocodile-headed god, Sobek, and<br>the falcon-headed god Horus.<br>Return to Dahabiya for overnight sailing Aswan<br>Overnight on board.</p>'),
(2894, 544, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2895, 544, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2896, 544, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2897, 544, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2898, 544, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2899, 544, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2900, 545, 'en', 'Day 6 Valley of the Kings and Karnak Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will start our tour by visiting Karnak Temple<br>which is believed to be the second most visited historical site<br>surpassed only by the Giza Pyramids. One of the many<br>highlights of Karnak Temple\'s is it hypostyle hall consisting of<br>134 massive columns in 16 rows.<br>Next stop is The Valley of Kings, the final resting place of many<br>of the ancient Egyptian Pharaohs. Here, we will visit some of the<br>better known tombs including that of Pharaoh Tutankhamen.<br>Overnight on board our dahabiya</p>'),
(2901, 545, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2902, 545, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2903, 545, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2904, 545, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2905, 545, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2906, 545, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2907, 546, 'en', 'Day 5 Dendera Temple and back to Luxor', '<p>Following breakfast, we set off, accompanied by our Egygo Egyptologist, to explore Dendera Temple.<br>Dedicated to goddess Hathor , the Temple is one of the best-preserved temples in Egypt. Depictions of Cleopatra VI appear on<br>Temple walls. On the rear wall is a carving of Cleoppatra VI (the popular Cleopatria) and her son Ptolemy XV who was fathered by Julius<br>Cesar.<br>Following our visits, we will have lunch at a local restaurant.<br>After lunch, we will transfer to Luxor for check-in at our Dahabiya.<br>Overnight in Luxor on board of Dahabiya.</p>'),
(2908, 546, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2909, 546, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2910, 546, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2911, 546, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2912, 546, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2913, 546, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2914, 547, 'en', 'Day 4 Flight to Luxor, Abydos Temple and overnight in Suhag', '<p>After breakfast, we travel to Cairo International Airport for<br>your flight to Luxor.<br>Upon arrival, we will be taken by private motor coach to<br>explore Abydos.<br>Abydos, home to the Temple of Seti I, father of Ramses II, is<br>one of the most important archaeological sites of Ancient<br>Egypt. During ancient times, it was the necropolis for Egypt\'s<br>earliest kings. The \"Abydos King List\" as well as Phoenician<br>and Aramaic graffiti are found on the temple walls.<br>While in Abydos, Egygo\'s Egytologist has arranged for a<br>private visit to the Osierion, it is normally closed to tourists.<br>The Osierion, a megalithic structure, built below ground<br>simulates an island. It is positioned at the rear of the Temple,<br>accessed only through the Temple body. On one of its<br>monoliths is painted the FLOWER OF LIFE, one of the most<br>important symbols of sacred geometry.<br>Overnight in Suhag</p>'),
(2915, 547, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2916, 547, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2917, 547, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2918, 547, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2919, 547, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2920, 547, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2921, 548, 'en', 'Day 3 Private visit to the Great Sphinx and Saqqara complex', '<p>Following breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you<br>for your special private visit to The Great Sphinx, arranged<br>by Egygo\'s experienced Egyptologist, commences by<br>private motor coach to the Giza Plateau. Constructed<br>around 2500BC (Old Kingdom) , the Great Sphinx is a<br>mythical creature with the head of a human and the body<br>of a lion. Facing east, The Great Sphinx greets the morning<br>sun while protecting the Giza pyramids.<br>After that, you will get to visit the Sakkara Complex, which<br>was the main burial area for kings, queens and nobles<br>during the old kingdom, in the same area, you will have the<br>opportunity to visit the Step Pyramid of King Djoser,<br>renowned as the first successful attempt at constructing a<br>standing pyramid 4800 years old</p>'),
(2922, 548, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2923, 548, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2924, 548, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2925, 548, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2926, 548, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2927, 548, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2928, 549, 'en', 'Day 2 GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to&nbsp;visit the Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM) Located near the&nbsp;Pyramids, the Grand Egyptian Museum is the largest&nbsp;archaeological museum in the world. It houses over&nbsp;100,000 artifacts, including the complete collection of&nbsp;King Tutankhamun. Designed to reflect ancient Egyptian&nbsp;heritage with a modern touch, GEM features state-of-the-&nbsp;art exhibits, conservation labs, and a grand staircase with&nbsp;colossal statues. A cultural landmark, it offers a unique&nbsp;journey through 5,000 years of history in one spectacular&nbsp;setting.<br>Egygo Travel would like to invite you to the Welcome&nbsp;Dinner.<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(2929, 549, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2930, 549, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2931, 549, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2932, 549, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(2933, 549, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(2934, 549, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(2935, 550, 'en', 'Day 1: Arrival', '<p>Upon arrival at Cairo International Airport, you will be met and<br>escorted by one of Egygo Travel representatives . They will assist<br>you in obtaining the necessary entry documents and guide you<br>through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we will<br>travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on<br>your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local<br>surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your<br>journey.<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(2936, 550, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(2937, 550, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(2938, 550, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(2939, 550, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
