INSERT INTO `tour_day_translations` (`id`, `tour_day_id`, `locale`, `title`, `description`) VALUES
(3096, 573, 'en', 'Day 2 GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to&nbsp;visit the Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM) Located near the&nbsp;Pyramids, the Grand Egyptian Museum is the largest&nbsp;archaeological museum in the world. It houses over&nbsp;100,000 artifacts, including the complete collection of&nbsp;King Tutankhamun. Designed to reflect ancient Egyptian&nbsp;heritage with a modern touch, GEM features state-of-the-&nbsp;art exhibits, conservation labs, and a grand staircase with&nbsp;colossal statues. A cultural landmark, it offers a unique&nbsp;journey through 5,000 years of history in one spectacular&nbsp;setting.<br>Egygo Travel would like to invite you to the Welcome&nbsp;Dinner.<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(3097, 573, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3098, 573, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3099, 573, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3100, 573, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3101, 573, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3102, 573, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3103, 574, 'en', 'Day 1: Arrival', '<p>Upon arrival at Cairo International Airport, you will be met and<br>escorted by one of Egygo Travel representatives . They will assist<br>you in obtaining the necessary entry documents and guide you<br>through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we will<br>travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on<br>your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local<br>surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your<br>journey.<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(3104, 574, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3105, 574, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3106, 574, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3107, 574, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3108, 574, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3109, 574, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3110, 575, 'en', 'Explore Giza', '<p>Vive Egiptos <span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Sun Pyramids Tours beckons you to a majestic journey through the beginning of time. Your private tour guide will collect you from your Cairo hotel and set you out to the iconic Giza Plateau. \\n\\nHere, the Pyramids of Cheops, Chephren, and Mykerinus rise from the sands, a testament to ancient ambition and ingenuity. Stand in awe at the Great Sphinx, Chephren\'s guardian, whose enigmatic visage has stirred the imaginations of travelers for centuries.\\n\\nYour exploration continues at the Valley Temple, a site of profound significance. It was here that the pharaohs\' mummies underwent purification and mummification, rituals as essential to their journey to the afterlife as the pyramids themselves.\\n\\nBehold the Seven Wonders of the World, where the 5000-year-old necropolis awaits. The Great Pyramids, a marvel of human achievement, stand as sentinels to history, watched over by the vigilant Sphinx. This is not merely a tour; it is a pilgrimage to the heart of Egypt\'s grandeur, a must-see for every wanderer of the world. With Sun Pyramids Tours, the past is not just to be seen, but to be experienced. &quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:9153,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;9&quot;:1,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">beckons you to a majestic journey through the beginning of time. Your private tour guide will collect you from your Cairo hotel and set you out to the iconic Giza Plateau.<br><br>Here, the Pyramids of Cheops, Chephren, and Mykerinus rise from the sands, a testament to ancient ambition and ingenuity. Stand in awe at the Great Sphinx, Chephren\'s guardian, whose enigmatic visage has stirred the imaginations of travelers for centuries.<br><br>Your exploration continues at the Valley Temple, a site of profound significance. It was here that the pharaohs\' mummies underwent purification and mummification, rituals as essential to their journey to the afterlife as the pyramids themselves.<br><br>Behold the Seven Wonders of the World, where the 5000-year-old necropolis awaits. The Great Pyramids, a marvel of human achievement, stand as sentinels to history, watched over by the vigilant Sphinx. This is not merely a tour; it is a pilgrimage to the heart of Egypt\'s grandeur, a must-see for every wanderer of the world. With Vive Egiptos, the past is not just to be seen, but to be experienced.&nbsp;</span></p>'),
(3111, 575, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3112, 575, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3113, 575, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3114, 575, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3115, 575, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3116, 575, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3117, 576, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>We will take you to the Sacred Valley of the Kings, where you will visit its most famous tombs. Then you will head to the great Temple of Hatshepsut, one of the greatest ancient architectures ever built. Its three massive terraces rise above the desert floor and into the cliffs of&nbsp;Deir El-Bahari. Images presented on the walls are of offerings and cult activity, with a painting showing Anubis escorting Hatshepsut to the shrine, and many more historic stories for you to discover. Then you will go to the famous Colossi of Memnon, and the great temple of Habu.</p>\r\n<p>A complimentary visit to the Alabaster Factory will be arranged for you, free of charge, so you can shop for the best Souvenirs to take back home.</p>\r\n<p>Guided by our professional Egyptologists, you will enjoy listening to the Story behind these ancient wonders and have all your inquiries answered with full attention.</p>'),
