(3157, 581, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3158, 581, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3159, 582, 'en', 'Day Tour Memphis Sakkara and Dahshur', '<p>With Our Representative, you will take a wonderful tour to discover Saqqara, where we will visit the oldest stone building in history. It was built by the engineer Imhotep for King Djoser, founder of the Third Dynasty. As well as enjoying visiting the pyramid of King Teti of the Sixth Dynasty, this pyramid is characterized by the presence of texts of the pyramids on its walls, which are magical texts to help the deceased in his sacred journey in the other world. then visiting the tombe of the Minister (Mre Roca) and then move to visit Memphis, the first ancient Egyptian capital to see the greatest statue of the greatest king in the history of ancient Egypt, King Ramses II. Then move immediately to visit the Dahshur&nbsp; where there are two great pyramids dating back to the era of the Fourth Dynasty and they were built by King Sneferu, the father of King Khufu, and the pyramids was built of limestone.</p>\r\n<p>At the end of the day return back to your hotel.</p>'),
(3160, 582, 'fr', 'Excursion d\'une journée à Memphis Sakkara et Dahchour', '<p>Avec notre repr&eacute;sentant, vous ferez une merveilleuse visite pour d&eacute;couvrir Saqqarah, o&ugrave; nous visiterons le plus ancien b&acirc;timent en pierre de l\'histoire. Elle fut construite par l\'ing&eacute;nieur Imhotep pour le roi Dj&eacute;ser, fondateur de la Troisi&egrave;me Dynastie. En plus d\'appr&eacute;cier la visite de la pyramide du roi Teti de la VIe dynastie, cette pyramide se caract&eacute;rise par la pr&eacute;sence sur ses murs de textes des pyramides, qui sont des textes magiques pour aider le d&eacute;funt dans son voyage sacr&eacute; dans l\'autre monde. puis visite de la tombe du ministre (Mre Roca), puis visite de Memphis, la premi&egrave;re capitale &eacute;gyptienne antique &agrave; voir la plus grande statue du plus grand roi de l\'histoire de l\'&Eacute;gypte ancienne, le roi Rams&egrave;s II. Ensuite, d&eacute;placez-vous imm&eacute;diatement pour visiter le Dahshur o&ugrave; se trouvent deux grandes pyramides datant de l\'&eacute;poque de la Quatri&egrave;me Dynastie et elles ont &eacute;t&eacute; construites par le roi Sneferu, le p&egrave;re du roi Kh&eacute;ops, et les pyramides ont &eacute;t&eacute; construites en calcaire.</p>\r\n<p>En fin de journ&eacute;e, retour &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel.</p>'),
(3161, 582, 'de', 'Tagestour Memphis Sakkara und Dahshur', '<p>Mit unserem Vertreter unternehmen Sie eine wundervolle Tour zur Entdeckung von Saqqara, wo wir das &auml;lteste Steingeb&auml;ude der Geschichte besichtigen werden. Es wurde vom Ingenieur Imhotep f&uuml;r K&ouml;nig Djoser, den Gr&uuml;nder der Dritten Dynastie, erbaut. Neben dem Besuch der Pyramide von K&ouml;nig Teti aus der sechsten Dynastie zeichnet sich diese Pyramide durch die Pr&auml;senz von Texten der Pyramiden an ihren W&auml;nden aus, bei denen es sich um magische Texte handelt, die dem Verstorbenen auf seiner heiligen Reise in die andere Welt helfen sollen. Dann besuchen Sie das Grab des Ministers (Mre Roca) und besuchen dann Memphis, die erste alt&auml;gyptische Hauptstadt, in der die gr&ouml;&szlig;te Statue des gr&ouml;&szlig;ten K&ouml;nigs in der Geschichte des alten &Auml;gypten, K&ouml;nig Ramses II., zu sehen ist. Dann machen Sie sich sofort auf den Weg, um Dahshur zu besuchen, wo sich zwei gro&szlig;e Pyramiden aus der Zeit der vierten Dynastie befinden. Sie wurden von K&ouml;nig Sneferu, dem Vater von K&ouml;nig Khufu, erbaut und die Pyramiden wurden aus Kalkstein gebaut.</p>\r\n<p>Am Ende des Tages kehren Sie zu Ihrem Hotel zur&uuml;ck.</p>'),
(3162, 582, 'it', 'Tour di un giorno Memphis Sakkara e Dahshur', '<p>Con il nostro rappresentante, farai un meraviglioso tour alla scoperta di Saqqara, dove visiteremo l\'edificio in pietra pi&ugrave; antico della storia. Fu costruito dall\'ingegnere Imhotep per il re Djoser, fondatore della Terza Dinastia. Oltre a visitare la piramide del re Teti della sesta dinastia, questa piramide &egrave; caratterizzata dalla presenza sulle sue pareti dei testi delle piramidi, che sono testi magici per aiutare il defunto nel suo sacro viaggio nell\'altro mondo. poi visitando la tomba del Ministro (Mre Roca) e poi spostandoci a visitare Menfi, la prima antica capitale egiziana a vedere la pi&ugrave; grande statua del pi&ugrave; grande re della storia dell\'antico Egitto, il re Ramses II. Quindi spostati immediatamente per visitare Dahshur dove ci sono due grandi piramidi risalenti all\'era della Quarta Dinastia e furono costruite dal re Sneferu, il padre del re Khufu, e le piramidi furono costruite in pietra calcarea.</p>\r\n<p>Alla fine della giornata, torna al tuo hotel.</p>'),
(3163, 582, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3164, 582, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3165, 582, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3166, 583, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Your adventure begins at morning as our expert guide whisks you away from your hotel to the awe-inspiring Step Pyramid of Zoser. Marvel at the world\'s earliest colossal stone monument, erected during the 3rd Dynasty for the venerable King Zoser.</p>\r\n<p>Your odyssey continues to Dahshur, where you\'ll step inside the Red Pyramid, hailed as history\'s inaugural true pyramid. Gaze upon the Bent Pyramid, renowned for its remarkable preservation. These architectural wonders offer a glimpse into the ingenuity of ancient builders.</p>\r\n<p>Next, we transport you to the storied city of Memphis, established by the illustrious King Menes. Once the heart of Egyptian rule and culture, Memphis thrived as the nation\'s capital for over three millennia. Here, we stand in the presence of the colossal Statue of Ramses II and the enigmatic alabaster Sphinx, symbols of a civilization that has captivated the world.</p>\r\n<p>Join us for an unforgettable day as we explore the grandeur of Egypt\'s storied past, bringing history to life with tales of pharaohs and pyramids. This is more than a tour; it\'s a passage through time, where every moment is a treasure waiting to be discovered. Take advantage of this opportunity to witness the most incredible ancient sites near Cairo in a single day. Secure your spot on this epic voyage into history with <strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(3167, 583, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3168, 583, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3169, 583, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3170, 583, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3171, 583, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3172, 583, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3173, 584, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p>Embark on a timeless journey with <strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>, where our expert guide will whisk you away from your hotel to the awe-inspiring</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Giza Pyramids Complex</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Giza Pyramids Complex</strong>, is home to three of the most iconic pyramids: the Great Pyramid of Khufu, the Pyramid of Khafre, and the Pyramid of Menkaure. Built during the Fourth Dynasty around 2600 BCE, these pyramids served as monumental tombs for the pharaohs. The complex also includes the Great Sphinx, a massive limestone statue with the body of a lion and the head of a pharaoh.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Great Pyramid</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Great Pyramid</strong>, also known as the Pyramid of Khufu or Cheops, is the largest and oldest of the three pyramids in the Giza Pyramids Complex. Built around 2580-2560 BCE during the Fourth Dynasty, it originally stood at 481 feet tall and was the tallest man-made structure in the world for over 3,800 years. Constructed from millions of limestone blocks, the Great Pyramid was built as a tomb for Pharaoh Khufu. It remains one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World and is a remarkable example of ancient Egyptian engineering and architectural prowess.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The&nbsp;</strong><strong>Great&nbsp;</strong><strong>Sphinx of Chephren</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Great Sphinx</strong>&nbsp;of Chephren, also known as the Great Sphinx of&nbsp;<strong>Giza</strong>, is a monumental limestone statue located near the Giza Pyramids in Egypt. Believed to have been carved during the reign of Pharaoh Khafre (Chephren) around 2500 BCE, the Sphinx features the body of a lion and the head of a pharaoh, likely representing Khafre himself. Measuring about 240 feet in length and 66 feet in height, the Great Sphinx is one of the most iconic&nbsp;<strong>symbols of ancient Egypt</strong>.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Valley Temple</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Valley Temple, is an ancient Egyptian structure dating back to approximately 2500 BCE. Constructed for Pharaoh Khafre, the temple was primarily used for mummification and ceremonial purification. It is renowned for its impressive architecture, featuring massive limestone blocks and granite pillars that showcase the grandeur and precision of ancient Egyptian craftsmanship.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Saqqara Step Pyramid</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Saqqara Step Pyramid</strong>, with its six towering steps reaching towards the heavens, stands at a height of 62 meters and is the earliest large-scale stone construction, built for King Djoser. This remarkable pyramid marks the beginning of the golden era of pyramid construction in ancient Egypt, laying the foundation for the grand monuments that would follow.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Lunch Time</strong></p>\r\n<p>Enjoy a delightful lunch at a local restaurant in Cairo, then continue your&nbsp;<strong>Full Day Tour To Giza Pyramids, Memphis, Sakkara and Dahshur</strong>. With your private guide to visit:</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Memphis City</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>Memphis</strong>&nbsp;City, was Egypt\'s ancient capital founded around 3100 BCE. It served as a major political and cultural hub with notable temples, including the Temple of Ptah. Today, it&rsquo;s an archaeological site with significant&nbsp;<strong>artifacts</strong>, including a colossal statue of Ramses II and the Alabaster Sphinx.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Dahshur Pyramids</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Dahshur Pyramids, south of Cairo, include the&nbsp;<strong>Bent Pyramid</strong>&nbsp;and the Red Pyramid, built by Pharaoh Snefru. The Bent Pyramid is notable for its unique shape, while the Red Pyramid is the first successful smooth-sided pyramid. These pyramids are significant in the evolution of pyramid architecture.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Book with us</strong>&nbsp;for an unparalleled exploration of Egypt\'s ancient wonders, where every step is a story and every monument a memory etched in stone.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>With <strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>, your journey into the heart of history begins.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(3174, 584, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3175, 584, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3176, 584, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3177, 584, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3178, 584, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3179, 584, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3180, 585, 'en', NULL, NULL),
(3181, 585, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3182, 585, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3183, 585, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3184, 585, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3185, 585, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3186, 585, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3187, 586, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Pharaoh Vibes Tours guide will pick up you from your Hotel to visit&nbsp;<strong>Old Cairo</strong>&nbsp;that known as&nbsp;<strong>Christian Coptic Cairo</strong>&nbsp;which is Among the most important locations visited by the Holy Family where the spiritual impact of their presence is most felt still; though their stay was brief, for the Governor of what was then Fustat enraged by the tumbling down of idols at Jesus&rsquo; approach sought to kill the Child. But they took shelter from his wrath in a cave above which, in later years, the Church of Abu Serga (St Sergious) was built. This, and the whole area of the Fort of Babylon, is a destination of pilgrimage not only for the Egyptians but for Christians from around the world. An air of piety and devotion pervades the whole district there. Also There you will be able to visit and Enter the Church of Abu-Sergah and St. Barbara, the&nbsp;<strong>hanging church.</strong></p>\r\n<p>Visit The Famous Cave Church of St. Simon in Cairo There are seven cave churches carved into the nearby Moqattam Mountain. The Monastery of St. Simon the Tanner is the largest and has an amphitheater with a seating capacity of 20,000. It is worth a visit if you are interesting to see something different in Egypt. after that return back to your Hotel.</p>'),
(3188, 586, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3189, 586, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3190, 586, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3191, 586, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3192, 586, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3193, 586, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3194, 587, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p data-start=\"106\" data-end=\"667\">Your evening begins with a pickup from your hotel before heading to the iconic Cairo Tower, where you&rsquo;ll enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of the city illuminated at night. Next, stroll through the lively lanes of Khan El Khalili Bazaar, soaking in the vibrant atmosphere and browsing its countless treasures. The experience continues with your choice of either a serene felucca ride on the Nile under the stars or a romantic horse-drawn carriage ride through the city&rsquo;s charming streets. At the end of the tour, you&rsquo;ll be comfortably returned to your hotel.</p>'),
(3195, 587, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3196, 587, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3197, 587, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3198, 587, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
