(3240, 593, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3241, 593, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3242, 593, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3243, 594, 'en', 'Day 1:', '<p>We will pick you up from your hotel in Cairo, where you&rsquo;ll meet your private tour guide. Together, in a comfortable air-conditioned vehicle, you\'ll embark on your&nbsp;<strong>Egyptian Museum, Citadel And Khan Khalili Bazaar tour</strong>, beginning with a visit to:</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Egyptian Museum</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>The Egyptian Museum</strong>&nbsp;in Cairo houses one of the world&rsquo;s largest collections of ancient&nbsp;<strong>Egyptian artifacts</strong>. Established in 1902, it showcases over 120,000 items, including statues, jewelry, and mummies.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Citadel of Salah El Din</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Citadel of Salah El Din, is a historic fortress built in the 12th century by Salah El Din (Saladin) to defend against Crusaders. The citadel served as Egypt&rsquo;s seat of government for over 700 years. It houses several important buildings, including the impressive Mohamed Ali Mosque. The Citadel offers stunning views of Cairo and is a significant symbol of Egypt\'s medieval history.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Mohamed Ali Mosque</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Mohamed Ali Mosque, Built between 1830 and 1848 by Mohamed Ali Pasha, the mosque is named for its extensive use of alabaster in its interior and exterior. It features a large central dome, two towering minarets, and intricate Ottoman-style architecture.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Khan El Khalili Bazaar</strong></h2>\r\n<p><strong>Khan El Khalili Bazaar</strong>, located in the heart of Islamic&nbsp;<strong>Cairo</strong>, is one of the city&rsquo;s oldest and most famous markets. Dating back to the 14th century, this bustling bazaar is filled with narrow alleys lined with shops selling everything from spices, jewelry, and textiles to traditional crafts and souvenirs. Visitors can also enjoy authentic Egyptian food at local cafes.</p>\r\n<p>As your day of exploration concludes, we&rsquo;ll ensure your safe return to your hotel. With&nbsp;<strong>Pharaoh Vibes Tours</strong>&nbsp;every journey is a doorway into the heart of Egypt&rsquo;s vibrant history and culture.&nbsp;<strong>Join us</strong> for an experience that will leave you with memories to cherish!</p>'),
