INSERT INTO `tour_day_translations` (`id`, `tour_day_id`, `locale`, `title`, `description`) VALUES
(3285, 600, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Pharaoh Vibes Tours beckons you to a majestic journey through the beginning of time. Your private tour guide will collect you from your Cairo hotel and set you out to the iconic Giza Plateau.<br><br>Here, the Pyramids of Cheops, Chephren, and Mykerinus rise from the sands, a testament to ancient ambition and ingenuity. Stand in awe at the Great Sphinx, Chephren\'s guardian, whose enigmatic visage has stirred the imaginations of travelers for centuries.<br><br>Your exploration continues at the Valley Temple, a site of profound significance. It was here that the pharaohs\' mummies underwent purification and mummification, rituals as essential to their journey to the afterlife as the pyramids themselves.<br><br>Behold the Seven Wonders of the World, where the 5000-year-old necropolis awaits. The Great Pyramids, a marvel of human achievement, stand as sentinels to history, watched over by the vigilant Sphinx. This is not merely a tour; it is a pilgrimage to the heart of Egypt\'s grandeur, a must-see for every wanderer of the world. With Pharaoh Vibes Tours, the past is not just to be seen, but to be experienced.&nbsp;</p>'),
(3286, 600, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3287, 600, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3288, 600, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3289, 600, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3290, 600, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3291, 600, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3292, 601, 'en', 'Tour Itinerary', '<p>Pick up with your expert Bird Guide from your departure point and transferred on to a traditional felucca sailboat at the dockside in Aswan. You will set sail across the Nile from the East Bank to the West Bank of the Nile towards Lord Kitchener\'s Island. From here, your Guide will start pointing out the locations of where you will see the birdlife ranging from Egrets both adult and chicks, to Parakeets amongst the trees. Whilst passing along the Island, there is beautiful flora and fauna such as Hibiscus, lantana, bougainvillea, Poinciana, acacia trees and mimosa all blooming in radiant colors.</p>\r\n<p>Sailing up river towards the Mausoleum of the Aga Khan, you may be astounded at the sight of many more bird species wading in the waters of the Cataract Islands such as Kingfishers, Malachite Kingfishers, Striated Herons, Little Bitten Herons, Night Herons, along with Little Green Bee Eaters, and Nile Valley Sunbirds. A truly delightful tour for nature lovers. at the end you will Return to the dock in Aswan and transferred to your original pick up point.</p>'),
(3293, 601, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3294, 601, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3295, 601, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3296, 601, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3297, 601, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3298, 601, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3299, 602, 'en', 'Tour Itinerary', '<div class=\"flex flex-col text-sm\">\r\n<section class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" data-turn-id=\"request-WEB:3b166c7b-2c9e-41f9-82b4-e0e1fdf274da-0\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-2\" data-scroll-anchor=\"true\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\">\r\n<div class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"0\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"04bda359-08da-4137-8051-40483c334e2f\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-4-thinking\" data-turn-start-message=\"true\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\r\n<div class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word light markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<p data-start=\"44\" data-end=\"637\" data-is-only-node=\"\">Begin your day before sunrise with hotel pickup and transfer to the launch site, where you will enjoy a light refreshment while watching the hot air balloon being prepared. After a short safety briefing, board the balloon and gently rise into the morning sky for a breathtaking flight, taking in panoramic views of the landscape as the sun comes up. Upon landing, celebrate the experience with a traditional toast and commemorative certificate before returning to your hotel. The rest of the morning can be spent at leisure, giving you time to relax and reflect on the unforgettable adventure.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>'),
(3300, 602, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3301, 602, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3302, 602, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3303, 602, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3304, 602, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3305, 602, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3306, 603, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Aswan excursion and Day Tour to visit main highlights of the city to visit the unfinished Oblisk, Philae temple and High Dam. Then proceed Shallal to take a motor boat and visit the&nbsp;Philae temple&nbsp;devoted to God Isis. After the building of the&nbsp;High Dam the temple was dismantled and reconstructed in its present location in Agilika Island. You will end your tour by visiting the High Dam which was constructed to save Egypt from the Nile River flooding.</p>\r\n<p>You will be taken along the road past the Fatimid Cemetery to the&nbsp;Unfinished Obelisk which is a curious sight where a huge obelisk is perfectly shaped on three sides but the fourth side is still attached to the rock bed. It was abandoned after a flaw was discovered on the rock.</p>\r\n<p>Philae Temple, originally located on Philae Island, is&nbsp;a complex of ancient Egyptian temples dedicated to the goddess Isis and other deities.&nbsp;Due to flooding from the Aswan High Dam, the temple complex was relocated to Agilkia Island.&nbsp;It\'s known for its well-preserved structures, including the Temple of Isis, the&nbsp;Kiosk of Trajan,&nbsp;and the&nbsp;Temple of Hathor.&nbsp;</p>'),
(3307, 603, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3308, 603, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3309, 603, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3310, 603, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3311, 603, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3312, 603, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3313, 604, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>In&nbsp;Abu Simbel, there exists one of the most famous ancient Egyptian monuments.&nbsp; The temple of Ramses II with his four massive Colossi adorning the entrance of the temple. The temple was marked as a convey of Egyptian supremacy for whoever intended to approach Egypt from the south. To the north of the temple is the smaller temple of Hathor, which was built in honor of Ramses&rsquo; wife Nefertari. Both these temples are the best-known archeological sites of Egypt. The huge sandstone statues carved into the temple facades and the decorated interiors with art and hieroglyphics should not be missed.</p>\r\n<p>The Abu Simbel Temples were originally carved into solid rock cliffs, but UNESCO relocated the temples in the 1960s after the building of the Aswan High Dam to save them from inundation. They are now present near the banks of Lake Nasser. Our Abu Simbel tour begins from the city of Aswan, after your tour to Abu Simbel, you will return to your hotel.</p>\r\n<p>with daily departures about 5:00 am. Transfer to Abu Simbel which is approximately three and half hours from Aswan.&nbsp;</p>'),
(3314, 604, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3315, 604, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3316, 604, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3317, 604, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3318, 604, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3319, 604, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3320, 605, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>In the morning, an air-conditioned coach will pick you up at your hotel in Aswan.&nbsp;Accompanied by a guide, you will be taken to the&nbsp;Kom Ombo Temple&nbsp;, located on the Nile about 50 km north of Aswan.</p>\r\n<p>Built in the Greco-Roman era, Kom Ombo is home to an unusual double temple. The temple on the right is dedicated to the crocodile god, Sobek, while the temple on the left was in honor of Haroeris. Each temple has its own entrance, courtyard, halls and shrine. The temple is supposed to change color after the sunset.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Further on, go to the&nbsp;Temple of Edfu&nbsp;built in sandstone during the Ptolemaic period.&nbsp;The temple is dedicated to the falcon god, Horus.&nbsp;It is the best preserved temple in Egypt and beautifully constructed, offering wonderful use of natural sunlight.&nbsp;The temple contains a nilometer, windows and wells, including a variety of battle and religious inscriptions on the walls.&nbsp;Two statues of hawks are located at the entrance of the temple.&nbsp;The interior includes a library, a cloakroom, a laboratory, a treasure room, a hall, a sanctuary and other rooms.</p>\r\n<p>After exploring the temple sites, you will return to your hotel in Aswan.</p>'),
(3321, 605, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3322, 605, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3323, 605, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3324, 605, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3325, 605, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3326, 605, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3327, 606, 'en', 'Explore Giza', '<p>Vive Egiptos <span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Sun Pyramids Tours beckons you to a majestic journey through the beginning of time. Your private tour guide will collect you from your Cairo hotel and set you out to the iconic Giza Plateau. \\n\\nHere, the Pyramids of Cheops, Chephren, and Mykerinus rise from the sands, a testament to ancient ambition and ingenuity. Stand in awe at the Great Sphinx, Chephren\'s guardian, whose enigmatic visage has stirred the imaginations of travelers for centuries.\\n\\nYour exploration continues at the Valley Temple, a site of profound significance. It was here that the pharaohs\' mummies underwent purification and mummification, rituals as essential to their journey to the afterlife as the pyramids themselves.\\n\\nBehold the Seven Wonders of the World, where the 5000-year-old necropolis awaits. The Great Pyramids, a marvel of human achievement, stand as sentinels to history, watched over by the vigilant Sphinx. This is not merely a tour; it is a pilgrimage to the heart of Egypt\'s grandeur, a must-see for every wanderer of the world. With Sun Pyramids Tours, the past is not just to be seen, but to be experienced. &quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:9153,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;9&quot;:1,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">beckons you to a majestic journey through the beginning of time. Your private tour guide will collect you from your Cairo hotel and set you out to the iconic Giza Plateau.<br><br>Here, the Pyramids of Cheops, Chephren, and Mykerinus rise from the sands, a testament to ancient ambition and ingenuity. Stand in awe at the Great Sphinx, Chephren\'s guardian, whose enigmatic visage has stirred the imaginations of travelers for centuries.<br><br>Your exploration continues at the Valley Temple, a site of profound significance. It was here that the pharaohs\' mummies underwent purification and mummification, rituals as essential to their journey to the afterlife as the pyramids themselves.<br><br>Behold the Seven Wonders of the World, where the 5000-year-old necropolis awaits. The Great Pyramids, a marvel of human achievement, stand as sentinels to history, watched over by the vigilant Sphinx. This is not merely a tour; it is a pilgrimage to the heart of Egypt\'s grandeur, a must-see for every wanderer of the world. With Vive Egiptos, the past is not just to be seen, but to be experienced.&nbsp;</span></p>'),
(3328, 606, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3329, 606, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3330, 606, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3331, 606, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3332, 606, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3333, 606, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3334, 607, 'en', 'ARRIVAL - FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will&nbsp;assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we&nbsp;will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local&nbsp;surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(3335, 607, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3336, 607, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3337, 607, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3338, 607, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3339, 607, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3340, 607, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3341, 608, 'en', 'THE PYRAMIDS OF GIZA, THE GREAT SPHINX, LUNCH, GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After Breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to visit the Pyramids and the Sphinx, which are the only surviving&nbsp;wonder of the ancient world. You will have the option to enjoy a memorable camel ride in the vicinity of these magnificent&nbsp;structures. Ahead of the pyramids, lies the Sphinx known as the guardian of the pyramids facing the sun every morning as it&nbsp;rises from the east. Lunch will then be served at a local hygienic restaurant. Proceeding to The Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)&nbsp;will host over 100,000 artifacts from ancient Egyptian civilization, many pieces are displayed for the first time<br><br><strong>SATURDAY,31TH OF JULY 2027 - Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(3342, 608, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3343, 608, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3344, 608, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3345, 608, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3346, 608, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3347, 608, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3348, 609, 'en', 'VALLEY OF KINGS, QUEEN HATSHEPSUT MORTURY TEMPLE, COLOSSI OF MEMNON', '<p>After having breakfast, After Breakfast, you will catch your flight to Luxor. Check in your Hotel. Next, you will be taken to the West Bank and&nbsp;visit The Valley of Kings the home Egypt most known Pharoahs. The tour covers the special visit of 5 tombs including the Golden Pharaoh&nbsp;Tutankhamun&rsquo;s tomb and Ramesses VI. Then we head to visit Queen Hatshepsut&rsquo;s magnificant Mortuary Temple built 3300 years ago; a&nbsp;unique temple that is engraved by the mountains and partially carved out of the rocks. After that visit Colossi of Memnon,Two towering&nbsp;statues of Pharaoh Amenhotep III, standing 18 meters high, built to guard the entrance of his lost mortuary temple. They are among the&nbsp;most iconic landmarks on Luxor&rsquo;s west bank.</p>\r\n<p><strong>SUNDAY,1ST OF AUGUST 2027 - Overnight in Luxor</strong></p>'),
(3349, 609, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3350, 609, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3351, 609, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3352, 609, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3353, 609, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3354, 609, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3355, 610, 'en', 'KARNAK TEMPLE & LUXOR TEMPLE - MONDAY,2ND OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>In the Morning: Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple, A special chance to witness the total solar eclipse from Karnak Temple. Watching&nbsp;this rare event from such a historic place will be a truly unforgettable experience.<br>Proceeding our tour to Luxor Temple in which you&rsquo;ll stand in the shadows of the Great Ramses II colossi</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Luxor .</strong></p>'),
(3356, 610, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3357, 610, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3358, 610, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3359, 610, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3360, 610, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3361, 610, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3362, 611, 'en', 'CHECK OUT - FLY BACK TO CAIRO, FINAL DEPARTURE - TUESDAY,3RD OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out from your Hotel.<br>Catch our flight back to Cairo. catch your international flight.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Final Departure</strong></p>'),
(3363, 611, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3364, 611, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3365, 611, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3366, 611, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3367, 611, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3368, 611, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3369, 612, 'en', 'KARNAK TEMPLE & LUXOR TEMPLE - MONDAY,2ND OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>In the Morning: Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple, A special chance to witness the total solar eclipse from Karnak Temple. Watching<br>this rare event from such a historic place will be a truly unforgettable experience.<br>Proceeding our tour to Luxor Temple in which you&rsquo;ll stand in the shadows of the Great Ramses II colossi.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Luxor .</strong></p>'),
(3370, 612, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3371, 612, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3372, 612, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3373, 612, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3374, 612, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3375, 612, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3376, 613, 'en', 'VALLEY OF KINGS, QUEEN HATSHEPSUT MORTURY TEMPLE, COLOSSI OF MEMNON', '<p>After having breakfast, you will be taken to the West Bank and visit The Valley of Kings the home Egypt most known Pharoahs. The tour&nbsp;covers the special visit of 5 tombs including the Golden Pharaoh Tutankhamun&rsquo;s tomb and Ramesses VI. Then we head to visit Queen<br>Hatshepsut&rsquo;s magnificant Mortuary Temple built 3300 years ago; a unique temple that is engraved by the mountains and partially carved&nbsp;out of the rocks. After that visit Colossi of Memnon,Two towering statues of Pharaoh Amenhotep III, standing 18 meters high, built to guard&nbsp;the entrance of his lost mortuary temple. They are among the most iconic landmarks on Luxor&rsquo;s west bank.<br><strong>SUNDAY,1ST OF AUGUST 2027</strong><br><strong>Overnight in Luxor</strong></p>'),
(3377, 613, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3378, 613, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3379, 613, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3380, 613, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3381, 613, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3382, 613, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3383, 614, 'en', 'KOMOMBO TEMPLE & EDFU TEMPLE - SATURDAY,31TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>After having breakfast, we will transfer to Luxor by car. Next will visit Kom Ombo Temple, a very unusual temple. It\'s<br>uniqueness is for several reasons. It is dedication to two different deities, the local crocodile-headed god, Sobek, and the<br>falcon-headed god Horus. After that we will visit Edfu Temple . Considered to be one of the best preserved temples from<br>ancient Egypt, It is the largest temple dedicated to the god Horus.<br><br><strong>Overnight in Luxor</strong></p>'),
(3384, 614, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3385, 614, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3386, 614, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3387, 614, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3388, 614, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3389, 614, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3390, 615, 'en', 'ABU SIMBEL - FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will be transferred to Abu Simbel where you will be standing in front of a<br>temple carved in the mountain; a true miracle of ancient and modern engineering that<br>deserves to be counted among the wonders of the world.<br>back to Aswan.<br><br><strong>Overnight in Aswan.</strong></p>'),
(3391, 615, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3392, 615, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3393, 615, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3394, 615, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3395, 615, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3396, 615, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3397, 616, 'en', 'THURSDAY,29TH OF JULY 2027 - FLY TO ASWAN, PHILAE TEMPLE, HIGH DAM', '<p>After Breakfast, you will catch your flight to Aswan . Check in your Hotel.<br>Next, you will visit Philae Temple also referred to as the Temple of Lovers which narrates the most ancient love story in&nbsp;history between Isis and Osiris. After that visit The High Dam, a rock fill dam across the River Nile at Aswan, completed&nbsp;in 1970 (and formally inaugurated in January 1971) The dam is 364 feet (111 meters) high, with a crest length of 12,562&nbsp;feet (3,830 meters) and a volume of 57,940,000 cubic yards (44,300,000 cubic meters), impounds a reservoir, Lake&nbsp;Nasser, that has a gross capacity of 5.97 trillion cubic feet (169 billion cubic meters.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Aswan</strong></p>'),
(3398, 616, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3399, 616, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3400, 616, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3401, 616, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3402, 616, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3403, 616, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3404, 617, 'en', 'THE PYRAMIDS OF GIZA, THE GREAT SPHINX, LUNCH, GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After Breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to visit the Pyramids and the Sphinx, which are the only surviving<br>wonder of the ancient world. You will have the option to enjoy a memorable camel ride in the vicinity of these magnificent<br>structures. Ahead of the pyramids, lies the Sphinx known as the guardian of the pyramids facing the sun every morning as it<br>rises from the east. Lunch will then be served at a local hygienic restaurant. Proceeding to The Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)<br>will host over 100,000 artifacts from ancient Egyptian civilization, many pieces are displayed for the first time.<br><br><strong>WEDNESDAY,28TH OF JULY 2027 - Overnight in Cairo</strong></p>'),
(3405, 617, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3406, 617, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3407, 617, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3408, 617, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3409, 617, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3410, 617, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3411, 618, 'en', 'Day 1 CAIRO BY NIGHT TUESDAY,27TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will&nbsp;assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we&nbsp;will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local&nbsp;surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey.<br><br><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(3412, 618, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3413, 618, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3414, 618, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3415, 618, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3416, 618, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3417, 618, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3418, 619, 'en', 'CHECK OUT - FLY BACK TO CAIRO, FINAL DEPARTURE - TUESDAY,3RD OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out from your Hotel.<br>Catch our flight back to Cairo. catch your international flight.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Final Departure</strong></p>'),
(3419, 619, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3420, 619, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3421, 619, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3422, 619, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3423, 619, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3424, 619, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3425, 620, 'en', 'Uncover the Mysteries of Kom Ombo and Edfu', '<p>Awaken to a delicious breakfast on board as we set sail for Kom Ombo. Here, you&rsquo;ll have the chance to explore the unique Temple of Sobek and Haeroris, a testament to the region&rsquo;s ancient religious practices. After a delightful lunch on board, we continue our journey to Edfu. Enjoy a sumptuous dinner on board and rest in the comfort of your cabin in Edfu. Meals : breakfast Lunch &amp; Dinner</p>'),
(3426, 620, 'fr', 'Découvrez les mystères de Kom Ombo et d\'Edfou', '<p>R&eacute;veillez-vous avec un d&eacute;licieux petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord alors que nous embarquons pour Kom Ombo. Ici, vous aurez l&rsquo;occasion d&rsquo;explorer le temple unique de Sobek et Haeroris, t&eacute;moignage des anciennes pratiques religieuses de la r&eacute;gion. Apr&egrave;s un d&eacute;licieux d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord, nous continuons notre voyage vers Edfou. Profitez d\'un somptueux d&icirc;ner &agrave; bord et reposez-vous dans le confort de votre cabine &agrave; Edfou. Repas : petit d&eacute;jeuner D&eacute;jeuner &amp; D&icirc;ner</p>'),
(3427, 620, 'de', 'Entdecken Sie die Geheimnisse von Kom Ombo und Edfu', '<p>Erwachen Sie mit einem k&ouml;stlichen Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord, w&auml;hrend wir nach Kom Ombo segeln. Hier haben Sie die M&ouml;glichkeit, den einzigartigen Tempel von Sobek und Haeroris zu erkunden, ein Zeugnis der alten religi&ouml;sen Praktiken der Region. Nach einem k&ouml;stlichen Mittagessen an Bord setzen wir unsere Reise nach Edfu fort. Genie&szlig;en Sie ein &uuml;ppiges Abendessen an Bord und ruhen Sie sich im Komfort Ihrer Kabine in Edfu aus. Mahlzeiten: Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck, Mittag- und Abendessen</p>'),
(3428, 620, 'it', 'Scopri i misteri di Kom Ombo e Edfu', '<p>Svegliati con una deliziosa colazione a bordo mentre salpiamo per Kom Ombo. Qui avrai la possibilit&agrave; di esplorare l\'esclusivo Tempio di Sobek e Haeroris, una testimonianza delle antiche pratiche religiose della regione. Dopo un delizioso pranzo a bordo, continuiamo il nostro viaggio verso Edfu. Goditi una sontuosa cena a bordo e riposa nel comfort della tua cabina a Edfu. Pasti: colazione, pranzo e cena</p>'),
(3429, 620, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3430, 620, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3431, 620, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3432, 621, 'en', 'Discover the Wonders of Aswan', '<p>Your adventure begins at Aswan Airport/Railway Station, where our team will greet you and escort you to your Nile Cruise aboard the cruise. Settle into your comfortable cabin before lunch, then prepare to immerse yourself in the rich culture of Aswan. Marvel at the engineering feat of the High Dam, explore the enchanting Philae Temple and witness the grandeur of the unfinished obelisk. As the day winds down, savor a delicious dinner on board and rest up for the next day&rsquo;s adventures in your cozy cabin.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Meals : Lunch &amp; Dinner</p>'),
(3433, 621, 'fr', 'Découvrez les merveilles d\'Assouan', '<p>Votre aventure commence &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport/gare d\'Assouan, o&ugrave; notre &eacute;quipe vous accueillera et vous accompagnera jusqu\'&agrave; votre croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil &agrave; bord de la croisi&egrave;re. Installez-vous dans votre cabine confortable avant le d&eacute;jeuner, puis pr&eacute;parez-vous &agrave; vous immerger dans la riche culture d\'Assouan. &Eacute;merveillez-vous devant l\'exploit d\'ing&eacute;nierie du haut barrage, explorez le magnifique temple de Philae et admirez la grandeur de l\'ob&eacute;lisque inachev&eacute;. &Agrave; la fin de la journ&eacute;e, savourez un d&eacute;licieux d&icirc;ner &agrave; bord et reposez-vous pour les aventures du lendemain dans votre cabine confortable.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Repas : D&eacute;jeuner et D&icirc;ner</p>'),
(3434, 621, 'de', 'Entdecken Sie die Wunder von Assuan', '<p>Ihr Abenteuer beginnt am Flughafen/Bahnhof Assuan, wo unser Team Sie begr&uuml;&szlig;t und Sie an Bord der Kreuzfahrt zu Ihrer Nilkreuzfahrt begleitet. Machen Sie es sich vor dem Mittagessen in Ihrer komfortablen Kabine gem&uuml;tlich und bereiten Sie sich darauf vor, in die reiche Kultur Assuans einzutauchen. Bewundern Sie die technische Meisterleistung des High Dam, erkunden Sie den bezaubernden Philae-Tempel und werden Sie Zeuge der Pracht des unvollendeten Obelisken. Lassen Sie den Tag ausklingen, genie&szlig;en Sie ein k&ouml;stliches Abendessen an Bord und ruhen Sie sich in Ihrer gem&uuml;tlichen Kabine f&uuml;r die Abenteuer des n&auml;chsten Tages aus.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Mahlzeiten: Mittag- und Abendessen</p>'),
(3435, 621, 'it', 'Scopri le meraviglie di Assuan', '<p>La tua avventura inizia all\'aeroporto/stazione ferroviaria di Aswan, dove il nostro team ti accoglier&agrave; e ti accompagner&agrave; alla tua crociera sul Nilo a bordo della crociera. Sistemati nella tua comoda cabina prima di pranzo, quindi preparati a immergerti nella ricca cultura di Assuan. Lasciati stupire dall\'impresa ingegneristica dell\'Alta Diga, esplora l\'incantevole Tempio di Philae e assisti alla grandiosit&agrave; dell\'obelisco incompiuto. Mentre la giornata volge al termine, assapora una deliziosa cena a bordo e riposati per le avventure del giorno successivo nella tua accogliente cabina.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Pasti: pranzo e cena</p>'),
(3436, 621, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3437, 621, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3438, 621, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3439, 622, 'en', 'Experience the Magic of Luxor’s East Bank', '<p>Rise early for morning tea and coffee before embarking on an adventure to the Temple of Horus in Edfu. Return to the cruise for a hearty breakfast as we sail towards Luxor via Esna. In Luxor, you&rsquo;ll have the opportunity to visit the awe-inspiring Karnak and Luxor Temples on the East Bank. After an afternoon tea on board, enjoy a delectable dinner and a lively Galabeya Party show. Overnight in Luxor, the city of palaces. Meals : breakfast Lunch &amp; Dinner</p>'),
(3440, 622, 'fr', 'Découvrez la magie de la rive est de Louxor', '<p>Levez-vous t&ocirc;t pour prendre le th&eacute; et le caf&eacute; du matin avant de vous lancer dans une aventure au temple d\'Horus &agrave; Edfou. Retour &agrave; la croisi&egrave;re pour un copieux petit-d&eacute;jeuner alors que nous naviguons vers Louxor via Esna. &Agrave; Louxor, vous aurez l&rsquo;occasion de visiter les impressionnants temples de Karnak et de Louxor sur la rive Est. Apr&egrave;s un th&eacute; l\'apr&egrave;s-midi &agrave; bord, savourez un d&eacute;licieux d&icirc;ner et un spectacle anim&eacute; de Galabeya Party. Nuit &agrave; Louxor, la ville des palais. Repas : petit d&eacute;jeuner D&eacute;jeuner &amp; D&icirc;ner</p>'),
(3441, 622, 'de', 'Erleben Sie den Zauber des Ostufers von Luxor', '<p>Stehen Sie fr&uuml;h auf, um morgens Tee und Kaffee zu trinken, bevor Sie sich auf ein Abenteuer zum Tempel des Horus in Edfu begeben. Kehren Sie f&uuml;r ein herzhaftes Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck zur Kreuzfahrt zur&uuml;ck, w&auml;hrend wir &uuml;ber Esna in Richtung Luxor segeln. In Luxor haben Sie die M&ouml;glichkeit, die beeindruckenden Karnak- und Luxor-Tempel am Ostufer zu besichtigen. Genie&szlig;en Sie nach einem Nachmittagstee an Bord ein k&ouml;stliches Abendessen und eine lebhafte Galabeya-Partyshow. &Uuml;bernachtung in Luxor, der Stadt der Pal&auml;ste. Mahlzeiten: Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck, Mittag- und Abendessen</p>'),
(3442, 622, 'it', 'Vivi la magia della sponda orientale di Luxor', '<p>Alzati presto per prendere il t&egrave; e il caff&egrave; mattutino prima di intraprendere un\'avventura al Tempio di Horus a Edfu. Ritorno alla crociera per un\'abbondante colazione mentre navighiamo verso Luxor via Esna. A Luxor avrai l\'opportunit&agrave; di visitare i maestosi templi di Karnak e Luxor sulla sponda orientale. Dopo un t&egrave; pomeridiano a bordo, goditi una cena deliziosa e un vivace spettacolo del Galabeya Party. Pernottamento a Luxor, la citt&agrave; dei palazzi. Pasti: colazione, pranzo e cena</p>'),
(3443, 622, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3444, 622, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3445, 622, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3446, 623, 'en', 'Farewell and Departure', '<p>Savor your final breakfast on board the cruise as we bid farewell to this unforgettable journey. Disembark after breakfast and continue your exploration of Luxor with a visit to the Valley of the Kings (three tombs only) and the majestic Queen Hatshepsut Temple, known as El-Deir El-Bahari. In the afternoon, our representative will accompany you to Luxor Airport/Railway Station for your onward journey. Meals : breakfast Note : if the mentioned cruises are not available, the company have the right to Change the Cruise as it of same category.</p>'),
(3447, 623, 'fr', 'Adieu et départ', '<p>Savourez votre dernier petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de la croisi&egrave;re alors que nous disons adieu &agrave; ce voyage inoubliable. D&eacute;barquez apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner et continuez votre exploration de Louxor avec une visite de la Vall&eacute;e des Rois (trois tombeaux seulement) et du majestueux temple de la reine Hatshepsout, connu sous le nom d\'El-Deir El-Bahari. Dans l\'apr&egrave;s-midi, notre repr&eacute;sentant vous accompagnera &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport/gare de Louxor pour la suite de votre voyage. Repas : petit-d&eacute;jeuner Remarque : si les croisi&egrave;res mentionn&eacute;es ne sont pas disponibles, la compagnie se r&eacute;serve le droit de modifier la croisi&egrave;re car elle est de m&ecirc;me cat&eacute;gorie.</p>'),
(3448, 623, 'de', 'Abschied und Abreise', '<p>Genie&szlig;en Sie Ihr letztes Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord der Kreuzfahrt, w&auml;hrend wir uns von dieser unvergesslichen Reise verabschieden. Gehen Sie nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck von Bord und setzen Sie Ihre Erkundung von Luxor mit einem Besuch des Tals der K&ouml;nige (nur drei Gr&auml;ber) und des majest&auml;tischen K&ouml;nigin-Hatschepsut-Tempels, bekannt als El-Deir El-Bahari, fort. Am Nachmittag begleitet Sie unser Vertreter zum Flughafen/Bahnhof Luxor f&uuml;r Ihre Weiterreise. Mahlzeiten: Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck. Hinweis: Wenn die genannten Kreuzfahrten nicht verf&uuml;gbar sind, hat das Unternehmen das Recht, die Kreuzfahrt in die gleiche Kategorie zu &auml;ndern.</p>'),
(3449, 623, 'it', 'Addio e partenza', '<p>Assapora la tua ultima colazione a bordo della crociera mentre salutiamo questo viaggio indimenticabile. Sbarco dopo colazione e continua la tua esplorazione di Luxor con una visita alla Valle dei Re (solo tre tombe) e al maestoso Tempio della Regina Hatshepsut, noto come El-Deir El-Bahari. Nel pomeriggio, il nostro rappresentante ti accompagner&agrave; all\'aeroporto/stazione ferroviaria di Luxor per il proseguimento del viaggio. Pasti: colazione Nota: se le crociere menzionate non sono disponibili, la compagnia si riserva il diritto di modificare la crociera assegnandola alla stessa categoria.</p>'),
(3450, 623, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3451, 623, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3452, 623, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3453, 624, 'en', 'ARRIVAL - FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will&nbsp;assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we&nbsp;will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local&nbsp;surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey<br><br><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(3454, 624, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3455, 624, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3456, 624, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3457, 624, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3458, 624, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3459, 624, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3460, 625, 'en', 'THE PYRAMIDS OF GIZA, THE GREAT SPHINX, LUNCH, GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After Breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to visit the Pyramids and the Sphinx, which are the only surviving&nbsp;wonder of the ancient world. You will have the option to enjoy a memorable camel ride in the vicinity of these magnificent&nbsp;structures. Ahead of the pyramids, lies the Sphinx known as the guardian of the pyramids facing the sun every morning as it&nbsp;rises from the east. Lunch will then be served at a local hygienic restaurant. Proceeding to The Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)&nbsp;will host over 100,000 artifacts from ancient Egyptian civilization, many pieces are displayed for the first time</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></p>'),
(3461, 625, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3462, 625, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3463, 625, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3464, 625, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3465, 625, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3466, 625, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3467, 626, 'en', 'FLY TO HURGHADA - SUNDAY,1 ST OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After Breakfast, you will catch your flight to Hurghada. Check in your Hotel.<br>Afternoon free time to enjoy the red sea</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Hurghada</strong></p>'),
(3468, 626, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3469, 626, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3470, 626, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3471, 626, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3472, 626, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3473, 626, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3474, 627, 'en', 'KARNAK TEMPLE & LUXOR TEMPLE - MONDAY,2ND OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>leave Hurghada in the early Morning, transfer to Luxor. Next, Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple, A special chance to witness the total&nbsp;solar eclipse from Karnak Temple. Watching this rare event from such a historic place will be a truly unforgettable experience.<br>Proceeding our tour to Luxor Temple in which you&rsquo;ll stand in the shadows of the Great Ramses II colossi.&nbsp;Back to Hurghada.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Hurghada</strong></p>'),
(3475, 627, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3476, 627, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3477, 627, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3478, 627, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3479, 627, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3480, 627, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3481, 628, 'en', 'FREE DAY - TUESDAY,3RD OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>free day at leisure.<br>optional activities: Snorkeling, diving, desert safari.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Overnight in Hurghada</strong></p>'),
(3482, 628, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3483, 628, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3484, 628, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3485, 628, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3486, 628, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3487, 628, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3488, 629, 'en', 'Day 1 : Cairo – Siwa.', '<p>Ready for Adventure!!! Early morning departure to Siwa Oasis our private limousine to Siwa oasis, The largest (23,000 habitants) &amp; most remote Egyptian Oasis lying some 17m below sea level.</p>\r\n<p>Crossing the Western Desert with a stop in AL alamin 2 world War museum then move to Marsa Matrouh on the Mediterranean Sea for lunch break in one from the local restaurants there after lunch move to Siwa oasis arrive afternoon and overnight in hotel.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals:</strong>&nbsp;Lunch, Dinner</p>\r\n<p><strong>Accommodation&nbsp;</strong>: Dream Lodge Hotel, Siwa &nbsp;</p>'),
(3489, 629, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3490, 629, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3491, 629, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3492, 629, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3493, 629, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3494, 629, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3495, 630, 'en', 'Day 2 : Siwa local attraction', '<p>After Breakfast start our tour with Shali Old Town. Some buildings here are still in use but due to their construction of salt, mud &amp; plaster they fall into ruin year after year then Following visiting the siwa museum located in a traditional siwan hoaus, the museum boasts traditional siwan objects such as silver, jewellery ,music instrument, wedding costumes , baskets and ceramic.</p>\r\n<p>Then move to Amoun temple (Om Obayda) dates back to the 30th dynasty, and the Oracle Temple where Alexander the Great consulted the oracle to validate his status as the son of Zeus and thus legitimate ruler of the country.</p>\r\n<p>Move to Cleopatra Spring, enjoy the lunch in local cafeteria beside the water spring then Spend today\'s afternoon at Bir Wahed set out 12 km southwest of Siwa.</p>\r\n<p>A hot spring and cold spring at the edge of Great Sand Sea with water right in the middle of the sand dunes and take a mazing sunset from a top of sand dunes , then move to the Bedouin camp for the attractive Bedouin dinner and back to the hotel.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals</strong>: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner</p>\r\n<p><strong>Accommodation&nbsp;</strong>: Dream Lodge Hotel, Siwa &nbsp;</p>'),
(3496, 630, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3497, 630, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3498, 630, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3499, 630, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3500, 630, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3501, 630, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3502, 631, 'en', 'Day 3 : Siwa – Cairo', '<div class=\"my-12\">\r\n<section class=\"p-4 pb-6 flex flex-col gap-4 border-b-2 border-b-[#EEEEEE]\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"mt-4\">\r\n<div class=\"relative flex gap-3\">\r\n<div class=\"border w-full border-[#eeeeee] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-4\">\r\n<div class=\"pt-4 mx-5 pb-6 text-[#666666]\">\r\n<div class=\"mt-\">\r\n<p>After Breakfast, Departure to Cairo, crossing the Western Desert &amp; back to hotel in Cairo and end the program.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals</strong>: Breakfast</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Note :</strong></p>\r\n<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;if the mentioned hotels or cruises are not available, the company have the right to Change the hotel or Cruise as it of&nbsp;same&nbsp;category&nbsp;.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:15357,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:4408131},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">if the mentioned hotels is not available, the company have the right to Change the hotel as it of same category.</span></p>\r\n<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;if the mentioned hotels or cruises are not available, the company have the right to Change the hotel or Cruise as it of&nbsp;same&nbsp;category&nbsp;.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:15357,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:4408131},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">That the order of the days could be change according to cruise sailing dates keeping the sightseeing you will visit as it is.</span></p>\r\n<p><strong><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;if the mentioned hotels or cruises are not available, the company have the right to Change the hotel or Cruise as it of&nbsp;same&nbsp;category&nbsp;.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:15357,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;5&qu