t;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:13421772}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:4408131},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Note : For pick up / drop off form Cairo airport, Sphinx airport, New Administrative Capital, New Cairo, Helioplis, Badr City, Shorouk, Rehab, Obour, Sheraton Almatar, Sheikh Zayed city or Madinty City will be for additional cost</span></strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"my-12\">\r\n<section class=\"p-4 pb-6 flex flex-col gap-4 border-b-2 border-b-[#EEEEEE]\">\r\n<div class=\"flex justify-between items-center\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>'),
(3503, 631, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3504, 631, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3505, 631, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3506, 631, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3507, 631, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3508, 631, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3509, 632, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>get picked up from your hotel in Luxor by your Egyptologist tour guide at 7 AM and begin driving north of Luxor past local daily life. As you drive, admire views of quaint villages all the way to Abydos Temple, and listen closely as your expert guide tells you about interesting historical details of the great temple. Unique because of its limestone construction laid out over three levels, Abydos Temple is considered one-of-kind in many other respects. Find out why as you explore this historical treasure trove.&nbsp; Afterwards, drive on to Dendara Temple. Dedicated to Hathor, the goddess of motherhood, the Dendara Temple dates back to the late Ptolemaic Period and is located on holy Egyptian ground. The site is renowned for its relics of religious structures built during the reign of the Old Kingdom of Pharaoh Pepi the First.&nbsp; Enjoy taking stunning photos at these mesmerizing historical locations. When the adventure is over, get dropped off back at your hotel in Luxor.</p>'),
(3510, 632, 'fr', 'Jour 1', '<p>Faites-vous chercher &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel &agrave; Louxor par votre guide &eacute;gyptologue &agrave; 7 heures du matin et commencez &agrave; conduire au nord de Louxor en passant par la vie quotidienne locale. Pendant que vous conduisez, admirez la vue sur les villages pittoresques jusqu\'au temple d\'Abydos et &eacute;coutez attentivement votre guide expert vous raconter des d&eacute;tails historiques int&eacute;ressants sur le grand temple. Unique en raison de sa construction en pierre calcaire r&eacute;partie sur trois niveaux, le temple d\'Abydos est consid&eacute;r&eacute; comme unique &agrave; bien d\'autres &eacute;gards. D&eacute;couvrez pourquoi en explorant ce tr&eacute;sor historique. Ensuite, continuez vers le temple de Dendara. D&eacute;di&eacute; &agrave; Hathor, la d&eacute;esse de la maternit&eacute;, le temple de Dendara remonte &agrave; la fin de la p&eacute;riode ptol&eacute;ma&iuml;que et est situ&eacute; sur le territoire sacr&eacute; de l\'&Eacute;gypte. Le site est r&eacute;put&eacute; pour ses reliques d\'&eacute;difices religieux construits sous le r&egrave;gne de l\'Ancien Empire du pharaon P&eacute;pi Premier. Profitez de prendre de superbes photos dans ces lieux historiques fascinants. Une fois l\'aventure termin&eacute;e, soyez d&eacute;pos&eacute; &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel &agrave; Louxor.</p>'),
(3511, 632, 'de', 'Tag 1', '<p>Lassen Sie sich um 7 Uhr morgens von Ihrem &auml;gyptologischen Reiseleiter von Ihrem Hotel in Luxor abholen und beginnen Sie mit der Fahrt n&ouml;rdlich von Luxor, vorbei am Alltagsleben der Einheimischen. Bewundern Sie w&auml;hrend der Fahrt die Aussicht auf malerische D&ouml;rfer bis hin zum Abydos-Tempel und h&ouml;ren Sie aufmerksam zu, w&auml;hrend Ihr fachkundiger Reisef&uuml;hrer Ihnen interessante historische Details des gro&szlig;en Tempels erz&auml;hlt. Der Abydos-Tempel ist aufgrund seiner Kalksteinkonstruktion auf drei Ebenen einzigartig und gilt in vielerlei Hinsicht als einzigartig. Finden Sie heraus, warum, w&auml;hrend Sie diese historische Schatzkammer erkunden. Anschlie&szlig;end fahren Sie weiter zum Dendara-Tempel. Der Dendara-Tempel ist Hathor, der G&ouml;ttin der Mutterschaft, gewidmet und stammt aus der sp&auml;ten Ptolem&auml;erzeit. Er befindet sich auf heiligem &auml;gyptischen Boden. Die St&auml;tte ist bekannt f&uuml;r ihre Relikte religi&ouml;ser Bauwerke, die w&auml;hrend der Herrschaft des Alten K&ouml;nigreichs von Pharao Pepi dem Ersten errichtet wurden. Genie&szlig;en Sie atemberaubende Fotos an diesen faszinierenden historischen Orten. Wenn das Abenteuer vorbei ist, werden Sie zu Ihrem Hotel in Luxor zur&uuml;ckgebracht.</p>');
INSERT INTO `tour_day_translations` (`id`, `tour_day_id`, `locale`, `title`, `description`) VALUES
(3512, 632, 'it', 'Giorno 1', '<p>prendi il prelievo dal tuo hotel a Luxor dalla tua guida turistica egittologa alle 7 del mattino e inizia a guidare a nord di Luxor, oltre la vita quotidiana locale. Mentre guidi, ammira le viste dei pittoreschi villaggi fino al Tempio di Abydos e ascolta attentamente mentre la tua guida esperta ti racconta interessanti dettagli storici del grande tempio. Unico per la sua costruzione in pietra calcarea disposta su tre livelli, il Tempio di Abydos &egrave; considerato unico nel suo genere sotto molti altri aspetti. Scopri perch&eacute; mentre esplori questo tesoro storico. Successivamente, prosegui fino al Tempio di Dendara. Dedicato a Hathor, la dea della maternit&agrave;, il Tempio di Dendara risale al tardo periodo tolemaico e si trova sul suolo sacro egiziano. Il sito &egrave; rinomato per le sue reliquie di strutture religiose costruite durante il regno dell\'Antico Regno del faraone Pepi I. Divertiti a scattare splendide foto in questi affascinanti luoghi storici. Al termine dell\'avventura, fatti riportare al tuo hotel a Luxor.</p>'),
(3513, 632, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3514, 632, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3515, 632, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3516, 633, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p data-start=\"915\" data-end=\"1278\">Your tour begins with a scenic drive south from Aswan through desert landscapes toward the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Abu Simbel. Upon arrival, you will explore the Great Temple of Ramses II, dominated by four monumental seated statues that guard the entrance. Inside, reliefs and scenes depict royal power, religious devotion, and the famous Battle of Kadesh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1280\" data-end=\"1706\">You then continue to the Temple of Queen Nefertari, dedicated to the goddess Hathor. This elegant structure honors the queen alongside Ramses II, showcasing beautifully preserved reliefs and vibrant details. Your guide will also explain how both temples were cut into massive blocks and moved to higher ground to save them from the rising waters of Lake Nasser. After your visit, you will return comfortably to Aswan by coach.</p>'),
(3517, 633, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3518, 633, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3519, 633, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3520, 633, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3521, 633, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3522, 633, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3523, 634, 'en', 'Day 1 : Safari Trip to Bahariya - Black Desert - Old & New White Desert', '<p>The adventure commences in the bustling city of&nbsp;<strong>Cairo</strong>. an early morning pick-up in our air-conditioned vehicle. We journey towards the serene&nbsp;<strong>Bahariya Oasis</strong>, a tranquil retreat in the desert. Upon arrival, an off-road jeep stands ready to kickstart our exhilarating exploration.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>White Desert National Park</strong></h2>\r\n<p>White Desert National Park, is famous for its surreal landscapes of white limestone rock formations shaped by wind erosion. These unique shapes, resembling giant mushrooms or animals, create an otherworldly scenery. The park offers a peaceful, natural escape and is popular for desert safaris, camping under the stars, and photography.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Black Desert</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Black Desert, is known for its unique dark, volcanic hills and black rocks that cover the sand. The landscape is dotted with mountains and hills, giving it a striking contrast to the nearby White Desert.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>El Hez Village&rsquo;s</strong></h2>\r\n<p>El Hez Village&rsquo;s Cold Spring, is a natural oasis spring offering cool, refreshing water in the middle of the desert. It&rsquo;s a popular spot for travelers to relax and enjoy the natural beauty of the area. Surrounded by palm trees and serene landscapes.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Crystal Mountain</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Crystal Mountain, is a natural wonder in Egypt&rsquo;s Western Desert. The mountain is made up of sparkling quartz crystals that shimmer in the sunlight, giving it its name. A popular stop on desert safaris.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Agabat Valley</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Agabat Valley, is known for its breathtaking, otherworldly landscapes. Surrounded by towering white limestone cliffs and golden sand dunes, the valley features stunning rock formations shaped by wind erosion.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The highlight of our expedition is the visit to the Old White Desert, a natural wonder housing unique formations that mimic mushrooms and tents. We further explore the New White Desert, a surreal landscape adorned with striking limestone formations. As the day draws to a close, we set up camp amidst these natural marvels. A delectable dinner under the starry sky offers the perfect setting to reminisce about the day&rsquo;s adventures.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals</strong>: Lunch, Dinner</p>'),
(3524, 634, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3525, 634, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3526, 634, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3527, 634, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3528, 634, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3529, 634, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3530, 635, 'en', 'Day 2 : Enjoy the Bahariya Oasis Sunrise & Return Back to Cairo', '<p>Awake to a stunning sunrise and savor a hearty breakfast in our camp. After breakfast, we drive back to the oasis in our jeep. A comfortable vehicle awaits to transport us back to the vibrant city of Cairo, marking the culmination of this unforgettable journey.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals</strong>: Breakfast.</p>'),
(3531, 635, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3532, 635, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3533, 635, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3534, 635, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3535, 635, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3536, 635, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3537, 636, 'en', 'ARRIVAL Day 1 FRIDAY,30TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>Welcome to Egypt! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be met and greeted by one of Egygo&rsquo;s travel representatives. They will<br>assist you to obtain the necessary entry documents and guide you through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we<br>will travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local<br>surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your journey.</p>'),
(3538, 636, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3539, 636, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3540, 636, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3541, 636, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3542, 636, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3543, 636, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3544, 637, 'en', 'FREE DAY - Day 2 - SATURDAY,31TH OF JULY 2027', '<p>After Breakfast, you will have free time to relax and enjoy the beautiful of the red sea at your leisure.<br><strong>Overnight in Hurghada.</strong><br><br></p>'),
(3545, 637, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3546, 637, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3547, 637, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3548, 637, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3549, 637, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3550, 637, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3551, 638, 'en', 'FREE DAY - Day 3 - SUNDAY,1 ST OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After Breakfast, Enjoy more free time by the red sea to relax, explore, or just soak up the sun.<br><strong>Overnight in Hurghada</strong></p>'),
(3552, 638, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3553, 638, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3554, 638, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3555, 638, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3556, 638, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3557, 638, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3558, 639, 'en', 'KARNAK TEMPLE & LUXOR TEMPLE - MONDAY,2ND OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>leave Hurghada in the early Morning, transfer to Luxor. Next, Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple, A special chance to witness the total<br>solar eclipse from Karnak Temple. Watching this rare event from such a historic place will be a truly unforgettable experience.<br>Proceeding our tour to Luxor Temple in which you&rsquo;ll stand in the shadows of the Great Ramses II colossi.<br>Back to Hurghada.KARNAK TEMPLE<br><strong>Overnight in Hurghada.</strong></p>'),
(3559, 639, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3560, 639, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3561, 639, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3562, 639, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3563, 639, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3564, 639, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3565, 640, 'en', 'FREE DAY - Day 5 - TUESDAY,3RD OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>free day at leisure.<br>optional activities: Snorkeling, diving, desert safari.Overnight in Hurghada</p>'),
(3566, 640, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3567, 640, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3568, 640, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3569, 640, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3570, 640, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3571, 640, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3572, 641, 'en', 'CHECK OUT - FLY BACK TO CAIRO, FINAL DEPARTURE - WEDNESDAY,4TH OF AUGUST 2027', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out from your Hotel.<br>Catch our flight back to Cairo. catch your international flight.<br><br></p>'),
(3573, 641, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3574, 641, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3575, 641, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3576, 641, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3577, 641, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3578, 641, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3579, 642, 'en', 'Day 1: Arrival', '<p>Upon arrival at Cairo International Airport, you will be met and<br>escorted by one of Egygo Travel representatives . They will assist<br>you in obtaining the necessary entry documents and guide you<br>through customs. Once your luggage has been retrieved, we will<br>travel by private air conditioned coach to our hotel. Depending on<br>your arrival time, you will have time to explore your local<br>surroundings or retire to you room to rest and relax after your<br>journey.<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(3580, 642, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3581, 642, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3582, 642, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3583, 642, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3584, 642, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3585, 642, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3586, 643, 'en', 'Day 2 GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM', '<p>After breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you up to&nbsp;visit the Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM) Located near the&nbsp;Pyramids, the Grand Egyptian Museum is the largest&nbsp;archaeological museum in the world. It houses over&nbsp;100,000 artifacts, including the complete collection of&nbsp;King Tutankhamun. Designed to reflect ancient Egyptian&nbsp;heritage with a modern touch, GEM features state-of-the-&nbsp;art exhibits, conservation labs, and a grand staircase with&nbsp;colossal statues. A cultural landmark, it offers a unique&nbsp;journey through 5,000 years of history in one spectacular&nbsp;setting.<br>Egygo Travel would like to invite you to the Welcome&nbsp;Dinner.<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(3587, 643, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3588, 643, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3589, 643, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3590, 643, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3591, 643, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3592, 643, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3593, 644, 'en', 'Day 3 Private visit to the Great Sphinx and Saqqara complex', '<p>Following breakfast, your Egyptologist guide will pick you<br>for your special private visit to The Great Sphinx, arranged<br>by Egygo\'s experienced Egyptologist, commences by<br>private motor coach to the Giza Plateau. Constructed<br>around 2500BC (Old Kingdom) , the Great Sphinx is a<br>mythical creature with the head of a human and the body<br>of a lion. Facing east, The Great Sphinx greets the morning<br>sun while protecting the Giza pyramids.<br>After that, you will get to visit the Sakkara Complex, which<br>was the main burial area for kings, queens and nobles<br>during the old kingdom, in the same area, you will have the<br>opportunity to visit the Step Pyramid of King Djoser,<br>renowned as the first successful attempt at constructing a<br>standing pyramid 4800 years old</p>'),
(3594, 644, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3595, 644, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3596, 644, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3597, 644, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3598, 644, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3599, 644, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3600, 645, 'en', 'Day 4 Flight to Luxor, Abydos Temple and overnight in Suhag', '<p>After breakfast, we travel to Cairo International Airport for<br>your flight to Luxor.<br>Upon arrival, we will be taken by private motor coach to<br>explore Abydos.<br>Abydos, home to the Temple of Seti I, father of Ramses II, is<br>one of the most important archaeological sites of Ancient<br>Egypt. During ancient times, it was the necropolis for Egypt\'s<br>earliest kings. The \"Abydos King List\" as well as Phoenician<br>and Aramaic graffiti are found on the temple walls.<br>While in Abydos, Egygo\'s Egytologist has arranged for a<br>private visit to the Osierion, it is normally closed to tourists.<br>The Osierion, a megalithic structure, built below ground<br>simulates an island. It is positioned at the rear of the Temple,<br>accessed only through the Temple body. On one of its<br>monoliths is painted the FLOWER OF LIFE, one of the most<br>important symbols of sacred geometry.<br>Overnight in Suhag</p>'),
(3601, 645, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3602, 645, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3603, 645, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3604, 645, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3605, 645, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3606, 645, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3607, 646, 'en', 'Day 5 Dendera Temple and back to Luxor', '<p>Following breakfast, we set off, accompanied by our Egygo Egyptologist, to explore Dendera Temple.<br>Dedicated to goddess Hathor , the Temple is one of the best-preserved temples in Egypt. Depictions of Cleopatra VI appear on<br>Temple walls. On the rear wall is a carving of Cleoppatra VI (the popular Cleopatria) and her son Ptolemy XV who was fathered by Julius<br>Cesar.<br>Following our visits, we will have lunch at a local restaurant.<br>After lunch, we will transfer to Luxor for check-in at our Dahabiya.<br>Overnight in Luxor on board of Dahabiya.</p>'),
(3608, 646, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3609, 646, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3610, 646, 'it', NULL, NULL),
