(3612, 646, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3613, 646, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3614, 647, 'en', 'Day 6 Valley of the Kings and Karnak Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will start our tour by visiting Karnak Temple<br>which is believed to be the second most visited historical site<br>surpassed only by the Giza Pyramids. One of the many<br>highlights of Karnak Temple\'s is it hypostyle hall consisting of<br>134 massive columns in 16 rows.<br>Next stop is The Valley of Kings, the final resting place of many<br>of the ancient Egyptian Pharaohs. Here, we will visit some of the<br>better known tombs including that of Pharaoh Tutankhamen.<br>Overnight on board our dahabiya</p>'),
(3615, 647, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3616, 647, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3617, 647, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3618, 647, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3619, 647, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3620, 647, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3621, 648, 'en', 'Day 7 Edfu Temple and Komombo Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will visit Edfu Temple . Considered to be one of<br>the best preserved temples from ancient Egypt, It is the largest<br>temple dedicated to the god Horus and his consort , the goddess,<br>Hathor of Dendera. Each year, Hathor would travel from her temple<br>in Dendera to visit Horus at Edfu. This event marked their sacred<br>marriage and, in ancient times, was an occasion of a great Festival<br>and pilgrimage. we will visit Kom Ombo Temple, a very unusual<br>temple. It\'s uniqueness is for several reasons. It is dedication to<br>two different deities, the local crocodile-headed god, Sobek, and<br>the falcon-headed god Horus.<br>Return to Dahabiya for overnight sailing Aswan<br>Overnight on board.</p>'),
(3622, 648, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3623, 648, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3624, 648, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3625, 648, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3626, 648, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3627, 648, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3628, 649, 'en', 'Day 8 Philae Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will be boarding a small motor boat from the landing, We will head to the Philae Island. The island is home to Philae<br>Temple aka \"Temple of Lovers\" Dedicated to the goddess Isis, Philae Temple presents the perfect backdrop to the most ancient of all<br>love stories in history, that of Isis and Osiris.<br>Back to Dahabiya<br>Overnight on board</p>'),
(3629, 649, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3630, 649, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3631, 649, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3632, 649, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3633, 649, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3634, 649, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3635, 650, 'en', 'Day 9 Abu Simble Temple', '<p>After breakfast, we will travel to Abu Simble, visit the Temple of Ramesses the great which is carved in the mountain; a true miracle of<br>ancient and modern engineering that deserves to be counted among the wonders of the world. back to Aswan</p>'),
(3636, 650, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3637, 650, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3638, 650, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3639, 650, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3640, 650, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3641, 650, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3642, 651, 'en', 'Day 10 Back to Cairo', '<p>After breakfast, we will check out from our cruise to catch our flight back to Cairo.<br>Arrive to Cairo.<br>Check in at the hotel<br>Overnight in Cairo.</p>'),
(3643, 651, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3644, 651, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3645, 651, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3646, 651, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3647, 651, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3648, 651, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3649, 652, 'en', 'Day 11: Private Opening of The Great Pyramid of Giza & Aromatherapy experience', '<p>After breakfast, you will experience an exclusive special private<br>opening of the Great Pyramid of Giza, the only surviving wonder of<br>the ancient world.<br>Next, we will visit a well-known perfumery.<br>Here, drawing on the knowledge of his ancestors, we will<br>be guided through this subject by a certified<br>aromatherapist. Known as \"Healer from the Heart\", he will present a<br>detailed explanation about the physical and psychological uses of<br>the organic essential oils of Egypt. Historically, the beneficial<br>effects of their use has been documented in various papyri of the<br>Ancients. After our essential oil lesson, we return to our hotel.<br>Egygo Travel would like to invite you to the Farewell Dinner.<br>Overnight in Cairo</p>'),
(3650, 652, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3651, 652, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3652, 652, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3653, 652, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3654, 652, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3655, 652, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3656, 653, 'en', 'Day 12 Departure', '<p>After breakfast, you will check out and be transported to Cairo<br>International Airport by private coach to catch your international<br>flight</p>'),
(3657, 653, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3658, 653, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3659, 653, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3660, 653, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3661, 653, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3662, 653, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3663, 654, 'en', '“Luxor Sightseeing / Fly back to Cairo”', '<p>Breakfast onboard the cruise, check-out the Nile cruise and then&nbsp;will be picked up by our tour guide to visit archaeological sites of the ancient Egyptians on the west bank of the Nile including the two colossal statues of <strong>Amenhotep III (Colossi of Memnon),</strong> and then visit the <strong>Valley of the Kings</strong>, where the magnificent tombs discovered, those tombs were carved deep into the desert rock, richly decorated and filled with treasures for the afterlife of the pharaohs, you will visit 3 tombs. Continue the tour to visit the <strong>Hatshepsut temple</strong> at El <strong>Deir El Bahary</strong>, this impressive temple dedicated to the Queen Hatshepsut the only female pharaoh rises out of the desert plain in a series of terraces and merges with the sheer limestone cliffs that surround it.</p>\r\n<p>Then heading to visit the two Massive temples on the eastern bank of the Nile, <strong>visit the Temple of Luxor and Temple of Karnak</strong>. Karnak Temple, the largest place of worship ever built. Its ancient name Ipet-isut means the most sacred of places. The temple, or, more correctly, the complex of temples, was built over more than two thousand years by generation after generation of pharaohs. Within the complex, the great Hypostyle Hall&nbsp;is an incredible forest of giant pillars. Then you will be transferred to the majestic Luxor temple which built by Amenhotep III and Ramses II for rituals and festivals and dedicated to the god Amun god of air sun and sky.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>After finishing the tour, you will be transferred to Luxor airport for <strong>Domestic Flight</strong> back to Cairo. Upon arrival to Cairo airport you will be picked up and transferred to the hotel for check in and Overnight.</p>'),
(3664, 654, 'fr', '« Visite de Louxor / Retour au Caire »', '<p>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de la croisi&egrave;re, d&eacute;part de la croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil, puis prise en charge par notre guide pour visiter les sites arch&eacute;ologiques des anciens &Eacute;gyptiens sur la rive ouest du Nil, y compris les deux statues colossales d\'Amenhotep III. (Colosses de Memnon), puis visitez la <strong>Vall&eacute;e des Rois</strong>, o&ugrave; ont &eacute;t&eacute; d&eacute;couverts les magnifiques tombeaux, ces tombeaux ont &eacute;t&eacute; creus&eacute;s profond&eacute;ment dans la roche du d&eacute;sert, richement d&eacute;cor&eacute;s et remplis de tr&eacute;sors de l\'au-del&agrave; des pharaons, vous visiterez 3 tombeaux. Continuez la visite pour visiter le <strong>temple d\'Hatchepsout</strong> &agrave; El <strong>Deir El Bahary</strong>, cet impressionnant temple d&eacute;di&eacute; &agrave; la reine Hatshepsout, la seule femme pharaon, s\'&eacute;l&egrave;ve de la plaine d&eacute;sertique dans une s&eacute;rie de terrasses et se confond avec les falaises calcaires abruptes qui l\'entourent.</p>\r\n<p>Ensuite, direction les deux temples massifs sur la rive orientale du Nil, <strong>visitez le temple de Louxor et le temple de Karnak. Temple de Karnak, le plus grand lieu de culte jamais construit. Son ancien nom Ipet-isut signifie le lieu le plus sacr&eacute;. Le temple, ou, plus exactement, le complexe de temples, a &eacute;t&eacute; construit sur plus de deux mille ans par g&eacute;n&eacute;ration apr&egrave;s g&eacute;n&eacute;ration de pharaons. Au sein du complexe, la grande salle hypostyle est une incroyable for&ecirc;t de piliers g&eacute;ants. Ensuite, vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute; au majestueux temple de Louxor construit par Amenhotep III et Rams&egrave;s II pour les rituels et les festivals et d&eacute;di&eacute; au dieu Amon, dieu de l\'air, du soleil et du ciel. </strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Une fois la visite termin&eacute;e, vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute; &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport de Louxor pour le <strong>vol int&eacute;rieur</strong> de retour au Caire. &Agrave; votre arriv&eacute;e &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport du Caire, vous serez pris en charge et transf&eacute;r&eacute; &agrave; l\'h&ocirc;tel pour l\'enregistrement et la nuit.</strong></p>'),
(3665, 654, 'de', '„Luxor-Sightseeing / Rückflug nach Kairo“', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord der Kreuzfahrt, Besichtigung der Nilkreuzfahrt und anschlie&szlig;ende Abholung durch unseren Reiseleiter zur Besichtigung der arch&auml;ologischen St&auml;tten der alten &Auml;gypter am Westufer des Nils, einschlie&szlig;lich der beiden kolossalen Statuen von <strong>Amenhotep III (Memnonkolosse)</strong> und besuchen Sie dann das <strong>Tal der K&ouml;nige</strong>, wo die pr&auml;chtigen Gr&auml;ber entdeckt wurden. Diese Gr&auml;ber wurden tief in den W&uuml;stenfelsen gehauen, reich verziert und mit Sch&auml;tzen gef&uuml;llt Nach dem Tod der Pharaonen besuchen Sie 3 Gr&auml;ber. Setzen Sie die Tour fort und besuchen Sie den <strong>Hatschepsut-Tempel</strong> in El <strong>Deir El Bahary</strong>. Dieser beeindruckende Tempel, der der K&ouml;nigin Hatschepsut gewidmet ist, der einzigen weiblichen Pharaonin, erhebt sich in mehreren Schritten aus der W&uuml;stenebene Terrassen und verschmilzt mit den steilen Kalksteinfelsen, die es umgeben.</p>\r\n<p>Besuchen Sie anschlie&szlig;end die beiden riesigen Tempel am Ostufer des Nils, <strong>den Luxor-Tempel und den Karnak-Tempel</strong> &gt;. Karnak-Tempel, die gr&ouml;&szlig;te jemals gebaute Kultst&auml;tte. Sein alter Name Ipet-isut bedeutet der heiligste aller Orte. Der Tempel, oder genauer gesagt der Tempelkomplex, wurde &uuml;ber mehr als zweitausend Jahre hinweg von Generationen von Pharaonen erbaut. Innerhalb des Komplexes ist die gro&szlig;e Hypostyle-Halle ein unglaublicher Wald aus riesigen S&auml;ulen. Anschlie&szlig;end werden Sie zum majest&auml;tischen Luxor-Tempel gebracht, der von Amenophis III. und Ramses II. f&uuml;r Rituale und Feste erbaut und dem Gott Amun, dem Gott der Luft, Sonne und des Himmels, gewidmet wurde.</p>\r\n<p>Nach Abschluss der Tour werden Sie zum Flughafen Luxor f&uuml;r einen <strong>Inlandsflug</strong> zur&uuml;ck nach Kairo gebracht. Bei Ihrer Ankunft am Flughafen Kairo werden Sie abgeholt und zum Hotel gebracht, wo Sie einchecken und &uuml;bernachten.</p>'),
(3666, 654, 'it', '“Giro turistico di Luxor / Ritorno al Cairo”', '<p>Colazione a bordo della crociera, check-out della crociera sul Nilo e poi verrai prelevato dalla nostra guida turistica per visitare i siti archeologici degli antichi egizi sulla riva occidentale del Nilo, tra cui le due colossali statue di <strong>Amenhotep III (Colossi di Memnone),</strong> e poi visitare la <strong>Valle dei Re</strong>, dove furono scoperte le magnifiche tombe, quelle tombe furono scavate in profondit&agrave; nella roccia del deserto, riccamente decorate e piene di tesori per i aldil&agrave; dei faraoni, visiterai 3 tombe. Continua il tour per visitare il <strong>tempio di Hatshepsut</strong> a El <strong>Deir El Bahary</strong>, questo imponente tempio dedicato alla regina Hatshepsut, l\'unico faraone donna, si erge dalla pianura desertica in una serie di terrazze e si fonde con le scogliere calcaree a strapiombo che lo circondano.</p>\r\n<p>Quindi dirigiti a visitare i due enormi templi sulla sponda orientale del Nilo, <strong>visita il Tempio di Luxor e il Tempio di Karnak</strong>. Tempio di Karnak, il pi&ugrave; grande luogo di culto mai costruito. Il suo antico nome Ipet-isut significa il pi&ugrave; sacro dei luoghi. Il tempio, o, pi&ugrave; correttamente, il complesso dei templi, fu costruito nel corso di pi&ugrave; di duemila anni da generazione dopo generazione di faraoni. All\'interno del complesso, la grande Sala Ipostila &egrave; un\'incredibile foresta di pilastri giganti. Quindi verrai trasferito al maestoso tempio di Luxor, costruito da Amenhotep III e Ramses II per rituali e feste e dedicato al dio Amon, dio dell\'aria, del sole e del cielo.</p>\r\n<p>Dopo aver terminato il tour, verrai trasferito all\'aeroporto di Luxor per il <strong>volo interno</strong> di ritorno al Cairo. All\'arrivo all\'aeroporto del Cairo verrai prelevato e trasferito in hotel per il check-in e il pernottamento.</p>'),
(3667, 654, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3668, 654, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3669, 654, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3670, 655, 'en', '“Nile Cruise Tour”', '<p>After breakfast you will be accompanied by your Egyptologist guide to <strong>visit</strong> <strong>Kom Ombo temple</strong>, the crocodile-headed God of fertility and creator of the world, lunch aboard your cruise with free time at leisure whilst sailing to Edfu to <strong>explore Edfu Temple of Horus</strong>, one of the best-preserved Ancient Egyptian temples on the Nile Continue the cruise down the Nile to Luxor and overnight stay onboard your Nile cruise ship.</p>'),
(3671, 655, 'fr', '«Croisière sur le Nil»', '<p>Apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner, vous serez accompagn&eacute; de votre guide &eacute;gyptologue pour <strong>visiter</strong> le <strong>temple de Kom Ombo</strong>, le dieu de la fertilit&eacute; &agrave; t&ecirc;te de crocodile et cr&eacute;ateur du monde, d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re. avec temps libre tout en naviguant vers Edfou pour <strong>explorer le temple d\'Horus d\'Edfou</strong>, l\'un des temples &eacute;gyptiens antiques les mieux conserv&eacute;s sur le Nil. Continuez la croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil jusqu\'&agrave; Louxor et passez la nuit &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil. navire.</p>'),
(3672, 655, 'de', '„Nilkreuzfahrt-Tour“', '<p>Nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck werden Sie von Ihrem &auml;gyptologischen Reiseleiter zum <strong>Kom-Ombo-Tempel</strong>, dem krokodilk&ouml;pfigen Gott der Fruchtbarkeit und Sch&ouml;pfer der Welt, begleitet. Mittagessen an Bord Ihrer Kreuzfahrt Mit Freizeit zur freien Verf&uuml;gung, w&auml;hrend Sie nach Edfu segeln, um den Horus-Tempel von Edfu zu erkunden, einen der am besten erhaltenen alt&auml;gyptischen Tempel auf dem Nil. Setzen Sie die Kreuzfahrt den Nil hinunter nach Luxor fort und &uuml;bernachten Sie an Bord Nilkreuzfahrtschiff.</p>'),
(3673, 655, 'it', '“Tour in crociera sul Nilo”', '<p>Dopo la colazione sarai accompagnato dalla tua guida egittologa per <strong>visitare</strong> il <strong>tempio di Kom Ombo</strong>, il dio della fertilit&agrave; dalla testa di coccodrillo e creatore del mondo, pranzo a bordo della tua crociera con tempo libero a disposizione durante la navigazione verso Edfu per <strong>esplorare il Tempio di Horus di Edfu</strong>, uno dei templi dell\'antico Egitto meglio conservati sul Nilo Continua la crociera lungo il Nilo fino a Luxor e pernottamento a bordo della tua crociera sul Nilo nave.</p>'),
(3674, 655, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3675, 655, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3676, 655, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3677, 656, 'en', '” Abu-Simbel Excursions / Nile Cruise Tour”', '<p>Breakfast box from your hotel in Aswan and then you will be escorted by your Egyptologist speaking guide and driver to explore the impressive temples built by <strong>Ramses II</strong> in <strong>Abu Simbel</strong> which is one of Egypt\'s most visited sites. Relocated in the 1960\'s with the building of the Aswan Dam, Abu Simbel is a feat of modern and ancient engineering then you will be transferred to Aswan to embark your Nile cruise ship. Lunch, afternoon tea and free time at leisure aboard your Nile cruise sailing to Kom-Ombo.</p>'),
(3678, 656, 'fr', '« Excursions à Abou-Simbel / Croisière sur le Nil »', '<p>Bo&icirc;te de petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel &agrave; Assouan, puis vous serez escort&eacute; par votre guide et chauffeur &eacute;gyptologue pour explorer les impressionnants temples construits par <strong>Rams&egrave;s II</strong> &agrave; <strong>Abou Simbel</strong> qui est l\'un des sites les plus visit&eacute;s d\'&Eacute;gypte. D&eacute;m&eacute;nag&eacute; dans les ann&eacute;es 1960 avec la construction du barrage d\'Assouan, Abou Simbel est une prouesse d\'ing&eacute;nierie moderne et ancienne. Vous serez ensuite transf&eacute;r&eacute; &agrave; Assouan pour embarquer sur votre bateau de croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil. D&eacute;jeuner, th&eacute; de l\'apr&egrave;s-midi et temps libre &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil en direction de Kom-Ombo.</p>'),
(3679, 656, 'de', '„Abu-Simbel-Ausflüge / Nilkreuzfahrt-Tour“', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ckspaket in Ihrem Hotel in Assuan. Anschlie&szlig;end werden Sie von Ihrem &auml;gyptologischen Reisef&uuml;hrer und Fahrer begleitet, um die beeindruckenden Tempel zu erkunden, die von <strong>Ramses II.</strong> in <strong>Abu Simbel</strong> erbaut wurden ist eine der meistbesuchten Sehensw&uuml;rdigkeiten &Auml;gyptens. Abu Simbel wurde in den 1960er Jahren mit dem Bau des Assuan-Staudamms verlegt und ist ein Meisterwerk moderner und alter Ingenieurskunst. Anschlie&szlig;end werden Sie nach Assuan gebracht, um an Bord Ihres Nilkreuzfahrtschiffs zu gehen. Mittagessen, Nachmittagstee und Freizeit an Bord Ihrer Nilkreuzfahrt nach Kom-Ombo.</p>'),
(3680, 656, 'it', '\"Escursioni ad Abu-Simbel / Tour in crociera sul Nilo\"', '<p>Colazione al sacco dal tuo hotel ad Assuan e poi sarai accompagnato dalla tua guida e autista parlante egittologo per esplorare gli imponenti templi costruiti da <strong>Ramses II</strong> ad <strong>Abu Simbel</strong> che &egrave; uno dei siti pi&ugrave; visitati dell\'Egitto. Trasferito negli anni \'60 con la costruzione della diga di Assuan, Abu Simbel &egrave; un\'impresa di ingegneria moderna e antica, quindi verrai trasferito ad Assuan per imbarcarti sulla tua nave da crociera sul Nilo. Pranzo, t&egrave; pomeridiano e tempo libero a bordo della crociera sul Nilo verso Kom-Ombo.</p>'),
(3681, 656, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3682, 656, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3683, 656, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3684, 657, 'en', '“Fly to Aswan/ Aswan sightseeing”', '<p>Breakfast at your hotel, and then you will be transferred to Cairo airport for your flight to Aswan city. Upon arrival will be met and assisted by Egyptologist who will accompany you in an exciting tour to the world famous <strong>High</strong> <strong>Dam</strong> that was an engineering miracle when it was built in the 1960s. It contains 18 times the material used in the Great Pyramid of Cheops; continue to the granite quarries which supplied the ancient Egyptians with most of the hard stone used in pyramids and temples. The quarries still hold the famous <strong>Unfinished Obelisk</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>Then you will be taking by motor-boat to island of <strong>Egilka</strong> visit the majestic <strong>Philae temple</strong> that was dedicated to the Goddesses Isis.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Then you will be transferred to your Nile cruise ship, where you will enjoy the next 4 Days / 3 Nights Nile cruise holiday from Aswan up to Luxor with fantastic sailing and thrilling tours. Free time at leisure aboard your Nile cruise ship in Aswan.</p>'),
(3685, 657, 'fr', '«Envolez-vous pour Assouan / Visite d\'Assouan»', '<p>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel, puis transfert &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport du Caire pour votre vol vers la ville d\'Assouan. &Agrave; votre arriv&eacute;e, vous serez accueilli et assist&eacute; par un &eacute;gyptologue qui vous accompagnera dans une visite passionnante du c&eacute;l&egrave;bre <strong>Haut</strong> <strong>Barrage</strong> qui &eacute;tait un miracle d\'ing&eacute;nierie lors de sa construction dans les ann&eacute;es 1960. Il contient 18 fois le mat&eacute;riau utilis&eacute; dans la Grande Pyramide de Kh&eacute;ops ; Continuez vers les carri&egrave;res de granit qui fournissaient aux anciens &Eacute;gyptiens la plupart des pierres dures utilis&eacute;es dans les pyramides et les temples. Les carri&egrave;res abritent encore le c&eacute;l&egrave;bre <strong>Ob&eacute;lisque inachev&eacute;</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>Ensuite, vous prendrez un bateau &agrave; moteur jusqu\'&agrave; l\'&icirc;le de <strong>Egilka</strong> pour visiter le majestueux <strong>Philae temple</strong> qui &eacute;tait d&eacute;di&eacute; aux d&eacute;esses Isis.</p>\r\n<p>Ensuite, vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute; &agrave; votre bateau de croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil, o&ugrave; vous profiterez des prochaines vacances en croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil de 4 jours / 3 nuits, d\'Assouan jusqu\'&agrave; Louxor, avec des navigations fantastiques et des visites passionnantes. Temps libre &agrave; bord de votre bateau de croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil &agrave; Assouan.</p>'),
(3686, 657, 'de', '„Flug nach Assuan/Sightseeing in Assuan“', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck in Ihrem Hotel und anschlie&szlig;end Transfer zum Flughafen Kairo f&uuml;r Ihren Flug nach Assuan. Bei Ihrer Ankunft werden Sie von einem &Auml;gyptologen empfangen und unterst&uuml;tzt, der Sie auf einer aufregenden Tour zum weltber&uuml;hmten <strong>High</strong> <strong>Staudamm</strong> begleitet, der bei seinem Bau in den 1960er Jahren ein Wunderwerk der Ingenieurskunst war. Es enth&auml;lt das 18-fache des Materials, das in der Gro&szlig;en Cheops-Pyramide verwendet wurde; Weiter geht es zu den Granitsteinbr&uuml;chen, aus denen die alten &Auml;gypter den Gro&szlig;teil des Hartgesteins f&uuml;r Pyramiden und Tempel bezogen. In den Steinbr&uuml;chen befindet sich noch immer der ber&uuml;hmte <strong>unvollendete Obelisk</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>Dann fahren Sie mit dem Motorboot zur Insel <strong>Egilka</strong> und besuchen das majest&auml;tische <strong>Philae Tempel, der der G&ouml;ttin Isis gewidmet war. </strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Dann werden Sie zu Ihrem Nilkreuzfahrtschiff gebracht, wo Sie die n&auml;chsten 4 Tage/3 N&auml;chte Nilkreuzfahrt von Assuan bis nach Luxor mit fantastischen Segeltouren und aufregenden Touren genie&szlig;en werden. Freizeit zur freien Verf&uuml;gung an Bord Ihres Nilkreuzfahrtschiffs in Assuan.</strong></p>'),
(3687, 657, 'it', '“Vola ad Assuan / giro turistico di Assuan”', '<p>Colazione in hotel e poi trasferimento all\'aeroporto del Cairo per il volo per Assuan. All\'arrivo verrai accolto e assistito da un egittologo che ti accompagner&agrave; in un emozionante tour alla famosa <strong>Alta</strong> <strong>Diga</strong> che fu un miracolo dell\'ingegneria quando fu costruita negli anni \'60. Contiene 18 volte il materiale utilizzato nella Grande Piramide di Cheope; proseguire verso le cave di granito che fornivano agli antichi egizi la maggior parte della pietra dura utilizzata nelle piramidi e nei templi. Le cave custodiscono ancora il famoso <strong>Obelisco incompiuto</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>Poi verrai portato in motoscafo all\'isola di <strong>Egilka</strong> per visitare la maestosa <strong>Philae tempio</strong> che era dedicato alla dea Iside.</p>\r\n<p>Quindi verrai trasferito sulla tua nave da crociera sul Nilo, dove potrai goderti la prossima vacanza in crociera sul Nilo di 4 giorni / 3 notti da Assuan fino a Luxor con fantastiche crociere ed emozionanti tour. Tempo libero a bordo della tua nave da crociera sul Nilo ad Assuan.</p>'),
(3688, 657, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3689, 657, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3690, 657, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3691, 658, 'en', '“Abu-Simbel Excursion / Flight back Cairo”', '<p>Enjoy your breakfast aboard your Nile cruise in Aswan: Today is your day for leisure in Aswan with amazing Excursion to <strong>Abu Simbel temples</strong> to discover the magnificent monuments and the majestic two temples of the Abu Simbel that were built by Egypt&rsquo;s great Pharaoh <strong>Ramses II</strong> one is of the Great Pharaoh himself and the second was dedicated for his favorite <strong>wife</strong> <strong>Nefertari</strong> then return back to Aswan with free time at leisure and then you will be transferred to Aswan airport for flight back to Cairo, upon arrival you will be met and assisted by representative who will pick you to you hotel for smooth check-in and overnight.</p>'),
(3692, 658, 'fr', '« Excursion Abou-Simbel / Vol retour Le Caire »', '<p>Profitez de votre petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil &agrave; Assouan : Aujourd\'hui, c\'est votre journ&eacute;e de loisirs &agrave; Assouan avec une incroyable excursion aux <strong>temples d\'Abou Simbel</strong> pour d&eacute;couvrir les magnifiques monuments et les deux majestueux temples d\'Abou Simbel qui ont &eacute;t&eacute; construits par le grand pharaon &eacute;gyptien <strong>Rams&egrave;s II</strong>, l\'un appartient au grand pharaon lui-m&ecirc;me et le second a &eacute;t&eacute; d&eacute;di&eacute; &agrave; son <strong>&eacute;pouse</strong> pr&eacute;f&eacute;r&eacute;e <strong>N&eacute;fertari</strong>, puis revenez &agrave; Assouan avec temps libre, puis vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute; &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport d\'Assouan pour le vol de retour au Caire. &Agrave; votre arriv&eacute;e, vous serez accueilli et assist&eacute; par un repr&eacute;sentant qui viendra vous chercher &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel pour un enregistrement et une nuit en douceur.</p>'),
(3693, 658, 'de', '„Abu-Simbel-Ausflug / Rückflug nach Kairo“', '<p>Genie&szlig;en Sie Ihr Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord Ihrer Nilkreuzfahrt in Assuan: Heute ist Ihr freier Tag in Assuan mit einem fantastischen Ausflug zu den <strong>Abu Simbel-Tempeln</strong>, um die pr&auml;chtigen Monumente und die beiden majest&auml;tischen Tempel von Abu Simbel zu entdecken wurden von &Auml;gyptens gro&szlig;em Pharao <strong>Ramses II</strong> erbaut, eines ist dem gro&szlig;en Pharao selbst gewidmet und das zweite war seiner Lieblingsfrau <strong>Nefertari</strong> gewidmet, zu der sie dann zur&uuml;ckkehrte Freizeit in Assuan. Anschlie&szlig;end werden Sie zum Flughafen Assuan gebracht und zur&uuml;ck nach Kairo geflogen. Bei Ihrer Ankunft werden Sie von einem Vertreter abgeholt und unterst&uuml;tzt, der Sie zu Ihrem Hotel abholt, wo Sie reibungslos einchecken und &uuml;bernachten k&ouml;nnen.</p>'),
(3694, 658, 'it', '“Escursione Abu-Simbel / Volo di ritorno al Cairo”', '<p>Goditi la colazione a bordo della tua crociera sul Nilo ad Assuan: oggi &egrave; la tua giornata di svago ad Assuan con una fantastica escursione ai <strong>templi di Abu Simbel</strong> per scoprire i magnifici monumenti e i maestosi due templi di Abu Simbel che furono costruiti dal grande Faraone egiziano <strong>Ramses II</strong> uno &egrave; del Grande Faraone stesso e il secondo fu dedicato alla sua <strong>moglie</strong> preferita <strong>Nefertari</strong> per poi ritornare a Assuan con tempo libero a disposizione e poi sarai trasferito all\'aeroporto di Assuan per il volo di ritorno al Cairo, all\'arrivo verrai accolto e assistito da un rappresentante che ti verr&agrave; a prendere in hotel per il check-in e il pernottamento senza intoppi.</p>'),
(3695, 658, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3696, 658, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3697, 658, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3698, 659, 'en', '“Nile Cruise Tour”', '<p>Breakfast aboard your Nile cruise ship in Aswan and then you will be accompanied by your Egyptologist guide for an exciting tour to the world famous <strong>High</strong> <strong>Dam</strong> that was an engineering miracle when it was built in the 1960s. It contains 18 times the material used in the Great Pyramid of Cheops; continue to the granite quarries which supplied the ancient Egyptian pharaohs with most of the hard stone used in pyramids and temples. The quarries still hold the famous <strong>Unfinished Obelisk</strong> and then you will be taking by motor-boat to island of Egilka visit the majestic <strong>Philae temple</strong> that was dedicated to the Goddesses Isis. With final <strong>optiona</strong>l evening excursion will offer the <strong>sound and light</strong> show at the <strong>Temple</strong> <strong>of</strong> <strong>Philae</strong> Return to your Nile cruise ship for lunch, afternoon tea and dinner and&nbsp;leisurely free time in Aswan and overnight stay aboard the cruise.</p>'),
(3699, 659, 'fr', '«Croisière sur le Nil»', '<p>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de votre bateau de croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil &agrave; Assouan, puis vous serez accompagn&eacute; par votre guide &eacute;gyptologue pour une visite passionnante du <strong>Haut</strong> <strong>Barrage</strong> de renomm&eacute;e mondiale qui &eacute;tait un miracle d\'ing&eacute;nierie. lors de sa construction dans les ann&eacute;es 1960. Il contient 18 fois le mat&eacute;riau utilis&eacute; dans la Grande Pyramide de Kh&eacute;ops ; Continuez vers les carri&egrave;res de granit qui fournissaient aux anciens pharaons &eacute;gyptiens la plupart des pierres dures utilis&eacute;es dans les pyramides et les temples. Les carri&egrave;res abritent encore le c&eacute;l&egrave;bre <strong>Ob&eacute;lisque inachev&eacute;</strong> et vous prendrez ensuite un bateau &agrave; moteur jusqu\'&agrave; l\'&icirc;le d\'Egilka pour visiter le majestueux <strong>temple de Philae</strong> d&eacute;di&eacute; aux d&eacute;esses Isis. Avec une derni&egrave;re excursion <strong>facultative</strong> en soir&eacute;e, le spectacle <strong>son et lumi&egrave;re</strong> au <strong>Temple</strong> <strong>de</strong> <strong>Philae&lt; /strong&gt; Retournez &agrave; votre bateau de croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil pour le d&eacute;jeuner, le th&eacute; et le d&icirc;ner de l\'apr&egrave;s-midi et temps libre &agrave; Assouan et nuit &agrave; bord de la croisi&egrave;re.</strong></p>'),
(3700, 659, 'de', '„Nilkreuzfahrt-Tour“', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord Ihres Nilkreuzfahrtschiffs in Assuan und dann werden Sie von Ihrem &auml;gyptologischen Reisef&uuml;hrer zu einer aufregenden Tour zum weltber&uuml;hmten <strong>Hohen</strong> <strong>Staudamm</strong> begleitet, der ein Wunder der Ingenieurskunst war als es in den 1960er Jahren gebaut wurde. Es enth&auml;lt das 18-fache des Materials, das in der Gro&szlig;en Cheops-Pyramide verwendet wurde; Weiter geht es zu den Granitsteinbr&uuml;chen, die die alten &auml;gyptischen Pharaonen mit dem Gro&szlig;teil des Hartgesteins versorgten, das in Pyramiden und Tempeln verwendet wurde. In den Steinbr&uuml;chen befindet sich noch immer der ber&uuml;hmte <strong>unvollendete Obelisk</strong>. Anschlie&szlig;end fahren Sie mit dem Motorboot zur Insel Egilka und besuchen den majest&auml;tischen <strong>Philae-Tempel</strong>, der der G&ouml;ttin Isis gewidmet war. Als letzten optionalen Abendausflug wird die <strong>Ton- und Lichtshow</strong> im <strong>Tempel</strong> von <strong>Philae</strong> angeboten /strong&gt; Kehren Sie zum Mittagessen, Nachmittagstee und Abendessen zu Ihrem Nilkreuzfahrtschiff zur&uuml;ck und genie&szlig;en Sie entspannte Freizeit in Assuan und &Uuml;bernachtung an Bord der Kreuzfahrt.</p>'),
(3701, 659, 'it', '“Tour in crociera sul Nilo”', '<p>Colazione a bordo della tua nave da crociera sul Nilo ad Assuan e poi sarai accompagnato dalla tua guida egittologa per un emozionante tour alla famosa <strong>Alta</strong> <strong>Diga</strong> che fu un miracolo dell\'ingegneria quando fu costruito negli anni \'60. Contiene 18 volte il materiale utilizzato nella Grande Piramide di Cheope; proseguire verso le cave di granito che fornivano agli antichi faraoni egiziani la maggior parte della pietra dura utilizzata nelle piramidi e nei templi. Le cave custodiscono ancora il famoso <strong>obelisco incompiuto</strong> e poi verrai portato in motoscafo all\'isola di Egilka per visitare il maestoso <strong>tempio di Philae</strong> dedicato alla dea Iside. Con l\'ultima escursione serale <strong>facoltativa</strong> verr&agrave; offerto lo spettacolo <strong>di</strong> suoni e luci al <strong>Tempio</strong> <strong>di</strong> <strong>Filae&lt; /strong&gt; Rientro alla nave da crociera sul Nilo per pranzo, t&egrave; pomeridiano e cena, tempo libero ad Assuan e pernottamento a bordo della crociera.</strong></p>'),
(3702, 659, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3703, 659, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3704, 659, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3705, 660, 'en', '“Nile Cruise Tour”', '<p>Before breakfast aboard your Nile cruise you may enjoy the amazing sunrise view from your river cruise in with leisurely free time while sailing to Edfu where you will be transferred by a horse drawn carriage to visit the famous <strong>Edfu temple&nbsp;</strong>also known as the temple of <strong>Horus</strong> &amp; <strong>Haroeris</strong>, the <strong>falcon</strong>-<strong>headed</strong> <strong>solar</strong> <strong>War</strong> <strong>God</strong> is the largest and most perfectly preserved of all the Nile temples, back to the Nile cruise by the same way to sail to <strong>Kom Ombo</strong> and visit <strong>temple of Kom-ombo</strong> which is the &nbsp;temple of the crocodile-headed God of fertility and creator of the world, and then return to your Nile cruise to take a relaxing sail to Aswan with lunch, afternoon tea and dinner aboard your cruise and a peaceful overnight stay.</p>'),
(3706, 660, 'fr', '«Croisière sur le Nil»', '<p>Avant le petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil, vous pourrez profiter de la vue imprenable sur le lever du soleil depuis votre croisi&egrave;re fluviale avec du temps libre tout en naviguant vers Edfou o&ugrave; vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute; en cal&egrave;che pour visiter le c&eacute;l&egrave;bre <strong>temple d\'Edfou &eacute;galement connu sous le nom de temple de Horus et Haroeris, le faucon &agrave; t&ecirc;te solaire strong&gt; Guerre Dieu est le plus grand et le mieux conserv&eacute; de tous les temples du Nil, retour &agrave; la croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil par le m&ecirc;me chemin pour naviguer vers Kom Ombo et visiter le temple de Kom -ombo qui est le temple du Dieu de la fertilit&eacute; &agrave; t&ecirc;te de crocodile et cr&eacute;ateur du monde, puis retournez &agrave; votre croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil pour prendre une navigation relaxante vers Assouan avec d&eacute;jeuner, th&eacute; de l\'apr&egrave;s-midi et d&icirc;ner &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re et un nuit paisible reste.</strong></p>'),
(3707, 660, 'de', '„Nilkreuzfahrt-Tour“', '<p>Vor dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord Ihrer Nilkreuzfahrt k&ouml;nnen Sie die atemberaubende Aussicht auf den Sonnenaufgang von Ihrer Flusskreuzfahrt aus genie&szlig;en. Anschlie&szlig;end haben Sie Zeit zur freien Verf&uuml;gung, w&auml;hrend Sie nach Edfu segeln, wo Sie mit einer Pferdekutsche zum ber&uuml;hmten <strong>Edfu-Tempel auch bekannt als der Tempel von Horus und Haroeris, dem falkenk&ouml;pfigen Sonnen stark&gt; War God ist der gr&ouml;&szlig;te und am besten erhaltene aller Niltempel, zur&uuml;ck zur Nilkreuzfahrt auf dem gleichen Weg, um nach Kom Ombo zu segeln Besuchen Sie den Kom-ombo-Tempel, den Tempel des krokodilk&ouml;pfigen Gottes der Fruchtbarkeit und des Sch&ouml;pfers der Welt, und kehren Sie dann zu Ihrer Nilkreuzfahrt zur&uuml;ck, um am Nachmittag eine entspannte Segelfahrt nach Assuan mit Mittagessen zu unternehmen Tee und Abendessen an Bord Ihrer Kreuzfahrt und eine ruhige &Uuml;bernachtung.</strong></p>'),
(3708, 660, 'it', '“Tour in crociera sul Nilo”', '<p>Prima di colazione a bordo della tua crociera sul Nilo, potrai goderti la splendida vista dell\'alba dalla crociera sul fiume con piacevole tempo libero durante la navigazione verso Edfu, dove verrai trasferito su una carrozza trainata da cavalli per visitare il famoso <strong>tempio di Edfu noto anche come tempio di Horus e Haroeris, il falco dalla testa solare War God &egrave; il pi&ugrave; grande e meglio conservato di tutti i templi del Nilo, per tornare alla crociera sul Nilo allo stesso modo per navigare verso Kom Ombo e visita il tempio di Kom-ombo che &egrave; il tempio del dio della fertilit&agrave; dalla testa di coccodrillo e creatore del mondo, quindi torna alla crociera sul Nilo per fare una rilassante navigazione verso Assuan con pranzo , t&egrave; pomeridiano e cena a bordo della tua crociera e tranquillo pernottamento.</strong></p>'),
(3709, 660, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3710, 660, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3711, 660, 'zh', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `tour_day_translations` (`id`, `tour_day_id`, `locale`, `title`, `description`) VALUES
(3712, 661, 'en', '“Nile Cruise Tour”', '<p>Breakfast onboard the Nile cruise in Luxor, and then you will be accompanied by your expert guide and driver to enjoy a visit to the West Bank of the river Nile to visit the two colossal statues of Amenhotep III (<strong>Colossi of Memnon</strong>), and then <strong>visit the Valley of the Kings</strong>, where the magnificent tombs discovered, those tombs were carved deep into the desert rock, richly decorated and filled with treasures for the afterlife of the pharaohs, then you will visit 3 tombs. You will also have the chance to visit the <strong>Hatshepsut temple</strong> at El Deir El Bahary, this impressive temple dedicated to the Queen Hatshepsut the only female pharaoh who rises out of the desert plain in a series of terraces and merges with the sheer limestone cliffs that surround it then back to the cruise to sail to Edfu via Esna Lock with lunch, afternoon tea and dinner aboard your cruise and overnight stay.</p>'),
(3713, 661, 'fr', '«Croisière sur le Nil»', '<p>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de la croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil &agrave; Louxor, puis vous serez accompagn&eacute; de votre guide expert et de votre chauffeur pour profiter d\'une visite sur la rive ouest du Nil pour visiter les deux statues colossales d\'Amenhotep III (<strong>Colosses de Memnon</strong>), puis <strong>visiter la Vall&eacute;e des Rois</strong>, o&ugrave; ont &eacute;t&eacute; d&eacute;couverts les magnifiques tombeaux, ces tombeaux ont &eacute;t&eacute; creus&eacute;s profond&eacute;ment dans la roche du d&eacute;sert, richement d&eacute;cor&eacute;s et remplis de tr&eacute;sors pour le l\'au-del&agrave; des pharaons, puis vous visiterez 3 tombeaux. Vous aurez &eacute;galement la chance de visiter le <strong>temple d\'Hatchepsout</strong> &agrave; El Deir El Bahary, cet impressionnant temple d&eacute;di&eacute; &agrave; la reine Hatshepsout, la seule femme pharaon qui surgit de la plaine d&eacute;sertique en une s&eacute;rie de terrasses et se fond avec les falaises calcaires abruptes qui l\'entourent, puis retour &agrave; la croisi&egrave;re pour naviguer vers Edfou via l\'&eacute;cluse d\'Esna avec d&eacute;jeuner, th&eacute; de l\'apr&egrave;s-midi et d&icirc;ner &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re et nuit.</p>'),
(3714, 661, 'de', '„Nilkreuzfahrt-Tour“', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord der Nilkreuzfahrt in Luxor. Anschlie&szlig;end genie&szlig;en Sie in Begleitung Ihres fachkundigen Reiseleiters und Fahrers einen Besuch am Westufer des Nils, wo Sie die beiden kolossalen Statuen von Amenhotep III Memnon) und <strong>besuchen Sie dann das Tal der K&ouml;nige</strong>, wo die pr&auml;chtigen Gr&auml;ber entdeckt wurden. Diese Gr&auml;ber wurden tief in den W&uuml;stenfelsen gehauen, reich verziert und gef&uuml;llt mit Sch&auml;tzen f&uuml;r das Leben nach dem Tod Pharaonen, dann besuchen Sie 3 Gr&auml;ber. Sie haben auch die M&ouml;glichkeit, den <strong>Hatschepsut-Tempel</strong> in El Deir El Bahary zu besuchen, diesen beeindruckenden Tempel, der der K&ouml;nigin Hatschepsut gewidmet ist, der einzigen weiblichen Pharaonin, die sich in einer Reihe von Terrassen und &Uuml;berg&auml;ngen aus der W&uuml;stenebene erhebt mit den steilen Kalksteinfelsen, die es umgeben, dann zur&uuml;ck zur Kreuzfahrt, um &uuml;ber die Esna-Schleuse nach Edfu zu segeln, Mittagessen, Nachmittagstee und Abendessen an Bord Ihrer Kreuzfahrt und &Uuml;bernachtung.</p>'),
(3715, 661, 'it', '“Tour in crociera sul Nilo”', '<p>Colazione a bordo della crociera sul Nilo a Luxor, quindi sarai accompagnato dalla tua guida esperta e autista per goderti una visita sulla sponda occidentale del fiume Nilo per visitare le due colossali statue di Amenhotep III (<strong>Colossi di Memnon</strong>), e poi <strong>visitare la Valle dei Re</strong>, dove furono scoperte le magnifiche tombe, quelle tombe furono scavate in profondit&agrave; nella roccia del deserto, riccamente decorate e piene di tesori per l\'aldil&agrave; dei faraoni, poi visiterai 3 tombe. Avrai anche la possibilit&agrave; di visitare il <strong>tempio di Hatshepsut</strong> a El Deir El Bahary, questo imponente tempio dedicato alla regina Hatshepsut, l\'unico faraone donna che si erge dalla pianura desertica in una serie di terrazze e si fonde con le ripide scogliere calcaree che la circondano, poi ritorno alla crociera per raggiungere Edfu via Esna Lock con pranzo, t&egrave; pomeridiano e cena a bordo della crociera e pernottamento.</p>'),
(3716, 661, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3717, 661, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3718, 661, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3719, 662, 'en', '“Fly to Luxor / East Bank Tour”', '<p>Breakfast at the hotel, and then you will be transferred to Cairo airport for our flight to Luxor, upon arrival you will be met and assisted by your own Egyptologist expert guide to visit <strong>Karnak Temple</strong>, the largest place of worship ever built. Its ancient name Ipet-isut means the most sacred of places. The temple, or, more correctly, the complex of temples, was built more than two thousand years ago by generation after generation of pharaohs. Within the complex, the great Hypostyle Hall is an incredible forest of giant pillars. Then you will be transferred to the majestic <strong>Luxor temple</strong> which built by Amenhotep III and Ramses II for ritual and festivals and dedicated to the god Amun Then enjoy some free time for shopping in Luxor and then you will be transferred to your Nile cruise ship in Luxor for embarkation with lunch afternoon tea, dinner and overnight stay in Luxor aboard Nile cruise. Tonight there is a chance to join and enjoy an <strong>optional</strong> <strong>sound and light show</strong> at the <strong>Temple of Karnak.</strong></p>'),
(3720, 662, 'fr', '«Envolez-vous vers Louxor / Tour de la Rive Est»', '<p>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; l\'h&ocirc;tel, puis transfert &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport du Caire pour notre vol vers Louxor. &Agrave; votre arriv&eacute;e, vous serez accueilli et assist&eacute; par votre propre guide expert &eacute;gyptologue pour visiter le <strong>Temple de Karnak</strong>, le le plus grand lieu de culte jamais construit. Son ancien nom Ipet-isut signifie le lieu le plus sacr&eacute;. Le temple, ou plus exactement le complexe de temples, a &eacute;t&eacute; construit il y a plus de deux mille ans par des g&eacute;n&eacute;rations de pharaons. Au sein du complexe, la grande salle hypostyle est une incroyable for&ecirc;t de piliers g&eacute;ants. Ensuite, vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute; au majestueux <strong>temple de Louxor</strong> construit par Amenhotep III et Rams&egrave;s II pour les rituels et les festivals et d&eacute;di&eacute; au dieu Amon. Profitez ensuite d\'un peu de temps libre pour faire du shopping &agrave; Louxor, puis vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute;. &agrave; votre bateau de croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil &agrave; Louxor pour l\'embarquement avec d&eacute;jeuner, th&eacute; de l\'apr&egrave;s-midi, d&icirc;ner et nuit &agrave; Louxor &agrave; bord de la croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil. Ce soir, vous avez la possibilit&eacute; de participer et de profiter d\'un <strong>spectacle son et lumi&egrave;re</strong> <strong>facultatif</strong> au <strong>Temple de Karnak.</strong></p>'),
(3721, 662, 'de', '„Flug nach Luxor / East Bank Tour“', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck im Hotel und anschlie&szlig;end Transfer zum Flughafen Kairo f&uuml;r unseren Flug nach Luxor. Bei Ihrer Ankunft werden Sie von Ihrem eigenen &Auml;gyptologen-Expertenf&uuml;hrer abgeholt und unterst&uuml;tzt, um den <strong>Karnak-Tempel</strong> zu besuchen gr&ouml;&szlig;te jemals gebaute Kultst&auml;tte. Sein alter Name Ipet-isut bedeutet der heiligste aller Orte. Der Tempel, oder genauer gesagt der Tempelkomplex, wurde vor mehr als zweitausend Jahren von Generationen von Pharaonen erbaut. Innerhalb des Komplexes ist die gro&szlig;e Hypostyle-Halle ein unglaublicher Wald aus riesigen S&auml;ulen. Dann werden Sie zum majest&auml;tischen <strong>Luxor-Tempel</strong> gebracht, der von Amenophis III. und Ramses II. f&uuml;r Rituale und Feste erbaut und dem Gott Amun geweiht wurde. Anschlie&szlig;end haben Sie etwas freie Zeit zum Einkaufen in Luxor und werden dann transferiert Fahrt zu Ihrem Nilkreuzfahrtschiff in Luxor zur Einschiffung mit Mittagessen, Nachmittagstee, Abendessen und &Uuml;bernachtung in Luxor an Bord einer Nilkreuzfahrt. Heute Abend besteht die M&ouml;glichkeit, an einer <strong>optionalen</strong> <strong>Ton- und Lichtshow</strong> im <strong>Karnak-Tempel</strong></p>\r\n<p>teilzunehmen</p>'),
(3722, 662, 'it', '“Vola a Luxor / Tour della sponda orientale”', '<p>Colazione in hotel e poi trasferimento all\'aeroporto del Cairo per il nostro volo per Luxor, all\'arrivo verrai accolto e assistito dalla tua guida esperta egittologa per visitare il <strong>Tempio di Karnak</strong>, il il pi&ugrave; grande luogo di culto mai costruito. Il suo antico nome Ipet-isut significa il pi&ugrave; sacro dei luoghi. Il tempio, o, pi&ugrave; correttamente, il complesso dei templi, fu costruito pi&ugrave; di duemila anni fa da generazione dopo generazione di faraoni. All\'interno del complesso, la grande Sala Ipostila &egrave; un\'incredibile foresta di pilastri giganti. Quindi verrai trasferito al maestoso <strong>tempio di Luxor</strong> costruito da Amenhotep III e Ramses II per rituali e feste e dedicato al dio Amon. Quindi goditi un po\' di tempo libero per lo shopping a Luxor e poi verrai trasferito alla tua nave da crociera sul Nilo a Luxor per l\'imbarco con pranzo, t&egrave; pomeridiano, cena e pernottamento a Luxor a bordo della crociera sul Nilo. Stasera c\'&egrave; la possibilit&agrave; di partecipare e godersi uno <strong>spettacolo di suoni e luci</strong> <strong>facoltativo</strong> al <strong>Tempio di Karnak.</strong></p>'),
(3723, 662, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3724, 662, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3725, 662, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3726, 663, 'en', 'Egyptian Museum & the Pyramids', '<p>Our representative will pick you up from your hotel in Cairo or Giza at 8:00 AM</p>\r\n<p>First, With Us, you will take a wonderful tour to discover the pyramids of Giza, the Great Pyramid of King Khufu, its height is 148 m, the second pyramid of King Khafre, its height is 137 m, and the third pyramid of King Menkaure, its height is 68. and next you will enjoy making nice photos&nbsp; done by a professional and specialized photographer, then we enjoy visiting the Sphinx,</p>\r\n<p>continue your&nbsp; tour to the Egyptian Museum of Antiquities. It displays the largest and most valuable pieces of Egyptian art in the world</p>\r\n<p>It displays a rare collection of more than 150,000 original artifacts dating back up to 5,000 years, including the treasures of the Golden Pharaoh Tutankhamun - discovered by Howard Carter in 1921 and dating back more than 3,500 years. The most important exhibit is the Golden Mask It weighs 11 kg of pure gold, as well as the golden sarcophagus and weighs 110 kg of pure gold</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp; After completing the visit to the Egyptian Museum, you will pass by Tahrir Square, where the Egyptian revolution began in 2011. Then we will move to the restaurant for lunch and your tour will end by returning to your hotel</p>'),
(3727, 663, 'fr', 'Musée égyptien et pyramides', '<p>Notre repr&eacute;sentant viendra vous chercher &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel au Caire ou &agrave; Gizeh &agrave; 8h00</p>\r\n<p>Tout d\'abord, avec nous, vous ferez une merveilleuse visite pour d&eacute;couvrir les pyramides de Gizeh, la Grande Pyramide de Le roi Kh&eacute;ops, sa hauteur est de 148 m, la deuxi&egrave;me pyramide du roi Khafr&eacute;, sa hauteur est de 137 m, et la troisi&egrave;me pyramide du roi Menkaure, sa hauteur est de 68. et ensuite vous prendrez plaisir &agrave; faire de belles photos r&eacute;alis&eacute;es par un professionnel et sp&eacute;cialis&eacute;. photographe, puis nous profiterons de la visite du Sphinx,</p>\r\n<p>continuez votre visite au Mus&eacute;e &eacute;gyptien des antiquit&eacute;s. Il pr&eacute;sente les &oelig;uvres d\'art &eacute;gyptiennes les plus grandes et les plus pr&eacute;cieuses au monde.</p>\r\n<p>Il pr&eacute;sente une collection rare de plus de 150 000 objets originaux remontant &agrave; 5 000 ans, y compris les tr&eacute;sors du pharaon d\'or Toutankhamon - d&eacute;couverts par Howard Carter en 1921 et il y a plus de 3 500 ans. L\'exposition la plus importante est le masque d\'or. Il p&egrave;se 11 kg d\'or pur, ainsi que le sarcophage dor&eacute; et p&egrave;se 110 kg d\'or pur.</p>\r\n<p>Apr&egrave;s avoir termin&eacute; la visite du mus&eacute;e &eacute;gyptien, vous passerez par Tahrir. Place, o&ugrave; la r&eacute;volution &eacute;gyptienne a commenc&eacute; en 2011. Ensuite, nous nous dirigerons vers le restaurant pour le d&eacute;jeuner et votre visite se terminera par le retour &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel</p>'),
(3728, 663, 'de', 'Ägyptisches Museum und die Pyramiden', '<p>Unser Vertreter holt Sie um 8:00 Uhr von Ihrem Hotel in Kairo oder Gizeh ab.</p>\r\n<p>Zun&auml;chst unternehmen Sie mit uns eine wundervolle Tour, um die Pyramiden von Gizeh, die Gro&szlig;e Pyramide von, zu entdecken K&ouml;nig Khufu, ihre H&ouml;he betr&auml;gt 148 m, die zweite Pyramide von K&ouml;nig Khafre, ihre H&ouml;he betr&auml;gt 137 m, und die dritte Pyramide von K&ouml;nig Mykerinos, ihre H&ouml;he betr&auml;gt 68 m. Und als N&auml;chstes werden Sie Spa&szlig; daran haben, sch&ouml;ne Fotos zu machen, die von einem Profi und Spezialisten gemacht wurden Fotograf, dann genie&szlig;en wir den Besuch der Sphinx.</p>\r\n<p>Setzen Sie Ihre Tour zum &Auml;gyptischen Museum f&uuml;r Altert&uuml;mer fort. Es zeigt die gr&ouml;&szlig;ten und wertvollsten &auml;gyptischen Kunstwerke der Welt</p>\r\n<p>Es zeigt eine seltene Sammlung von mehr als 150.000 Originalartefakten, die bis zu 5.000 Jahre alt sind, darunter die Sch&auml;tze des goldenen Pharaos Tutanchamun &ndash; entdeckt von Howard Carter im Jahr 1921 und ist mehr als 3.500 Jahre alt. Das wichtigste Ausstellungsst&uuml;ck ist die Goldene Maske. Sie wiegt 11 kg reines Gold, ebenso wie der goldene Sarkophag, der 110 kg reines Gold wiegt</p>\r\n<p>Nach Abschluss des Besuchs im &Auml;gyptischen Museum passieren Sie Tahrir Platz, wo 2011 die &auml;gyptische Revolution begann. Dann gehen wir zum Mittagessen ins Restaurant und Ihre Tour endet mit der R&uuml;ckkehr zu Ihrem Hotel</p>'),
(3729, 663, 'it', 'Museo Egizio e Piramidi', '<p>Il nostro rappresentante verr&agrave; a prendervi al vostro hotel al Cairo o a Giza alle 8:00</p>\r\n<p>Per prima cosa, con noi, farai un meraviglioso tour alla scoperta delle piramidi di Giza, la Grande Piramide di Re Khufu, la sua altezza &egrave; di 148 m, la seconda piramide di Re Khafre, la sua altezza &egrave; di 137 m, e la terza piramide di Re Menkaure, la sua altezza &egrave; di 68. e poi ti divertirai a fare belle foto fatte da un professionista e specializzato fotografo, poi ci divertiamo a visitare la Sfinge,</p>\r\n<p>continua il tuo tour al Museo delle antichit&agrave; egizie. Espone le opere d\'arte egizia pi&ugrave; grandi e preziose al mondo</p>\r\n<p>Espone una rara collezione di oltre 150.000 manufatti originali risalenti fino a 5.000 anni fa, inclusi i tesori del faraone d\'oro Tutankhamon, scoperti da Howard Carter nel 1921 e risalente a pi&ugrave; di 3.500 anni fa. Il reperto pi&ugrave; importante &egrave; la Maschera d\'oro. Pesa 11 kg di oro puro, cos&igrave; come il sarcofago d\'oro e pesa 110 kg di oro puro</p>\r\n<p>Dopo aver completato la visita al Museo Egizio, passerai da Tahrir Square, dove &egrave; iniziata la rivoluzione egiziana nel 2011. Successivamente ci sposteremo al ristorante per il pranzo e il tour terminer&agrave; con il ritorno in hotel</p>'),
(3730, 663, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3731, 663, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3732, 663, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3733, 664, 'en', 'Day Tour Pyramids, The Museum & The Citadel', '<p>Our representative will pick you up from your hotel in Cairo or Giza at 8:00 AM</p>\r\n<p>First, With Our Representative, you will take a wonderful tour to discover the pyramids of Giza, the Great Pyramid of King Khufu, its height is 148 m, the second pyramid of King Khafre, its height is 137 m, and the third pyramid of King Menkaure, its height is 68. and next you will enjoy making nice photos&nbsp;done by a professional and specialized photographer, then we enjoy visiting the Sphinx,&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>continue your&nbsp; tour to the Egyptian Museum of Antiquities. It displays the largest and most valuable pieces of Egyptian art in the world</p>\r\n<p>It displays a rare collection of more than 150,000 original artifacts dating back up to 5,000 years, including the treasures of the Golden Pharaoh Tutankhamun - discovered by Howard Carter in 1921 and dating back more than 3,500 years. The most important exhibit is the Golden Mask It weighs 11 kg of pure gold, as well as the golden sarcophagus and weighs 110 kg of pure gold</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp; After completing the visit to the Egyptian Museum, you will pass by Tahrir Square, where the Egyptian revolution began in 2011 Then we move to visit the Saladin Castle, which is a defensive fortress dating back to the Middle Ages and was built by Salah al-Din al-Ayyubi to protect Cairo against any attacks from the Crusaders. It was built of limestone. We will enjoy visiting the high defensive walls and huge defensive towers. Inside the castle there is the most important mosque in Egypt And the Islamic world, which is the Mosque of Muhammad Ali Pasha, which was built between 1830 and 1840. It is built with very pure marble, and that is why it is called the Alabaster Mosque. Then we take beautiful souvenir photos in the panorama area and then return to the hotel.</p>'),
(3734, 664, 'fr', 'Excursion d\'une journée aux pyramides, au musée et à la citadelle', '<p>Notre repr&eacute;sentant viendra vous chercher &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel au Caire ou &agrave; Gizeh &agrave; 8h00</p>\r\n<p>Tout d\'abord, avec notre repr&eacute;sentant, vous ferez une merveilleuse visite pour d&eacute;couvrir les pyramides de Gizeh, la Grande Pyramide. du roi Kh&eacute;ops, sa hauteur est de 148 m, la deuxi&egrave;me pyramide du roi Khafr&eacute;, sa hauteur est de 137 m, et la troisi&egrave;me pyramide du roi Menkaure, sa hauteur est de 68. et ensuite vous prendrez plaisir &agrave; faire de belles photos r&eacute;alis&eacute;es par un professionnel et photographe sp&eacute;cialis&eacute;, puis nous profiterons de la visite du Sphinx,</p>\r\n<p>continuez votre visite au Mus&eacute;e &eacute;gyptien des antiquit&eacute;s. Il pr&eacute;sente les &oelig;uvres d\'art &eacute;gyptiennes les plus grandes et les plus pr&eacute;cieuses au monde.</p>\r\n<p>Il pr&eacute;sente une collection rare de plus de 150 000 objets originaux remontant &agrave; 5 000 ans, y compris les tr&eacute;sors du pharaon d\'or Toutankhamon - d&eacute;couverts par Howard Carter en 1921 et il y a plus de 3 500 ans. L\'exposition la plus importante est le masque d\'or. Il p&egrave;se 11 kg d\'or pur, ainsi que le sarcophage dor&eacute; et p&egrave;se 110 kg d\'or pur.</p>\r\n<p>Apr&egrave;s avoir termin&eacute; la visite du mus&eacute;e &eacute;gyptien, vous passerez par Tahrir. Place, o&ugrave; la r&eacute;volution &eacute;gyptienne a commenc&eacute; en 2011. Ensuite, nous visiterons le ch&acirc;teau de Saladin, qui est une forteresse d&eacute;fensive datant du Moyen &Acirc;ge et construite par Salah al-Din al-Ayyubi pour prot&eacute;ger le Caire. contre toute attaque des crois&eacute;s. Elle a &eacute;t&eacute; construite en pierre calcaire. Nous appr&eacute;cierons visiter les hauts murs d&eacute;fensifs et les immenses tours d&eacute;fensives. &Agrave; l\'int&eacute;rieur du ch&acirc;teau se trouve la mosqu&eacute;e la plus importante d\'&Eacute;gypte et du monde islamique, la mosqu&eacute;e de Muhammad Ali Pacha, construite entre 1830 et 1840. Elle est construite avec du marbre tr&egrave;s pur, c\'est pourquoi elle est appel&eacute;e l\'alb&acirc;tre. Mosqu&eacute;e. Ensuite, nous prenons de belles photos souvenirs dans la zone panoramique puis retournons &agrave; l\'h&ocirc;tel.</p>'),
(3735, 664, 'de', 'Tagestour Pyramiden, Museum und Zitadelle', '<p>Unser Vertreter holt Sie um 8:00 Uhr von Ihrem Hotel in Kairo oder Gizeh ab.</p>\r\n<p>Zun&auml;chst unternehmen Sie mit unserem Vertreter eine wundervolle Tour, um die Pyramiden von Gizeh, die Gro&szlig;e Pyramide, zu entdecken Die Pyramide von K&ouml;nig Cheops ist 148 m hoch, die zweite Pyramide von K&ouml;nig Chephren ist 137 m hoch und die dritte Pyramide von K&ouml;nig Mykerinos ist 68 m hoch. Anschlie&szlig;end k&ouml;nnen Sie sch&ouml;ne Fotos machen, die von einem Profi und Spezialisten gemacht wurden Fotograf, dann genie&szlig;en wir den Besuch der Sphinx.</p>\r\n<p>Setzen Sie Ihre Tour zum &Auml;gyptischen Museum f&uuml;r Altert&uuml;mer fort. Es zeigt die gr&ouml;&szlig;ten und wertvollsten &auml;gyptischen Kunstwerke der Welt</p>\r\n<p>Es zeigt eine seltene Sammlung von mehr als 150.000 Originalartefakten, die bis zu 5.000 Jahre alt sind, darunter die Sch&auml;tze des goldenen Pharaos Tutanchamun &ndash; entdeckt von Howard Carter im Jahr 1921 und ist mehr als 3.500 Jahre alt. Das wichtigste Ausstellungsst&uuml;ck ist die Goldene Maske. Sie wiegt 11 kg reines Gold, ebenso wie der goldene Sarkophag, der 110 kg reines Gold wiegt</p>\r\n<p>Nach Abschluss des Besuchs im &Auml;gyptischen Museum passieren Sie Tahrir Platz, auf dem 2011 die &auml;gyptische Revolution begann. Anschlie&szlig;end besuchen wir die Burg Saladin, eine Verteidigungsfestung aus dem Mittelalter, die von Salah al-Din al-Ayyubi erbaut wurde, um Kairo vor Angriffen der Kreuzfahrer zu sch&uuml;tzen. Es wurde aus Kalkstein gebaut. Wir werden es genie&szlig;en, die hohen Verteidigungsmauern und riesigen Verteidigungst&uuml;rme zu besichtigen. Im Inneren der Burg befindet sich die wichtigste Moschee &Auml;gyptens und der islamischen Welt, die Moschee von Muhammad Ali Pascha, die zwischen 1830 und 1840 erbaut wurde. Sie besteht aus sehr reinem Marmor und wird deshalb Alabaster genannt Moschee. Anschlie&szlig;end machen wir sch&ouml;ne Erinnerungsfotos im Panoramabereich und kehren dann zur&uuml;ck zum Hotel.</p>'),
(3736, 664, 'it', 'Tour di un giorno Piramidi, Museo e Cittadella', '<p>Il nostro rappresentante verr&agrave; a prenderti dal tuo hotel al Cairo o Giza alle 8:00</p>\r\n<p>Per prima cosa, con il nostro rappresentante, farai un meraviglioso tour alla scoperta delle piramidi di Giza, la Grande Piramide del re Cheope, la sua altezza &egrave; di 148 m, la seconda piramide del re Chefren, la sua altezza &egrave; di 137 m, e la terza piramide del re Menkaure, la sua altezza &egrave; di 68. e poi ti divertirai a fare belle foto fatte da un professionista e specializzato fotografo, poi ci divertiamo a visitare la Sfinge,</p>\r\n<p>continua il tuo tour al Museo delle Antichit&agrave; Egizie. Espone le opere d\'arte egizia pi&ugrave; grandi e preziose al mondo</p>\r\n<p>Espone una rara collezione di oltre 150.000 manufatti originali risalenti fino a 5.000 anni fa, inclusi i tesori del faraone d\'oro Tutankhamon, scoperti da Howard Carter nel 1921 e risalente a pi&ugrave; di 3.500 anni fa. Il reperto pi&ugrave; importante &egrave; la Maschera d\'oro. Pesa 11 kg di oro puro, cos&igrave; come il sarcofago d\'oro e pesa 110 kg di oro puro</p>\r\n<p>Dopo aver completato la visita al Museo Egizio, passerai da Tahrir Square, dove inizi&ograve; la rivoluzione egiziana nel 2011. Successivamente ci spostiamo a visitare il Castello di Saladino, che &egrave; una fortezza difensiva risalente al Medioevo e fu costruita da Salah al-Din al-Ayyubi per proteggere il Cairo da eventuali attacchi dei crociati. Era costruito in pietra calcarea. Ci divertiremo a visitare le alte mura difensive e le enormi torri difensive. All\'interno del castello si trova la moschea pi&ugrave; importante dell\'Egitto e del mondo islamico, ovvero la Moschea di Muhammad Ali Pasha, che fu costruita tra il 1830 e il 1840. &Egrave; costruita con marmo purissimo, ed &egrave; per questo che &egrave; chiamata l\'Alabastro Moschea. Successivamente scattiamo bellissime foto ricordo nella zona panoramica e poi ritorniamo in hotel.</p>'),
(3737, 664, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3738, 664, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3739, 664, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3740, 665, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Visiting the Nubian village is a must when you are in Aswan. Between all Aswan attractions, this could be the only trip that will capture your heart in all meanings. The Nubian people are so friendly and overwhelming, great hospitality will be waiting for you in one of the Nubian family houses. They have dark skin and speak a language called Nuba or Nubian. Some said they consider their language as a very sacred custom of their own and refuse to teach it to any foreigner.&nbsp; The Nubian houses are made of mud and often colored blue or orange. Palm trees and gardens are everywhere; they raise chickens and goats mostly on their farms. Some locals if not farming, they would live from selling handicrafts and women drawing Henna for tourists. Such a wonderful trip for adults, kids, and all ages. Book Aswan Nubian Village Tour Day Trip Now &amp; Enjoy the best local experience.</p>'),
(3741, 665, 'fr', 'Jour 1', '<p>La visite du village nubien est un incontournable lorsque vous &ecirc;tes &agrave; Assouan. Entre toutes les attractions d\'Assouan, cela pourrait &ecirc;tre le seul voyage qui captivera votre c&oelig;ur dans tous les sens. Le peuple nubien est si sympathique et chaleureux qu\'une grande hospitalit&eacute; vous attend dans l\'une des maisons familiales nubiennes. Ils ont la peau fonc&eacute;e et parlent une langue appel&eacute;e Nuba ou Nubien. Certains ont d&eacute;clar&eacute; qu&rsquo;ils consid&eacute;raient leur langue comme une coutume tr&egrave;s sacr&eacute;e et refusaient de l&rsquo;enseigner &agrave; un &eacute;tranger. Les maisons nubiennes sont faites de boue et souvent color&eacute;es en bleu ou orange. Les palmiers et les jardins sont partout ; ils &eacute;l&egrave;vent des poulets et des ch&egrave;vres principalement dans leurs fermes. Certains habitants, s\'ils ne cultivaient pas, vivaient de la vente d\'objets artisanaux et de femmes dessinant du henn&eacute; pour les touristes. Un voyage merveilleux pour les adultes, les enfants et tous les &acirc;ges. R&eacute;servez d&egrave;s maintenant l\'excursion d\'une journ&eacute;e dans le village nubien d\'Assouan et profitez de la meilleure exp&eacute;rience locale.</p>'),
(3742, 665, 'de', 'Tag 1', '<p>Der Besuch des nubischen Dorfes ist ein Muss, wenn Sie in Assuan sind. Unter all den Sehensw&uuml;rdigkeiten Assuans k&ouml;nnte dies die einzige Reise sein, die Ihr Herz in jeder Hinsicht erobern wird. Das nubische Volk ist so freundlich und &uuml;berw&auml;ltigend, dass Sie in einem der nubischen Familienh&auml;user gro&szlig;artige Gastfreundschaft erwartet. Sie haben dunkle Haut und sprechen eine Sprache namens Nuba oder Nubiisch. Einige sagten, sie betrachten ihre Sprache als einen sehr heiligen Brauch und weigern sich, sie einem Ausl&auml;nder beizubringen. Die nubischen H&auml;user bestehen aus Lehm und sind oft blau oder orange gef&auml;rbt. &Uuml;berall gibt es Palmen und G&auml;rten; Sie z&uuml;chten haupts&auml;chlich H&uuml;hner und Ziegen auf ihren H&ouml;fen. Einige Einheimische lebten, wenn sie nicht in der Landwirtschaft t&auml;tig waren, vom Verkauf von Kunsthandwerk und von Frauen, die Henna f&uuml;r Touristen zeichneten. Was f&uuml;r eine wundervolle Reise f&uuml;r Erwachsene, Kinder und alle Altersgruppen. Buchen Sie jetzt einen Tagesausflug zum nubischen Dorf Assuan und genie&szlig;en Sie das beste Erlebnis vor Ort.</p>'),
(3743, 665, 'it', 'Giorno 1', '<p>Visitare il villaggio nubiano &egrave; d\'obbligo quando ti trovi ad Assuan. Tra tutte le attrazioni di Assuan, questo potrebbe essere l\'unico viaggio che catturer&agrave; il tuo cuore in tutti i significati. Il popolo nubiano &egrave; cos&igrave; amichevole e travolgente, una grande ospitalit&agrave; ti aspetter&agrave; in una delle case della famiglia nubiana. Hanno la pelle scura e parlano una lingua chiamata Nuba o Nubiano. Alcuni hanno affermato di considerare la loro lingua come un\'usanza molto sacra e di rifiutarsi di insegnarla a qualsiasi straniero. Le case nubiane sono fatte di fango e spesso colorate di blu o arancione. Palme e giardini sono ovunque; allevano polli e capre principalmente nelle loro fattorie. Alcuni locali, se non coltivassero, vivrebbero vendendo prodotti artigianali e donne che disegnavano l\'henn&eacute; per i turisti. Un viaggio cos&igrave; meraviglioso per adulti, bambini e tutte le et&agrave;. Prenota subito la gita di un giorno al tour del villaggio nubiano di Assuan e goditi la migliore esperienza locale.</p>'),
(3744, 665, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3745, 665, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3746, 665, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3747, 666, 'en', 'Giza Pyramids, Memphis and Sakkara Tour', '<p><strong>Pyramids of Giza: ( 3hours)</strong><br>Giza Pyramids where you Visit the Great Pyramids Of Giza - Cheops ,Chephren &amp; Mykerinos then Visit the Valley Temple The Place where the Priests Mummified the dead body of king Chephren owner of the second pyramid at Giza Platue Also it`s the same place where you Can have a close-up look at the Sphinx - The legendary guardian that stands by the huge funeral complex with its lion body and the head of king Chephren&nbsp;<br><br><strong>Great Pyramid of Cheops (Khufu) &nbsp;( 30 minutes )</strong><br>Khufu\'s pyramid complex consists of a valley temple, now buried beneath the village of Nazlet el-Samman; diabase paving and nummulitic limestone walls have been found but the site has not been excavated<br><br><br><strong>Khafre\'s Pyramid (30 minutes )</strong><br>Khafre\'s pyramid complex consists of a valley temple, the Sphinx temple, a causeway, a mortuary temple and the king\'s pyramid. The valley temple yielded several statues of Khafre. Several were found in a well in the floor of the temple by Mariette in 1860<br><br><strong>Menkaure Pyramid (30 minutes )</strong><br>Menkaure\'s pyramid complex consists of a valley temple, a causeway, a mortuary temple, and the king\'s pyramid. The valley temple once contained several statues of Menkaure. During the 5th Dynasty, a smaller ante-temple was added on to the valley temple. The mortuary temple also yielded several statues of Menkaure.&nbsp;<br><br><strong>Great Sphinx (30 minutes )</strong><br>The Sphinx dates from the reign of king Khafre.[7] During the New Kingdom, Amenhotep II dedicated a new temple to Hauron-Haremakhet and this structure was added onto by later rulers&nbsp;<br><br><strong>Saqqara (Sakkara) (2 hours)</strong><br>&nbsp;Pyramids Sakkara, located only 27 km southwest away from Cairo. Visit the Step Pyramid (Built for king Zoser), it is considered an important part of the process of the pyramid evolution, which were made from the simple mastaba to its widely known form&nbsp;<br><br><strong>Mit Rahina Museum (1 hour )</strong><br>Memphis City that was the ancient capital of Egypt, where the colossal statue of Ramses II and the great Alabaster Sphinx are. this City Dates back to 3100 B.C&nbsp;</p>'),
(3748, 666, 'fr', 'Visite des pyramides de Gizeh, de Memphis et de Sakkara', '<p><strong>Pyramides de Gizeh : (3 heures)</strong><br>Pyramides de Gizeh o&ugrave; vous visitez les grandes pyramides de Gizeh - Kh&eacute;ops, Chephren et Mykerinos puis visitez le temple de la vall&eacute;e, le lieu o&ugrave; les pr&ecirc;tres ont momifi&eacute; le cadavre du roi Chephren, propri&eacute;taire de la deuxi&egrave;me pyramide de Gizeh Platue. C\'est &eacute;galement le m&ecirc;me endroit o&ugrave; vous pouvez observer de pr&egrave;s le Sphinx - Le gardien l&eacute;gendaire qui se tient pr&egrave;s de l\'immense complexe fun&eacute;raire avec son corps de lion et la t&ecirc;te du roi. Chephren <br><br><strong>Grande Pyramide de Kh&eacute;ops (Khoufou) ( 30 minutes )</strong><br>Le complexe pyramidal de Kh&eacute;ops se compose d\'un temple de la vall&eacute;e, maintenant enterr&eacute; sous le village de Nazlet el-Samman ; des pav&eacute;s en diabase et des murs en calcaire nummulitique ont &eacute;t&eacute; trouv&eacute;s mais le site n\'a pas &eacute;t&eacute; fouill&eacute;<br><br><br><strong>Pyramide de Khafre (30 minutes)</strong><br>Le complexe pyramidal de Khafre se compose d\'un temple de la vall&eacute;e, le temple du Sphinx, une chauss&eacute;e, un temple mortuaire et la pyramide du roi. Le temple de la vall&eacute;e a livr&eacute; plusieurs statues de Khafr&eacute;. Plusieurs ont &eacute;t&eacute; trouv&eacute;s dans un puits dans le sol du temple par Mariette en 1860<br><br><strong>Pyramide de Menkaour&ecirc; (30 minutes)</strong><br>Le complexe pyramidal de Menkaour&ecirc; se compose d\'un temple de la vall&eacute;e, d\'une chauss&eacute;e, un temple mortuaire et la pyramide du roi. Le temple de la vall&eacute;e contenait autrefois plusieurs statues de Menkaour&ecirc;. Au cours de la Ve dynastie, un anti-temple plus petit fut ajout&eacute; au temple de la vall&eacute;e. Le temple fun&eacute;raire a &eacute;galement livr&eacute; plusieurs statues de Menkaour&ecirc;. <br><br><strong>Grand Sphinx (30 minutes)</strong><br>Le Sphinx date du r&egrave;gne du roi Khafr&eacute;.[7] Pendant le Nouvel Empire, Amenhotep II a consacr&eacute; un nouveau temple &agrave; Hauron-Haremakhet et cette structure a &eacute;t&eacute; ajout&eacute;e par les dirigeants ult&eacute;rieurs <br><br><strong>Saqqara (Sakkara) (2 heures)</strong><br>Pyramides de Sakkara , situ&eacute; &agrave; seulement 27 km au sud-ouest du Caire. Visitez la pyramide &agrave; degr&eacute;s (construite pour le roi Zoser), elle est consid&eacute;r&eacute;e comme une partie importante du processus d\'&eacute;volution de la pyramide, qui a &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;e depuis le simple mastaba jusqu\'&agrave; sa forme largement connue <br><br><strong>Mus&eacute;e Mit Rahina ( 1 heure )</strong><br>Memphis City qui &eacute;tait l\'ancienne capitale de l\'&Eacute;gypte, o&ugrave; se trouvent la statue colossale de Rams&egrave;s II et le grand Sphinx d\'alb&acirc;tre. cette ville remonte &agrave; 3100 avant JC</p>'),
(3749, 666, 'de', 'Tour zu den Pyramiden von Gizeh, Memphis und Sakkara', '<p><strong>Pyramiden von Gizeh: (3 Stunden)</strong><br>Pyramiden von Gizeh, wo Sie die Gro&szlig;en Pyramiden von Gizeh besuchen &ndash; Cheops, Chephren und Mykerinos. Anschlie&szlig;end besuchen Sie den Taltempel, den Ort, an dem die Priester den toten K&ouml;rper mumifizierten von K&ouml;nig Chephren, dem Besitzer der zweiten Pyramide von Giza Platue. Es ist auch derselbe Ort, an dem Sie die Sphinx aus n&auml;chster N&auml;he betrachten k&ouml;nnen &ndash; den legend&auml;ren W&auml;chter, der neben dem Riesen steht Bestattungskomplex mit seinem L&ouml;wenk&ouml;rper und dem Kopf von K&ouml;nig Chephren <br><br><strong>Gro&szlig;e Cheops-Pyramide (Khufu) ( 30 Minuten)</strong><br>Der Pyramidenkomplex von Cheops besteht aus einem Taltempel, der jetzt begraben ist unterhalb des Dorfes Nazlet el-Samman; Es wurden Diabaspflaster und nummulitische Kalksteinw&auml;nde gefunden, die St&auml;tte wurde jedoch nicht ausgegraben<br><br><br><strong>Khafre-Pyramide (30 Minuten)</strong><br>Khafres Pyramidenkomplex besteht aus einem Taltempel, der Sphinx-Tempel, ein Damm, ein Totentempel und die K&ouml;nigspyramide. Der Taltempel beherbergte mehrere Statuen von Khafre. Mehrere wurden 1860 von Mariette in einem Brunnen im Boden des Tempels gefunden<br><br><strong>Menkaure-Pyramide (30 Minuten)</strong><br>Der Pyramidenkomplex des Menkaure-Tempels besteht aus einem Taltempel, einem Damm, ein Totentempel und die K&ouml;nigspyramide. Der Taltempel enthielt einst mehrere Statuen von Mykerinos. W&auml;hrend der 5. Dynastie wurde dem Taltempel ein kleinerer Vortempel angebaut. Der Totentempel beherbergte auch mehrere Menkaure-Statuen. <br><br><strong>Gro&szlig;e Sphinx (30 Minuten)</strong><br>Die Sphinx stammt aus der Regierungszeit von K&ouml;nig Khafre.[7] W&auml;hrend des Neuen Reiches weihte Amenophis II. einen neuen Tempel f&uuml;r Hauron-Haremakhet und dieses Bauwerk wurde von sp&auml;teren Herrschern erweitert. <br><br><strong>Sakkara (Sakkara) (2 Stunden)</strong><br>Pyramiden Sakkara , liegt nur 27 km s&uuml;dwestlich von Kairo entfernt. Besuchen Sie die Stufenpyramide (erbaut f&uuml;r K&ouml;nig Zoser). Sie gilt als wichtiger Teil des Prozesses der Pyramidenentwicklung, die von der einfachen Mastaba bis zu ihrer weithin bekannten Form entstand. <br><br><strong>Mit Rahina Museum ( 1 Stunde)</strong><br>Memphis City, die alte Hauptstadt &Auml;gyptens, wo sich die kolossale Statue von Ramses II. und die gro&szlig;e Alabaster-Sphinx befinden. Diese Stadt stammt aus dem Jahr 3100 v. Chr.</p>'),
(3750, 666, 'it', 'Tour delle Piramidi di Giza, Menfi e Sakkara', '<p><strong>Piramidi di Giza: (3 ore)</strong><br>Piramidi di Giza dove visiti le Grandi Piramidi di Giza - Cheope, Chefren e Micerino quindi visita il Tempio della Valle Il luogo in cui i sacerdoti mummificarono il cadavere del re Chefren proprietario della seconda piramide a Giza Platue Inoltre &egrave; lo stesso posto dove puoi dare un\'occhiata da vicino alla Sfinge - Il leggendario guardiano che sta accanto all\'enorme funerale complesso con il corpo di leone e la testa del re Chefren <br><br><strong>Grande Piramide di Cheope (Cheope) (30 minuti)</strong><br>Il complesso piramidale di Cheope &egrave; costituito da un tempio della valle, ora sepolto sotto il villaggio di Nazlet el-Samman; sono stati trovati pavimenti in diabase e pareti di calcare nummulitico, ma il sito non &egrave; stato scavato<br><br><br><strong>Piramide di Khafre (30 minuti)</strong><br>Il complesso piramidale di Khafre &egrave; costituito da un tempio a valle, il tempio della Sfinge, una strada rialzata, un tempio funerario e la piramide del re. Il tempio della valle ha prodotto diverse statue di Chefren. Molti furono trovati in un pozzo nel pavimento del tempio da Mariette nel 1860<br><br><strong>Piramide di Menkaure (30 minuti)</strong><br>Il complesso piramidale di Menkaure &egrave; costituito da un tempio a valle, una strada rialzata, un tempio funerario e la piramide del re. Il tempio della valle un tempo conteneva diverse statue di Menkaure. Durante la V dinastia, al tempio della valle fu aggiunto un antitempio pi&ugrave; piccolo. Il tempio funerario ha restituito anche diverse statue di Menkaure. <br><br><strong>Grande Sfinge (30 minuti)</strong><br>La Sfinge risale al regno del re Chefren.[7] Durante il Nuovo Regno, Amenhotep II dedic&ograve; un nuovo tempio a Hauron-Haremakhet e questa struttura fu aggiunta dai sovrani successivi <br><br><strong>Saqqara (Sakkara) (2 ore)</strong><br>Piramidi Sakkara , situato a soli 27 km a sud-ovest dal Cairo. Visita la piramide a gradoni (costruita per il re Zoser), &egrave; considerata una parte importante del processo di evoluzione della piramide, che &egrave; stata realizzata dalla semplice mastaba alla sua forma ampiamente conosciuta <br><br><strong>Museo Mit Rahina ( 1 ora)</strong><br>Memphis City che era l\'antica capitale dell\'Egitto, dove si trovano la colossale statua di Ramses II e la grande Sfinge di alabastro. questa citt&agrave; risale al 3100 a.C.</p>'),
(3751, 666, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3752, 666, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3753, 666, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3754, 667, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Morning/Noon; check in the Dahabiya in Aswan&nbsp;<br>Lunch and sailing<br>Dinner and overnight on board in Daraw.</p>'),
(3755, 667, 'fr', 'Jour 1', '<p>Matin/midi ; enregistrement sur le Dahabiya &agrave; Assouan <br>D&eacute;jeuner et navigation<br>D&icirc;ner et nuit &agrave; bord &agrave; Daraw.</p>'),
(3756, 667, 'de', 'Tag 1', '<p>Morgens/Mittag; Einchecken in der Dahabiya in Assuan <br>Mittagessen und Segeln<br>Abendessen und &Uuml;bernachtung an Bord in Daraw.</p>'),
(3757, 667, 'it', 'Giorno 1', '<p>Mattina/mezzogiorno; check-in al Dahabiya ad Assuan <br>Pranzo e navigazione<br>Cena e pernottamento a bordo a Daraw.</p>'),
(3758, 667, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3759, 667, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3760, 667, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3761, 668, 'en', 'Day 2', '<p>Breakfast on board<br>Visit Draw town and the camel market<br>Visit Kom Ombo temple<br>Lunch on board<br>Sailing<br>Visit El Selsela ancient quarry and shrines in the afternoon.<br>Dinner and night stay on board near Bisaw.<br>&nbsp;</p>'),
(3762, 668, 'fr', 'Jour 2', '<p>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord<br>Visite de la ville de Draw et du march&eacute; aux chameaux<br>Visite du temple de Kom Ombo<br>D&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord<br>Voile<br>Visite de l\'ancienne carri&egrave;re et des sanctuaires d\'El Selsela dans l\'apr&egrave;s-midi.<br>D&icirc;ner et nuit &agrave; bord pr&egrave;s de Bisaw.</p>'),
(3763, 668, 'de', 'Tag 2', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord<br>Besuchen Sie die Stadt Draw und den Kamelmarkt<br>Besuchen Sie den Kom Ombo-Tempel<br>Mittagessen an Bord<br>Segeln<br>Besuchen Sie am Nachmittag den alten Steinbruch und die Schreine von El Selsela.<br>Abendessen und &Uuml;bernachtung an Bord in der N&auml;he von Bisaw.</p>'),
(3764, 668, 'it', 'Giorno 2', '<p>Colazione a bordo<br>Visita alla citt&agrave; di Draw e al mercato dei cammelli<br>Visita al tempio di Kom Ombo<br>Pranzo a bordo<br>Vela<br>Visita all\'antica cava e ai santuari di El Selsela nel pomeriggio.<br>Cena e pernottamento a bordo vicino a Bisaw.</p>'),
(3765, 668, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3766, 668, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3767, 668, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3768, 669, 'en', 'Day 3', '<p>Explore Bisaw Island and the village and meet more locals and learn about lifestyle in a remote<br>Egyptian village.<br>Breakfast in a local house or on board.<br>Sail to Edfu and visit Edfu temple.<br>Lunch on board<br>Dinner and night stay on board in El Hegz</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(3769, 669, 'fr', 'Jour 3', '<p>Explorez l\'&icirc;le de Bisaw et le village, rencontrez d\'autres habitants et d&eacute;couvrez le mode de vie dans un village &eacute;gyptien isol&eacute;.<br>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner dans une maison locale ou &agrave; bord.<br>Naviguez vers Edfou et visitez le temple d\'Edfou.<br>br&gt;D&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord<br>D&icirc;ner et nuit &agrave; bord &agrave; El Hegz</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(3770, 669, 'de', 'Tag 3', '<p>Erkunden Sie Bisaw Island und das Dorf, treffen Sie weitere Einheimische und erfahren Sie mehr &uuml;ber den Lebensstil in einem abgelegenen<br>&auml;gyptischen Dorf.<br>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck in einem &ouml;rtlichen Haus oder an Bord.<br>Segeln Sie nach Edfu und besuchen Sie den Edfu-Tempel.&lt; br&gt;Mittagessen an Bord<br>Abendessen und &Uuml;bernachtung an Bord in El Hegz</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(3771, 669, 'it', 'Giorno 3', '<p>Esplora l\'isola di Bisaw e il villaggio, incontra pi&ugrave; gente del posto e scopri lo stile di vita in un remoto<br>villaggio egiziano.<br>Colazione in una casa locale o a bordo.<br>Naviga per Edfu e visita il tempio di Edfu.&lt; br&gt;Pranzo a bordo<br>Cena e pernottamento a bordo a El Hegz</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(3772, 669, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3773, 669, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3774, 669, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3775, 670, 'en', 'Day 4', '<p>Breakfast on board<br>Sail to Esna<br>Check out after breakfast.<br>&nbsp;</p>'),
(3776, 670, 'fr', 'Jour 4', '<p>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord<br>Navigation vers Esna<br>D&eacute;part apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner.</p>'),
(3777, 670, 'de', 'Tag 4', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord<br>Segelfahrt nach Esna<br>Check-out nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck.</p>'),
(3778, 670, 'it', 'Giorno 4', '<p>Colazione a bordo<br>Naviga per Esna<br>Check out dopo la colazione.</p>'),
(3779, 670, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3780, 670, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3781, 670, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3782, 671, 'en', '“Fly to Aswan/ Aswan sightseeing”', '<p>Breakfast at your hotel, and then you will be transferred to Cairo airport for your flight to Aswan city. Upon arrival will be met and assisted by Egyptologist who will accompany you in an exciting tour to the world famous <strong>High</strong> <strong>Dam</strong> that was an engineering miracle when it was built in the 1960s. It contains 18 times the material used in the Great Pyramid of Cheops; continue to the granite quarries which supplied the ancient Egyptians with most of the hard stone used in pyramids and temples. The quarries still hold the famous <strong>Unfinished Obelisk</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>Then you will be taking by motor-boat to island of <strong>Egilka</strong> visit the majestic <strong>Philae temple</strong> that was dedicated to the Goddesses Isis.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Then you will be transferred to your Nile cruise ship, where you will enjoy the next 4 Days / 3 Nights Nile cruise holiday from Aswan up to Luxor with fantastic sailing and thrilling tours. Free time at leisure aboard your Nile cruise ship in Aswan.</p>'),
(3783, 671, 'fr', '«Envolez-vous pour Assouan / Visite d\'Assouan»', '<p>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel, puis transfert &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport du Caire pour votre vol vers la ville d\'Assouan. &Agrave; votre arriv&eacute;e, vous serez accueilli et assist&eacute; par un &eacute;gyptologue qui vous accompagnera dans une visite passionnante du c&eacute;l&egrave;bre <strong>Haut</strong> <strong>Barrage</strong> qui &eacute;tait un miracle d\'ing&eacute;nierie lors de sa construction dans les ann&eacute;es 1960. Il contient 18 fois le mat&eacute;riau utilis&eacute; dans la Grande Pyramide de Kh&eacute;ops ; Continuez vers les carri&egrave;res de granit qui fournissaient aux anciens &Eacute;gyptiens la plupart des pierres dures utilis&eacute;es dans les pyramides et les temples. Les carri&egrave;res abritent encore le c&eacute;l&egrave;bre <strong>Ob&eacute;lisque inachev&eacute;</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>Ensuite, vous prendrez un bateau &agrave; moteur jusqu\'&agrave; l\'&icirc;le de <strong>Egilka</strong> pour visiter le majestueux <strong>Philae temple</strong> qui &eacute;tait d&eacute;di&eacute; aux d&eacute;esses Isis.</p>\r\n<p>Ensuite, vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute; &agrave; votre bateau de croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil, o&ugrave; vous profiterez des prochaines vacances en croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil de 4 jours / 3 nuits, d\'Assouan jusqu\'&agrave; Louxor, avec des navigations fantastiques et des visites passionnantes. Temps libre &agrave; bord de votre bateau de croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil &agrave; Assouan.</p>'),
(3784, 671, 'de', '„Flug nach Assuan/Sightseeing in Assuan“', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck in Ihrem Hotel und anschlie&szlig;end Transfer zum Flughafen Kairo f&uuml;r Ihren Flug nach Assuan. Bei Ihrer Ankunft werden Sie von einem &Auml;gyptologen empfangen und unterst&uuml;tzt, der Sie auf einer aufregenden Tour zum weltber&uuml;hmten <strong>High</strong> <strong>Staudamm</strong> begleitet, der bei seinem Bau in den 1960er Jahren ein Wunderwerk der Ingenieurskunst war. Es enth&auml;lt das 18-fache des Materials, das in der Gro&szlig;en Cheops-Pyramide verwendet wurde; Weiter geht es zu den Granitsteinbr&uuml;chen, aus denen die alten &Auml;gypter den Gro&szlig;teil des Hartgesteins f&uuml;r Pyramiden und Tempel bezogen. In den Steinbr&uuml;chen befindet sich noch immer der ber&uuml;hmte <strong>unvollendete Obelisk</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>Dann fahren Sie mit dem Motorboot zur Insel <strong>Egilka</strong> und besuchen das majest&auml;tische <strong>Philae Tempel, der der G&ouml;ttin Isis gewidmet war. </strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Dann werden Sie zu Ihrem Nilkreuzfahrtschiff gebracht, wo Sie die n&auml;chsten 4 Tage/3 N&auml;chte Nilkreuzfahrt von Assuan bis nach Luxor mit fantastischen Segeltouren und aufregenden Touren genie&szlig;en werden. Freizeit zur freien Verf&uuml;gung an Bord Ihres Nilkreuzfahrtschiffs in Assuan.</strong></p>'),
(3785, 671, 'it', '“Vola ad Assuan / giro turistico di Assuan”', '<p>Colazione in hotel e poi trasferimento all\'aeroporto del Cairo per il volo per Assuan. All\'arrivo verrai accolto e assistito da un egittologo che ti accompagner&agrave; in un emozionante tour alla famosa <strong>Alta</strong> <strong>Diga</strong> che fu un miracolo dell\'ingegneria quando fu costruita negli anni \'60. Contiene 18 volte il materiale utilizzato nella Grande Piramide di Cheope; proseguire verso le cave di granito che fornivano agli antichi egizi la maggior parte della pietra dura utilizzata nelle piramidi e nei templi. Le cave custodiscono ancora il famoso <strong>Obelisco incompiuto</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>Poi verrai portato in motoscafo all\'isola di <strong>Egilka</strong> per visitare la maestosa <strong>Philae tempio</strong> che era dedicato alla dea Iside.</p>\r\n<p>Quindi verrai trasferito sulla tua nave da crociera sul Nilo, dove potrai goderti la prossima vacanza in crociera sul Nilo di 4 giorni / 3 notti da Assuan fino a Luxor con fantastiche crociere ed emozionanti tour. Tempo libero a bordo della tua nave da crociera sul Nilo ad Assuan.</p>'),
(3786, 671, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3787, 671, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3788, 671, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3789, 672, 'en', '” Abu-Simbel Excursions / Nile Cruise Tour”', '<p>Breakfast box from your hotel in Aswan and then you will be escorted by your Egyptologist speaking guide and driver to explore the impressive temples built by <strong>Ramses II</strong> in <strong>Abu Simbel</strong> which is one of Egypt\'s most visited sites. Relocated in the 1960\'s with the building of the Aswan Dam, Abu Simbel is a feat of modern and ancient engineering then you will be transferred to Aswan to embark your Nile cruise ship. Lunch, afternoon tea and free time at leisure aboard your Nile cruise sailing to Kom-Ombo.</p>');
INSERT INTO `tour_day_translations` (`id`, `tour_day_id`, `locale`, `title`, `description`) VALUES
(3790, 672, 'fr', '« Excursions à Abou-Simbel / Croisière sur le Nil »', '<p>Bo&icirc;te de petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; votre h&ocirc;tel &agrave; Assouan, puis vous serez escort&eacute; par votre guide et chauffeur &eacute;gyptologue pour explorer les impressionnants temples construits par <strong>Rams&egrave;s II</strong> &agrave; <strong>Abou Simbel</strong> qui est l\'un des sites les plus visit&eacute;s d\'&Eacute;gypte. D&eacute;m&eacute;nag&eacute; dans les ann&eacute;es 1960 avec la construction du barrage d\'Assouan, Abou Simbel est une prouesse d\'ing&eacute;nierie moderne et ancienne. Vous serez ensuite transf&eacute;r&eacute; &agrave; Assouan pour embarquer sur votre bateau de croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil. D&eacute;jeuner, th&eacute; de l\'apr&egrave;s-midi et temps libre &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil en direction de Kom-Ombo.</p>'),
(3791, 672, 'de', '„Abu-Simbel-Ausflüge / Nilkreuzfahrt-Tour“', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ckspaket in Ihrem Hotel in Assuan. Anschlie&szlig;end werden Sie von Ihrem &auml;gyptologischen Reisef&uuml;hrer und Fahrer begleitet, um die beeindruckenden Tempel zu erkunden, die von <strong>Ramses II.</strong> in <strong>Abu Simbel</strong> erbaut wurden ist eine der meistbesuchten Sehensw&uuml;rdigkeiten &Auml;gyptens. Abu Simbel wurde in den 1960er Jahren mit dem Bau des Assuan-Staudamms verlegt und ist ein Meisterwerk moderner und alter Ingenieurskunst. Anschlie&szlig;end werden Sie nach Assuan gebracht, um an Bord Ihres Nilkreuzfahrtschiffs zu gehen. Mittagessen, Nachmittagstee und Freizeit an Bord Ihrer Nilkreuzfahrt nach Kom-Ombo.</p>'),
(3792, 672, 'it', '\"Escursioni ad Abu-Simbel / Tour in crociera sul Nilo\"', '<p>Colazione al sacco dal tuo hotel ad Assuan e poi sarai accompagnato dalla tua guida e autista parlante egittologo per esplorare gli imponenti templi costruiti da <strong>Ramses II</strong> ad <strong>Abu Simbel</strong> che &egrave; uno dei siti pi&ugrave; visitati dell\'Egitto. Trasferito negli anni \'60 con la costruzione della diga di Assuan, Abu Simbel &egrave; un\'impresa di ingegneria moderna e antica, quindi verrai trasferito ad Assuan per imbarcarti sulla tua nave da crociera sul Nilo. Pranzo, t&egrave; pomeridiano e tempo libero a bordo della crociera sul Nilo verso Kom-Ombo.</p>'),
(3793, 672, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3794, 672, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3795, 672, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3796, 673, 'en', '“Nile Cruise Tour”', '<p>After breakfast you will be accompanied by your Egyptologist guide to <strong>visit</strong> <strong>Kom Ombo temple</strong>, the crocodile-headed God of fertility and creator of the world, lunch aboard your cruise with free time at leisure whilst sailing to Edfu to <strong>explore Edfu Temple of Horus</strong>, one of the best-preserved Ancient Egyptian temples on the Nile Continue the cruise down the Nile to Luxor and overnight stay onboard your Nile cruise ship.</p>'),
(3797, 673, 'fr', '«Croisière sur le Nil»', '<p>Apr&egrave;s le petit-d&eacute;jeuner, vous serez accompagn&eacute; de votre guide &eacute;gyptologue pour <strong>visiter</strong> le <strong>temple de Kom Ombo</strong>, le dieu de la fertilit&eacute; &agrave; t&ecirc;te de crocodile et cr&eacute;ateur du monde, d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re. avec temps libre tout en naviguant vers Edfou pour <strong>explorer le temple d\'Horus d\'Edfou</strong>, l\'un des temples &eacute;gyptiens antiques les mieux conserv&eacute;s sur le Nil. Continuez la croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil jusqu\'&agrave; Louxor et passez la nuit &agrave; bord de votre croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil. navire.</p>'),
(3798, 673, 'de', '„Nilkreuzfahrt-Tour“', '<p>Nach dem Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck werden Sie von Ihrem &auml;gyptologischen Reiseleiter zum <strong>Kom-Ombo-Tempel</strong>, dem krokodilk&ouml;pfigen Gott der Fruchtbarkeit und Sch&ouml;pfer der Welt, begleitet. Mittagessen an Bord Ihrer Kreuzfahrt Mit Freizeit zur freien Verf&uuml;gung, w&auml;hrend Sie nach Edfu segeln, um den Horus-Tempel von Edfu zu erkunden, einen der am besten erhaltenen alt&auml;gyptischen Tempel auf dem Nil. Setzen Sie die Kreuzfahrt den Nil hinunter nach Luxor fort und &uuml;bernachten Sie an Bord Nilkreuzfahrtschiff.</p>'),
(3799, 673, 'it', '“Tour in crociera sul Nilo”', '<p>Dopo la colazione sarai accompagnato dalla tua guida egittologa per <strong>visitare</strong> il <strong>tempio di Kom Ombo</strong>, il dio della fertilit&agrave; dalla testa di coccodrillo e creatore del mondo, pranzo a bordo della tua crociera con tempo libero a disposizione durante la navigazione verso Edfu per <strong>esplorare il Tempio di Horus di Edfu</strong>, uno dei templi dell\'antico Egitto meglio conservati sul Nilo Continua la crociera lungo il Nilo fino a Luxor e pernottamento a bordo della tua crociera sul Nilo nave.</p>'),
(3800, 673, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3801, 673, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3802, 673, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3803, 674, 'en', '“Luxor Sightseeing / Fly back to Cairo”', '<p>Breakfast onboard the cruise, check-out the Nile cruise and then&nbsp;will be picked up by our tour guide to visit archaeological sites of the ancient Egyptians on the west bank of the Nile including the two colossal statues of <strong>Amenhotep III (Colossi of Memnon),</strong> and then visit the <strong>Valley of the Kings</strong>, where the magnificent tombs discovered, those tombs were carved deep into the desert rock, richly decorated and filled with treasures for the afterlife of the pharaohs, you will visit 3 tombs. Continue the tour to visit the <strong>Hatshepsut temple</strong> at El <strong>Deir El Bahary</strong>, this impressive temple dedicated to the Queen Hatshepsut the only female pharaoh rises out of the desert plain in a series of terraces and merges with the sheer limestone cliffs that surround it.</p>\r\n<p>Then heading to visit the two Massive temples on the eastern bank of the Nile, <strong>visit the Temple of Luxor and Temple of Karnak</strong>. Karnak Temple, the largest place of worship ever built. Its ancient name Ipet-isut means the most sacred of places. The temple, or, more correctly, the complex of temples, was built over more than two thousand years by generation after generation of pharaohs. Within the complex, the great Hypostyle Hall&nbsp;is an incredible forest of giant pillars. Then you will be transferred to the majestic Luxor temple which built by Amenhotep III and Ramses II for rituals and festivals and dedicated to the god Amun god of air sun and sky.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>After finishing the tour, you will be transferred to Luxor airport for <strong>Domestic Flight</strong> back to Cairo. Upon arrival to Cairo airport you will be picked up and transferred to the hotel for check in and Overnight.</p>'),
(3804, 674, 'fr', '« Visite de Louxor / Retour au Caire »', '<p>Petit-d&eacute;jeuner &agrave; bord de la croisi&egrave;re, d&eacute;part de la croisi&egrave;re sur le Nil, puis prise en charge par notre guide pour visiter les sites arch&eacute;ologiques des anciens &Eacute;gyptiens sur la rive ouest du Nil, y compris les deux statues colossales d\'Amenhotep III. (Colosses de Memnon), puis visitez la <strong>Vall&eacute;e des Rois</strong>, o&ugrave; ont &eacute;t&eacute; d&eacute;couverts les magnifiques tombeaux, ces tombeaux ont &eacute;t&eacute; creus&eacute;s profond&eacute;ment dans la roche du d&eacute;sert, richement d&eacute;cor&eacute;s et remplis de tr&eacute;sors de l\'au-del&agrave; des pharaons, vous visiterez 3 tombeaux. Continuez la visite pour visiter le <strong>temple d\'Hatchepsout</strong> &agrave; El <strong>Deir El Bahary</strong>, cet impressionnant temple d&eacute;di&eacute; &agrave; la reine Hatshepsout, la seule femme pharaon, s\'&eacute;l&egrave;ve de la plaine d&eacute;sertique dans une s&eacute;rie de terrasses et se confond avec les falaises calcaires abruptes qui l\'entourent.</p>\r\n<p>Ensuite, direction les deux temples massifs sur la rive orientale du Nil, <strong>visitez le temple de Louxor et le temple de Karnak. Temple de Karnak, le plus grand lieu de culte jamais construit. Son ancien nom Ipet-isut signifie le lieu le plus sacr&eacute;. Le temple, ou, plus exactement, le complexe de temples, a &eacute;t&eacute; construit sur plus de deux mille ans par g&eacute;n&eacute;ration apr&egrave;s g&eacute;n&eacute;ration de pharaons. Au sein du complexe, la grande salle hypostyle est une incroyable for&ecirc;t de piliers g&eacute;ants. Ensuite, vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute; au majestueux temple de Louxor construit par Amenhotep III et Rams&egrave;s II pour les rituels et les festivals et d&eacute;di&eacute; au dieu Amon, dieu de l\'air, du soleil et du ciel. </strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Une fois la visite termin&eacute;e, vous serez transf&eacute;r&eacute; &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport de Louxor pour le <strong>vol int&eacute;rieur</strong> de retour au Caire. &Agrave; votre arriv&eacute;e &agrave; l\'a&eacute;roport du Caire, vous serez pris en charge et transf&eacute;r&eacute; &agrave; l\'h&ocirc;tel pour l\'enregistrement et la nuit.</strong></p>'),
(3805, 674, 'de', '„Luxor-Sightseeing / Rückflug nach Kairo“', '<p>Fr&uuml;hst&uuml;ck an Bord der Kreuzfahrt, Besichtigung der Nilkreuzfahrt und anschlie&szlig;ende Abholung durch unseren Reiseleiter zur Besichtigung der arch&auml;ologischen St&auml;tten der alten &Auml;gypter am Westufer des Nils, einschlie&szlig;lich der beiden kolossalen Statuen von <strong>Amenhotep III (Memnonkolosse)</strong> und besuchen Sie dann das <strong>Tal der K&ouml;nige</strong>, wo die pr&auml;chtigen Gr&auml;ber entdeckt wurden. Diese Gr&auml;ber wurden tief in den W&uuml;stenfelsen gehauen, reich verziert und mit Sch&auml;tzen gef&uuml;llt Nach dem Tod der Pharaonen besuchen Sie 3 Gr&auml;ber. Setzen Sie die Tour fort und besuchen Sie den <strong>Hatschepsut-Tempel</strong> in El <strong>Deir El Bahary</strong>. Dieser beeindruckende Tempel, der der K&ouml;nigin Hatschepsut gewidmet ist, der einzigen weiblichen Pharaonin, erhebt sich in mehreren Schritten aus der W&uuml;stenebene Terrassen und verschmilzt mit den steilen Kalksteinfelsen, die es umgeben.</p>\r\n<p>Besuchen Sie anschlie&szlig;end die beiden riesigen Tempel am Ostufer des Nils, <strong>den Luxor-Tempel und den Karnak-Tempel</strong> &gt;. Karnak-Tempel, die gr&ouml;&szlig;te jemals gebaute Kultst&auml;tte. Sein alter Name Ipet-isut bedeutet der heiligste aller Orte. Der Tempel, oder genauer gesagt der Tempelkomplex, wurde &uuml;ber mehr als zweitausend Jahre hinweg von Generationen von Pharaonen erbaut. Innerhalb des Komplexes ist die gro&szlig;e Hypostyle-Halle ein unglaublicher Wald aus riesigen S&auml;ulen. Anschlie&szlig;end werden Sie zum majest&auml;tischen Luxor-Tempel gebracht, der von Amenophis III. und Ramses II. f&uuml;r Rituale und Feste erbaut und dem Gott Amun, dem Gott der Luft, Sonne und des Himmels, gewidmet wurde.</p>\r\n<p>Nach Abschluss der Tour werden Sie zum Flughafen Luxor f&uuml;r einen <strong>Inlandsflug</strong> zur&uuml;ck nach Kairo gebracht. Bei Ihrer Ankunft am Flughafen Kairo werden Sie abgeholt und zum Hotel gebracht, wo Sie einchecken und &uuml;bernachten.</p>'),
(3806, 674, 'it', '“Giro turistico di Luxor / Ritorno al Cairo”', '<p>Colazione a bordo della crociera, check-out della crociera sul Nilo e poi verrai prelevato dalla nostra guida turistica per visitare i siti archeologici degli antichi egizi sulla riva occidentale del Nilo, tra cui le due colossali statue di <strong>Amenhotep III (Colossi di Memnone),</strong> e poi visitare la <strong>Valle dei Re</strong>, dove furono scoperte le magnifiche tombe, quelle tombe furono scavate in profondit&agrave; nella roccia del deserto, riccamente decorate e piene di tesori per i aldil&agrave; dei faraoni, visiterai 3 tombe. Continua il tour per visitare il <strong>tempio di Hatshepsut</strong> a El <strong>Deir El Bahary</strong>, questo imponente tempio dedicato alla regina Hatshepsut, l\'unico faraone donna, si erge dalla pianura desertica in una serie di terrazze e si fonde con le scogliere calcaree a strapiombo che lo circondano.</p>\r\n<p>Quindi dirigiti a visitare i due enormi templi sulla sponda orientale del Nilo, <strong>visita il Tempio di Luxor e il Tempio di Karnak</strong>. Tempio di Karnak, il pi&ugrave; grande luogo di culto mai costruito. Il suo antico nome Ipet-isut significa il pi&ugrave; sacro dei luoghi. Il tempio, o, pi&ugrave; correttamente, il complesso dei templi, fu costruito nel corso di pi&ugrave; di duemila anni da generazione dopo generazione di faraoni. All\'interno del complesso, la grande Sala Ipostila &egrave; un\'incredibile foresta di pilastri giganti. Quindi verrai trasferito al maestoso tempio di Luxor, costruito da Amenhotep III e Ramses II per rituali e feste e dedicato al dio Amon, dio dell\'aria, del sole e del cielo.</p>\r\n<p>Dopo aver terminato il tour, verrai trasferito all\'aeroporto di Luxor per il <strong>volo interno</strong> di ritorno al Cairo. All\'arrivo all\'aeroporto del Cairo verrai prelevato e trasferito in hotel per il check-in e il pernottamento.</p>'),
(3807, 674, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3808, 674, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3809, 674, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3810, 675, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p>Venture on an unforgettable journey with us where we promise to make your dreams come true. From the moment you step out of your hotel in Luxor, our representative will be there to guide you on a magical exploration of the West bank of Luxor.<br><br>Your day will begin with a visit to the awe-inspiring Valley of the Kings. This architectural masterpiece, once a burial ground, is the final resting place of many illustrious kings. You will have the opportunity to explore three of these royal tombs, each one a testament to the grandeur of ancient Egyptian civilization.&nbsp;<br>The adventure continues as you are whisked away to the Temple of Queen Hatshepsut. Constructed by Queen Hatshepsut herself, the only woman to have reigned over ancient Egypt as a pharaoh, this temple stands as a symbol of her powerful 20-year rule during the 18th Dynasty (approximately from 1490 to 1469 B.C).<br><br>As the day draws to a close, you will be safely transported back to your hotel in Luxor, carrying with you memories of a day spent stepping back in time and exploring the wonders of ancient Egypt. With us, every journey is an experience, every moment a memory. Book your tour today, and let us guide you through the pages of history.</p>'),
(3811, 675, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3812, 675, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3813, 675, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3814, 675, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3815, 675, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3816, 675, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3817, 676, 'en', 'Day 1', '<p>Vive Egiptos beckons you to a majestic journey through the beginning of time. Your private tour guide will collect you from your Cairo hotel and set you out to the iconic Giza Plateau.<br><br>Here, the Pyramids of Cheops, Chephren, and Mykerinus rise from the sands, a testament to ancient ambition and ingenuity. Stand in awe at the Great Sphinx, Chephren\'s guardian, whose enigmatic visage has stirred the imaginations of travelers for centuries.<br><br>Your exploration continues at the Valley Temple, a site of profound significance. It was here that the pharaohs\' mummies underwent purification and mummification, rituals as essential to their journey to the afterlife as the pyramids themselves.<br><br>Behold the Seven Wonders of the World, where the 5000-year-old necropolis awaits. The Great Pyramids, a marvel of human achievement, stand as sentinels to history, watched over by the vigilant Sphinx. This is not merely a tour; it is a pilgrimage to the heart of Egypt\'s grandeur, a must-see for every wanderer of the world. With Pharaoh Vibes Tours, the past is not just to be seen, but to be experienced.&nbsp;</p>'),
(3818, 676, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
(3819, 676, 'de', NULL, NULL),
(3820, 676, 'it', NULL, NULL),
(3821, 676, 'pt', NULL, NULL),
(3822, 676, 'es', NULL, NULL),
(3823, 676, 'zh', NULL, NULL),
(3824, 677, 'en', 'Itinerary', '<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Experience an unforgettable journey with Sun Pyramids Tours! We\'ll collect you from your hotel in Sharm El Sheikh at 8:30 pm, whisking you away in a modern, air-conditioned vehicle to the historic St. Catherine. A scenic three-hour drive will bring you to the foot of the majestic Moses Mountain.\\n\\nAt 2:00 am, under the starlit sky, you\'ll embark on a climb up Moses Mountain. As you ascend, you\'ll feel a sense of awe and anticipation. Reaching the summit at 7:00 am, you\'ll be rewarded with a breathtaking view of the sunrise, painting the sky with hues of gold and orange.\\n\\nYour adventure continues with a visit to the world-renowned St. Catherine Monastery. This sacred site, dedicated to Saint Catherine, one of Alexander\'s rulers who embraced her faith even in the face of death, is a testament to resilience and faith.\\n\\nAs the day concludes, we\'ll transport you back to your hotel in Sharm El Sheikh, leaving you with memories of an extraordinary adventure.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:9153,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;9&quot;:1,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Experience an unforgettable journey with Vive Egiptos! We\'ll collect you from your hotel in Sharm El Sheikh at 20:00 pm, whisking you away in a modern, air-conditioned vehicle to the historic St. Catherine. A scenic three-hour drive will bring you to the foot of the majestic Moses Mountain.<br><br>At 2:00 am, under the starlit sky, you\'ll embark on a climb up Moses Mountain. As you ascend, you\'ll feel a sense of awe and anticipation. Reaching the summit at 7:00 am, you\'ll be rewarded with a breathtaking view of the sunrise, painting the sky with hues of gold and orange.<br><br>Your adventure continues with a visit to the world-renowned St. Catherine Monastery. This sacred site, dedicated to Saint Catherine, one of Alexander\'s rulers who embraced her faith even in the face of death, is a testament to resilience and faith.<br><br>As the day concludes, we\'ll transport you back to your hotel in Sharm El Sheikh, leaving you with memories of an extraordinary adventure.</span></p>\r\n<p><span data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Experience an unforgettable journey with Sun Pyramids Tours! We\'ll collect you from your hotel in Sharm El Sheikh at 8:30 pm, whisking you away in a modern, air-conditioned vehicle to the historic St. Catherine. A scenic three-hour drive will bring you to the foot of the majestic Moses Mountain.\\n\\nAt 2:00 am, under the starlit sky, you\'ll embark on a climb up Moses Mountain. As you ascend, you\'ll feel a sense of awe and anticipation. Reaching the summit at 7:00 am, you\'ll be rewarded with a breathtaking view of the sunrise, painting the sky with hues of gold and orange.\\n\\nYour adventure continues with a visit to the world-renowned St. Catherine Monastery. This sacred site, dedicated to Saint Catherine, one of Alexander\'s rulers who embraced her faith even in the face of death, is a testament to resilience and faith.\\n\\nAs the day concludes, we\'ll transport you back to your hotel in Sharm El Sheikh, leaving you with memories of an extraordinary adventure.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:9153,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;9&quot;:1,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;16&quot;:12}\">Please provide a copy of passport which must be sent to the local partner at the most 2 days before the tour</span></p>'),
(3825, 677, 'fr', NULL, NULL),
