(105, 33, 'en', 'ECLIPSE SEASONS CAIRO - ASWAN- LUXOR', '8 days 7 hours', 'Private Tour', 'https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d57517.20954759506!2d32.58216785189068!3d25.710197811359333!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x14491599d174b82b%3A0x92db9d280a1b7cd4!2sKarnak%2C%20Luxor%2C%20Luxor%20Governorate!5e0!3m2!1sen!2seg!4v1776693370122!5m2!1sen!2seg', '8 am', '<p data-start=\"127\" data-end=\"825\">Embark on a remarkable journey through Egypt, beginning with the vibrant charm of Cairo by night, followed by an in-depth visit to the legendary Pyramids of Giza, the Great Sphinx, and the Grand Egyptian Museum. Continue south to Aswan to explore the beautiful Philae Temple, the High Dam, and the awe-inspiring rock-cut temples of Abu Simbel. Travel onward through Kom Ombo and Edfu before reaching Luxor, where you&rsquo;ll discover the Valley of the Kings, Queen Hatshepsut&rsquo;s magnificent temple, and the Colossi of Memnon. Your adventure culminates with a once-in-a-lifetime viewing of the Total Solar Eclipse at Karnak Temple and a final visit to Luxor Temple before returning to Cairo for departure.</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"864\" data-end=\"930\">\r\n<p data-start=\"866\" data-end=\"930\"><strong data-start=\"866\" data-end=\"884\">Cairo by Night</strong> &ndash; Explore the capital&rsquo;s evening atmosphere.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"931\" data-end=\"1024\">\r\n<p data-start=\"933\" data-end=\"1024\"><strong data-start=\"933\" data-end=\"972\">Pyramids of Giza &amp; The Great Sphinx</strong> &ndash; The only surviving wonder of the ancient world.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1025\" data-end=\"1102\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1027\" data-end=\"1102\"><strong data-start=\"1027\" data-end=\"1058\">Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)</strong> &ndash; Home to over 100,000 ancient artifacts.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1103\" data-end=\"1166\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1105\" data-end=\"1166\"><strong data-start=\"1105\" data-end=\"1122\">Philae Temple</strong> &ndash; The romantic Temple of Isis and Osiris.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1167\" data-end=\"1256\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1256\"><strong data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1187\">Aswan High Dam</strong> &ndash; One of Egypt&rsquo;s most significant modern engineering achievements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1257\" data-end=\"1361\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1259\" data-end=\"1361\"><strong data-start=\"1259\" data-end=\"1273\">Abu Simbel</strong> &ndash; Majestic rock-cut temples of Ramses II, a marvel of ancient and modern engineering.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1362\" data-end=\"1436\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1364\" data-end=\"1436\"><strong data-start=\"1364\" data-end=\"1383\">Kom Ombo Temple</strong> &ndash; Unique dual-dedicated temple to Sobek and Horus.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1437\" data-end=\"1514\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1439\" data-end=\"1514\"><strong data-start=\"1439\" data-end=\"1454\">Edfu Temple</strong> &ndash; The best-preserved temple in Egypt, dedicated to Horus.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1515\" data-end=\"1599\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1517\" data-end=\"1599\"><strong data-start=\"1517\" data-end=\"1540\">Valley of the Kings</strong> &ndash; Including 5 tombs such as Tutankhamun and Ramesses VI.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1600\" data-end=\"1686\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1602\" data-end=\"1686\"><strong data-start=\"1602\" data-end=\"1640\">Queen Hatshepsut&rsquo;s Mortuary Temple</strong> &ndash; A striking temple carved into the cliffs.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1687\" data-end=\"1767\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1689\" data-end=\"1767\"><strong data-start=\"1689\" data-end=\"1710\">Colossi of Memnon</strong> &ndash; Two massive statues guarding a lost mortuary temple.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1768\" data-end=\"1868\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1770\" data-end=\"1868\"><strong data-start=\"1770\" data-end=\"1787\">Karnak Temple</strong> &ndash; Special viewing of the <strong data-start=\"1813\" data-end=\"1836\">Total Solar Eclipse</strong> from this monumental complex.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1869\" data-end=\"1935\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1871\" data-end=\"1935\"><strong data-start=\"1871\" data-end=\"1887\">Luxor Temple</strong> &ndash; Explore its grand colossi and ancient beauty.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', 'All transfers by a private air-conditioned vehicle new model,Representative in airports to assist you through passport control and customs.,Accommodation in hotel Steigenberger El Tahrir or similar in Cairo on BB basis,Accommodation in hotel Basma Hotel Aswan or similar in Aswan on BB basis,Accommodation in hotel Steigenberger Nile Palace or similar in Luxor on BB basis,24/7 customer service,Lunch on tours,All domestic flights (CAI-ASW,The above mentioned sightseeing tours including English speaking Egyptologist guide,Entrance fees,All service charges and taxes', 'Personal Expenses,Optional visits,Tipping,Entry Visa'),
